<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="ACT" style="id">act --- Māori NT converted from rtf (LAI); 20100830 zb</book>
  <para style="h">MAHI</para>
  <para style="mt2">Ko</para>
  <para style="mt1">NGĀ MAHI</para>
  <para style="mt2">a ngā Āpōtoro</para>
  <para style="imt">Kupu Whakataki</para>
  <para style="ip">
    <char style="bk">Ko Ngā Mahi a Ngā Āpōtoro</char> he roanga ake o<char style="bk">Te Rongopai ki te Ritenga a Ruka</char>. Tōna kaupapa matua ki te whaka­atu i pēhea ngā kaiaru tua­tahi a Īhu, e āra­hina ana e te Wairua Tapu, e hohou ana i te Rongopai mōna “ki Hiruhārama, ki Hūria katoa, ki Hamāria o te ao.” (1.8) Koia nei te kōrero mō te rōpū Karaiti­ana i tōna tīmata­tanga i waenga­nui i te iwi Hūrai, ka tipu ake hei whaka­pono mō te ao. I āwanga­wanga anō te kai­tuhi ki te whaka­ahuru i ngā kai­pānui ehara ngā Karaiti­ana he hunga whaka­turaki tō­ranga­pū ki te Emepaea o Roma, atu anō ko tā te whaka­pono Karaiti­ana te whaka­rite­nga o te hāhi Hūrai.</para>
  <para style="ip">Ka taea te wehe i <char style="bk">Ngā Mahi</char> ki ngā wāhanga e toru, e whaka­atu ana i te whānui o te hāhi. (1) Te tīmata­tanga o te whaka­pono Karaiti­ana ki Hiruhārama ā muri mai i te kake­nga atu o Īhu: (2) te whaka­whānui atu ki ētahi atu rohe o Paratini; me (3) te whaka­whānui atu ki ngā rohe o te ao o Metitareiniana puta noa ki Roma.</para>
  <para style="ip">Te mea tino nui o <char style="bk">Ngā Mahi</char> ko te nga­nga­hau a te Wairua Tapu, ka tau mai me tōna mana ki ngā hunga whaka­pono i Hiruhārama, i te rā o te Petekoha, me te mahi tonu hei kai­ārahi, hei whaka­kaha hoki i te hāhi me ōna kai­hautū, puta noa i ngā mahi i rī­po­ata­hia nei i roto i te puka­puka. Ko te pū­rongo a ngā Karaiti­ana mātā­mua i whaka­rā­po­toto­tia ki ētahi kauhau, ka kitea te kaha o te pū­rongo o <char style="bk">Ngā Mahi</char> i roto i te oranga o ngā kai­whaka­pono me te whanaunga­tanga o te hāhi.</para>
  <para style="iot">Rāpopoto o Ngā Take</para>
  <para style="io1">Te whakaritenga mō te kaiwhakaatu 1.1-26</para>
  <para style="io2">a. Tā Īhu tohutohu me tōna ōhākī whakamutunga 1.1-14</para>
  <para style="io2">e. Te kaiwahakakapi o te tūranga o Hūrā 1.15-26</para>
  <para style="io1">Te tauwhakaatu i Hiruhārama 2.1–8.3</para>
  <para style="io1">Te tauwhakaatu i Hūria me Hamāria 8.4–12.25</para>
  <para style="io1">Te minitatanga a Paora 13.1–28.31</para>
  <para style="io2">a. Te mihinare haerenga tuatahi 13.1–14.28</para>
  <para style="io2">e. Te hui i Hiruhārama 15.1-35</para>
  <para style="io2">i. Te haerenga mihinare tuarua 15.36–18.22</para>
  <para style="io2">o. Te haerenga mihinare tuatoru 18.23–21.16</para>
  <para style="io2">u. Paora he mauhere i Hiruhārama, Hiharia, me Roma 21.17–28.31</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="ACT 1" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 1:1" />Ko te puka­puka tua­tahi rā he mea tuhi­tuhi nāku, e Tiopira, mō ngā mea katoa i tīmata ai a Īhu te mahi, te ako, <verse eid="ACT 1:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 1:2" />taea noatia te rā i tango­hia atu ai ia, i muri i tāna whaka­ako­ranga, arā i tā te Wairua Tapu, ki ngā āpō­toro i whiri­whiria e ia. <verse eid="ACT 1:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 1:3" />He maha hoki ngā tohu i whaka­kite ora ai ia i a ia ki a rātou, i muri i tōna whaka­mamae­tanga, e whā tekau hoki ngā rā i kitea ai e rātou, kōrero­tia ai e ia ngā mea o te ranga­tira­tanga o te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 1:4" />Ā, i a rātou ka hui­hui tahi me ia, ka whai kupu ia kia kaua rātou e haere atu i Hiruhārama, ā, ka mea, “Engari, kia tāria te mea i kōrero­tia i mua e te Matua, i rongo rā koutou ki ahau. <verse eid="ACT 1:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 1:5" />I iri­iri hoki a Hoani ki te wai; ko koutou ia, e kore e maha ake ngā rā, ka iri­iria ki te Wairua Tapu.”<verse eid="ACT 1:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Mauria ake a Īhu ki te Rangi</para>
  <para style="r">(<ref loc="MRK 16:19-20">Māka 16.19-20</ref>; <ref loc="LUK 24:50-53">Ruka 24.50-53</ref>)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 1:6" />Nō reira, i a rātou ka tāmene, ka ui rātou ki a ia, “E te Ariki, ko te wā ianei tēnei e whaka­hoki ai koe i te ranga­tira­tanga ki a Īharaira?”<verse eid="ACT 1:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 1:7" />Nā, ko tāna mea­tanga ki a rātou, “Ehara mā koutou te mōhio ki ngā tāima, ki ngā wā rānei, kua whaka­ritea e te Matua māna ake te tikanga. <verse eid="ACT 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 1:8" />Otiia, ka riro he kaha i a koutou, ina haere mai te Wairua Tapu ki runga ki a koutou, ā, hei kai­whaka­atu koutou mōku ki Hiruhārama, ki Hūria katoa, ki Hamaria hoki, ā tae noa ki te pito whaka­mutu­nga o te ao.” <verse eid="ACT 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 1:9" />Ā, nō ka mutu tāna kōrero i ēnei mea, i a rātou anō e ti­tiro atu ana, ka tango­hia atu ia, ā, nā te kapua i kōpaki atu i ō rātou kanohi.<verse eid="ACT 1:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 1:10" />Ā, i a rātou e ti­tiro mata­tau atu ana ki te rangi, i a ia e haere ana, nā, ko ngā tāngata toko­rua e tū ana i tō rātou taha, he mā ngā kākahu. <verse eid="ACT 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 1:11" />E mea ana, “E ngā tāngata o Kariri, he aha tā koutou e tū, e mā­taki­taki atu nā ki te rangi? Ko tēnā Īhu kua tango­hia atu nā i a koutou ki te rangi, ka pērā anō tōna haere­nga mai me ia i tiro­hia atu nā e koutou e haere ana ki te rangi.”<verse eid="ACT 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Kairīwhi o Hūrā</para>
  <para style="r">(<ref loc="MAT 27:3-10">Matiu 27.3-10</ref>)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 1:12" />Nā, hoki ana rātou ki Hiruhārama i te maunga e huaina nei ko Ōriwa, he wāhi e tata ana ki Hiruhārama, he haere­nga hāpati. <verse eid="ACT 1:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 1:13" />Ā, ka tomo rātou, ka kake ki te rūma i runga, ki te wāhi i noho ai rātou; arā a Pita, a Hēmi, a Hoani, a Anaru, a Piripi, a Tamati, a Patoromu, a Matiu, a Hēmi tama a Arapiu, a Haimona Heroti, a Hūrā te teina o Hēmi. <verse eid="ACT 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 1:14" />Ko ēnei katoa kotahi tonu te whaka­aro i ū ai ki te īnoi, ki te kara­kia, me ngā wāhine; me te whaea o Īhu, me Meri; me ōna tēina.<verse eid="ACT 1:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 1:15" />I aua rā, ka whaka­tika a Pita i waenga­nui o ngā ākonga; ā, he toko­maha ngā tāngata i hui­hui, kei te kotahi rau e rua tekau; ā, ka mea, <verse eid="ACT 1:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 1:16" />“E hoa mā, e ōku tēina, i tika anō kia whaka­ritea tēnei karaipi­ture, tā te Wairua Tapu i kōrero­tia rā i mua e te māngai o Rāwiri mō Hūrā, mō te kai­ārahi i te hunga nāna i hopu a Īhu. <verse eid="ACT 1:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 1:17" />I hui­huia tahi­tia hoki ia ki a tātou, i a ia anō tētahi wāhi o tēnei mahi.”<verse eid="ACT 1:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 1:18" />(Nā, hokona ana e taua tangata tētahi māra ki te utu o tōna hara; ā, taka tūpou iho, kōara pū i waenga­nui, pakaru katoa ki waho ōna whēkau. <verse eid="ACT 1:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 1:19" />I mōhio­tia tēnei e te hunga katoa e noho ana i Hiruhārama; nā reira taua wāhi i huaina ai ki tō tātou reo ko Akērama, arā ko te Māra o te Toto.)<verse eid="ACT 1:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 1:20" />“Kua oti hoki te tuhi­tuhi ki te puka­puka o Ngā Waiata,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 1:20">‘Kia uru­rua­tia tōna nohoa­nga,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 1:20">kaua hoki tētahi tangata e noho ki reira’,</para>
  <para style="m" vid="ACT 1:20">me tēnei:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 1:20">‘Kia riro tāna mahi tiro­tiro i tētahi atu.’<verse eid="ACT 1:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 1:21" />“Nō reira, ko ngā tāngata i haere tahi nei tātou, i ngā wā katoa i hāere­ere mai ai, i hāere­ere atu ai te Ariki, a Īhu i roto i a tātou, <verse eid="ACT 1:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 1:22" />hei te iri­iri­nga a Hoani tīmata ai, ā tae noa ki te rā i tango­hia atu ai ia i a tātou, me whaka­tū tētahi o ērā hei hoa mō tātou ki te whaka­atu i tōna aranga mai.”<verse eid="ACT 1:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 1:23" />Ā, toko­rua a rātou i whaka­rite ai, ko Hōhepa i huaina nei ko Pāhapa, ko tētahi o ōna ingoa ko Hutuha, rāua ko Matiaha. <verse eid="ACT 1:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 1:24" />Nā, ka īnoi rātou, ka mea, “Ko koe, e te Ariki, e mōhio ana ki ngā ngākau o te katoa, māu e whaka­atu ko wai o tēnei toko­rua tāu i whiri­whiri ai, <verse eid="ACT 1:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 1:25" />hei tango i te wāhi i tēnei mahi minita, i te tū­ranga āpō­toro hoki, i taka atu a Hūrā, he mea kia haere ai ia ki tōna wāhi.” <verse eid="ACT 1:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 1:26" />Nā, ka makā e rātou ō rāua rota; ā, ka tau te rota ki a Matiaha; ā, uru ana ia ki ngā āpō­toro tekau mā tahi.<verse eid="ACT 1:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="ACT 2" />
  <para style="s1">Te Haerenga Mai o te Wairua Tapu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 2:1" />Ā, nō ka taka mai te rā o te Petekoha, e noho tahi ana rātou katoa i te wāhi kotahi. <verse eid="ACT 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 2:2" />Nā, puta whaka­rere mai ana he haruru nui nō te rangi, ānō he hau nui e keri ana, ā, kī katoa te whare i noho ai rātou. <verse eid="ACT 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 2:3" />Heoi, puta mai ana ki a rātou ētahi arero he mea manga­nga, ānō he ahi, ā, tau iho ana ki runga ki tēnei, ki tēnei o rātou. <verse eid="ACT 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 2:4" />Nā, kī katoa rātou i te Wairua Tapu, ā, ka tīmata te kōrero rere­kē ana ngā reo, rite tonu ki tā te Wairua i hoatu ai ki a rātou kia kōrero­tia.<verse eid="ACT 2:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 2:5" />I Hiruhārama anō e noho ana ētahi Hūrai, he hunga whaka­aro, nō ngā iwi katoa i raro o te rangi. <verse eid="ACT 2:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 2:6" />Nā, i te wā i rangona ai taua haruru, ka whaka­rā­po­poto te mano, ka poro­raru, nō te mea ka rangona e tērā, e tērā, tōna reo e kōrero­tia ana e rātou. <verse eid="ACT 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 2:7" />Nā, ka oho rātou katoa, ka mīharo, ka mea, “Nā, ehara ianei ēnei katoa e kōrero nei i te hunga nō Kariri? <verse eid="ACT 2:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 2:8" />He aha tātou ka rongo nei, ia tangata, ia tangata, i ō tātou reo o tō tātou whānau­tanga? <verse eid="ACT 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 2:9" />Ko te hunga o Patia, o Meria, o Erama, ko ngā mea e noho ana i Mehopotamia, i Hūria, i Kaparokia, i Ponoto, i Āhia, <verse eid="ACT 2:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 2:10" />i Perikia, i Pamapu­ria, i Īhipa, i ngā wāhi o Ripia e pātata ana ki Hairini, me ngā manu­hiri o Roma, ngā Hūrai, ngā poro­hira­iti, <verse eid="ACT 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 2:11" />ngā Kariti, ngā Ārapi, e rongo ana tātou i a rātou e whaka­puaki ana i ngā mahi tohu a te Atua, nō tātou anō ngā reo.” <verse eid="ACT 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 2:12" />Ā, mīharo katoa ana rātou, pōhēhē ana, ka mea tētahi ki tētahi, “He aha tēnei?”<verse eid="ACT 2:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 2:13" />Ko ētahi i tāwai, i mea, “E kī ana rātou i te wāina hou!”<verse eid="ACT 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Kupu a Pita</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 2:14" />Otirā, ka whaka­tika a Pita me te tekau mā tahi, ka hiki­tia tōna reo, ka whai kupu ki a rātou, “E ngā tāngata o Hūria, me koutou katoa e noho nei i Hiruhārama, kia mōhio koutou ki tēnei, kia whai tari­nga mai ki āku kupu. <verse eid="ACT 2:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 2:15" />Kāhore hoki o ēnei hau­rangi me tā koutou e whaka­aro nei, ko te toru noa hoki tēnei o ngā hāora o te rā. <verse eid="ACT 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 2:16" />Engari, ko te mea tēnei i kōrero­tia e Hoera poro­piti:<verse eid="ACT 2:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 2:17" />‘Ā, tēnei ake kei ngā rā whaka­mutu­nga, e ai tā te Atua,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:17">ka ringi­hia e ahau tōku Wairua ki ngā kiko­kiko katoa;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:17">ka poro­piti hoki ā koutou tama, ā koutou tamā­hine,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:17">e kite anō ā koutou tai­tama­riki i ngā kite­nga,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:17">ka moe­moeā hoki ō koutou kaumātua.<verse eid="ACT 2:17" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 2:18" />Āe, ka ringi­hia anō e ahau tōku Wairua i aua rā,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:18">ki āku pono­nga tāne, ki āku pono­nga wāhine;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:18">ā, ka poro­piti rātou.<verse eid="ACT 2:18" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 2:19" />Ka whaka­kitea anō e ahau ngā mea whaka­mīharo i te rangi i runga,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:19">me ngā tohu ki te whenua i raro;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:19">he toto, he kāpura, he paowa po­ngere. <verse eid="ACT 2:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 2:20" />Ko te rā ka huri hei pōuri,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:20">ko te marama hoki hei toto,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:20">i mua o te pu­tanga mai o te rā o te Ariki,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:20">taua rā nui whaka­hara­hara, rongo­nui.<verse eid="ACT 2:20" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 2:21" />Nā, ko reira ora ai te hunga katoa e karanga ana ki te ingoa o te Ariki.’<verse eid="ACT 2:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 2:22" />“E ngā tāngata o Īharaira, kia rongo koutou ki ēnei kupu; Ko Īhu o Nahareta, he tangata i tino whai­tohu­ngia e te Atua ki a koutou i runga i ngā mere­kara, i ngā mea whaka­mīharo, i ngā tohu i mea ai te Atua kia mahia e ia i waenga­nui o koutou, e mōhio ana anō rā koutou. <verse eid="ACT 2:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 2:23" />Ko tēnei tangata i tukua atu, he mea i āta whaka­aroa, ā, i mōhio­tia noatia ake e te Atua, tango­hia ana e koutou, whaka­matea iho, he mea rīpeka nā te ringa o ngā tāngata kino. <verse eid="ACT 2:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 2:24" />Nā te Atua ia i whaka­ara ake, nāna i wewete ngā mamae o te mate; nō te mea e kore ia e taea te pupuri e taua mate. <verse eid="ACT 2:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 2:25" />Ko tā Rāwiri kōrero hoki tēnei mōna:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:25">‘I kite ahau i te Ariki i mua i tōku aro­aro i ngā rā katoa;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:25">kei tōku ringa matau nei ia,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:25">e kore ai ahau e whaka­kori­koria.<verse eid="ACT 2:25" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 2:26" />Koia i koa ai tōku ngākau,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:26">i whaka­mana­mana ai tōku arero;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:26">i takoto tū­mana­ko ai anō ōku kiko­kiko.<verse eid="ACT 2:26" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 2:27" />Nō te mea e kore e waiho e koe tōku wairua i te rēinga,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:27">e kore anō e tukua tāu Mea Tapu kia kite i te pirau.<verse eid="ACT 2:27" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 2:28" />Kua whaka­kitea e koe ki ahau ngā hua­rahi o te ora;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:28">ka meinga e koe kia kī tonu tōku koa i tōu aro­aro.’<verse eid="ACT 2:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 2:29" />“E ōku tēina, e tika ana kia aronui he kupu ki a koutou mō te tupuna nei mō Rāwiri, arā kua mate ia, kua tanu­mia, kei a tātou anō tōna urupā, ā, taea noatia tēnei rā. <verse eid="ACT 2:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 2:30" />I te mea he poro­piti ia, ā, i mōhio kua oati te Atua i te oati ki a ia, ka whaka­puta­ina ake tētahi, he hua nō tōna hope, hei noho ki runga ki tōna torōna. <verse eid="ACT 2:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 2:31" />Ā, i tāna kite wawe i tēnei, kōrero­tia ana e ia te aranga o te Karaiti, arā:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:31">‘Kīhai tōna wairua i waiho i te rēinga,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:31">kīhai anō tōna kiko­kiko i kite i te pirau.’<verse eid="ACT 2:31" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 2:32" />Kua whaka­ara­hia ake tēnei Īhu e te Atua: ko mātou katoa ngā kai­whaka­atu. <verse eid="ACT 2:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 2:33" />Ā, ka oti nei ia te whaka­nui e te ringa matau o te Atua, ā, ka hōmai nei ki a ia e te Matua te Wairua Tapu i kōrero­tia rā i mua, nā, kua ringi­hia mai e ia tēnei, e kite nei, e rongo nei koutou. <verse eid="ACT 2:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 2:34" />Kāhore hoki a Rāwiri i kake ki te rangi; heoi, e mea ana ia:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:34">‘I mea te Ariki ki tōku Ariki,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:34">Hei tōku matau koe noho ai,<verse eid="ACT 2:34" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 2:35" />kia meinga rā anō e ahau ōu hoa­riri hei tū­ranga wae­wae mōu.’<verse eid="ACT 2:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 2:36" />“Nō reira rā, kia mātau pū te whare katoa o Īharaira, kua meinga e te Atua hei Ariki, hei Karaiti, taua Īhu i rīpeka­tia nā e koutou.”<verse eid="ACT 2:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 2:37" />Nō rātou ka rongo, ka wero­wero i roto i ō rātou ngākau, ka mea ki a Pita rātou ko ērā atu āpō­toro, “E ngā tuā­kana, me aha mātou?”<verse eid="ACT 2:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 2:38" />Nā, ko te mea­tanga a Pita ki a rātou, “Rīpenetā, kia iri­iria, tēnā tangata, tēnā tangata o koutou i runga i te ingoa o Īhu Karaiti, hei muru­nga hara; ā, ka riro i a koutou te mea hōmai, arā te Wairua Tapu. <verse eid="ACT 2:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 2:39" />Ki a koutou hoki, ki ā koutou tama­riki, te kupu hōmai, ki te hunga katoa anō o tawhiti, ki ngā mea e karanga­tia e te Ariki, e tō tātou Atua, ki a ia.”<verse eid="ACT 2:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 2:40" />He maha atu anō ngā kupu i kōrero ai, i kauwhau ai ia, i mea ai, “Me whaka­ora koutou i a koutou i tēnei whaka­tupu­ranga parori kē.” <verse eid="ACT 2:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 2:41" />Nā, ko ngā mea tonu i tango i tāna kupu i iri­iria, me te mea e toru mano ngā wairua i honoa mai ki a rātou i taua rā. <verse eid="ACT 2:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 2:42" />Ā, i ū tonu rātou ki te whaka­ako­ranga a ngā āpō­toro, ki te kotahi­tanga, ki te whawhati taro, ā, ki te īnoi.<verse eid="ACT 2:42" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Ora i waenga o te Hunga Whakapono</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 2:43" />Tau iho ana te wehi ki ngā wairua katoa; he maha hoki ngā mea whaka­mīharo me ngā tohu i meinga e ngā āpō­toro. <verse eid="ACT 2:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 2:44" />I noho tahi anō te hunga whaka­pono katoa, i hui­huia anō hoki ā rātou mea katoa; <verse eid="ACT 2:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 2:45" />i hokona atu hoki ā rātou rawa me ngā taonga, tu­whai­na ana mā te katoa, rite tonu, ki te mate o tēnei, o tēnei. <verse eid="ACT 2:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 2:46" />Haere tonu ana hoki rātou i tēnei rā, i tēnei rā ki te teme­para, kotahi tonu anō te whaka­aro; whawhati taro ana i ō rātou kāinga, kai ana i ā rātou kai i runga i te koa, i te ngākau tapa­tahi; <verse eid="ACT 2:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 2:47" />e whaka­moe­miti ana ki te Atua, e pai­ngia ana hoki e te iwi katoa. Ā, honoa mai ana e te Ariki ki a rātou i tēnā rā, i tēnā rā, i tēnā rā, te hunga e whaka­ora­ngia ana.<verse eid="ACT 2:47" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 2" />
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="ACT 3" />
  <para style="s1">Ka Whakaorangia tētahi Pīnono Kopa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 3:1" />Nā, e haere tahi atu ana a Pita rāua ko Hoani ki te teme­para i te hāora īnoi, i te iwa o ngā hāora. <verse eid="ACT 3:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 3:2" />Nā, ka kawea mai tētahi tangata, he kopa nō te kōpū mai anō o tōna whaea, he mea whaka­takoto i ngā rā katoa ki te kūwaha o te teme­para i huaina nei ko Āta­ahua, ki te tono mea māna i te hunga e tomo ana ki te teme­para. <verse eid="ACT 3:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 3:3" />Nō tōna kite­nga i a Pita rāua ko Hoani meāke tomo ki te teme­para, ka tono ia i tētahi mea māna. <verse eid="ACT 3:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 3:4" />Nā, ka whaka­mau atu ngā kanohi o Pita rāua ko Hoani ki a ia, ka mea, “Ti­tiro mai ki a māua.” <verse eid="ACT 3:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 3:5" />Ka whaka­rongo ia ki a rāua, hua noa e riro mai tētahi mea a rāua māna. <verse eid="ACT 3:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 3:6" />Anō rā ko Pita, “Ko te hiriwa me te kōura kāhore i ahau; ko te mea ia kei ahau, māku tēnā e hoatu ki a koe; i runga i te ingoa o Īhu Karaiti o Nahareta, whaka­tika, haere.” <verse eid="ACT 3:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 3:7" />Kātahi ia ka hopu i tōna ringa matau ka whaka­ara ake i a ia. I reira tonu kua whai kaha ōna wae­wae me ngā pona. <verse eid="ACT 3:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 3:8" />Ā, ko tōna mawhiti­tanga ake, ka tū, ka tīmata te haere, tomo tahi ana me rāua ki te teme­para, e haere ana, tūpeke ana, e whaka­moe­miti ana ki te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 3:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 3:9" />Ā, i kite te iwi katoa i a ia e haere ana, e whaka­moe­miti ana ki te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 3:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 3:10" />Kātahi rātou ka mōhio ki a ia, ko ia anō tērā i noho rā ki te tatau Āta­ahua o te teme­para, tono mea ai māna; nā, nui atu tō rātou mīharo me te ihi­ihi ki taua mea i pā ki a ia.<verse eid="ACT 3:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Kupu a Pita i roto i te Temepara</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 3:11" />I a ia e pupuri ana ki a Pita rāua ko Hoani, ka oma atu te iwi katoa ki a rātou i te whaka­mahau i huaina nei ko tā Horomona, nui rawa te whaka­mīharo. <verse eid="ACT 3:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 3:12" />Ā, i te kite­nga o Pita, ka whai kupu atu ia ki te iwi, “E ngā tāngata o Īharaira, he aha tā koutou e mīharo nei ki tēnei tangata? He aha hoki koutou ka whaka­mau ai te ti­tiro ki a māua, me te mea he mana nō māua ake he ngākau kara­kia rānei i meatia ai ia kia haere? <verse eid="ACT 3:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 3:13" />Nā te Atua o Āperahama, o Īhaka, o Hākopa, nā te Atua o ō tātou mātua, i whaka­korōria tāna Tama a Īhu; ko tā koutou i tuku nā, i whaka­kāhore nā i te aro­aro o Pirato, kua oti rā i a ia kia tukua ia. <verse eid="ACT 3:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 3:14" />Otirā, whaka­kāhore­tia ana e koutou te Mea Tapu, te Mea Tika, tonoa ana ko te tangata kōhuru kia hōmai ki a koutou. <verse eid="ACT 3:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 3:15" />Patua ana hoki e koutou te Take o te Ora; kua whaka­ara­hia nei ia e te Atua i te hunga mate, ko mātou nei ōna kai­whaka­atu. <verse eid="ACT 3:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 3:16" />Ā, nā te whaka­pono ki tōna ingoa i meinga ai e tōna ingoa tēnei tangata kia kaha, e kite nei, e mātau nei koutou; āe rā, ko te whaka­pono ki a ia te mea nāna i hoatu tēnei ora nui ki tēnei i te aro­aro o koutou katoa.<verse eid="ACT 3:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 3:17" />“Nā, e ōku tēina, e mahara ana ahau nā te kūware tēnā mahi a koutou, pērā i tā ō koutou ranga­tira. <verse eid="ACT 3:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 3:18" />Engari, ko ngā mea a te Atua i whaka­kitea i mua e te māngai o ngā poro­piti katoa, mō tāna Karaiti kia whaka­mamae­tia, kua rite ēnei i a ia. <verse eid="ACT 3:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 3:19" />Nō reira, rīpe­netā, ā, tahuri mai anō koutou, kia murua ai ō koutou hara, kia puta mai ai i te aro­aro o te Ariki he wā whaka­hauora. <verse eid="ACT 3:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 3:20" />Ā, kia tonoa mai ai e ia te Karaiti i whaka­ritea nei mō koutou, arā a Īhu. <verse eid="ACT 3:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 3:21" />Kua takoto nei te tikanga kia noho ia ki te rangi ā taea noatia ngā wā o te whaka­hoki­nga mai o ngā mea katoa, i kōrero ai te Atua rā te māngai o āna poro­piti tapu nō te tīma­tanga mai anō o te ao. <verse eid="ACT 3:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 3:22" />I mea rā hoki a Mohi, ‘Mā te Ariki, mā te Atua, e whaka­ara ake he poro­piti mō koutou i roto i ō koutou tēina, he pēnei anō me ahau. Ko ia tā koutou e whaka­rongo ai i ngā mea katoa e mea ai ia ki a koutou. <verse eid="ACT 3:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 3:23" />Ā taua wā, ko ngā wairua katoa e kore e whaka­rongo ki taua poro­piti, ka whaka­matea rawa­tia i roto i te iwi.’ <verse eid="ACT 3:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 3:24" />Āe rā, ko ngā poro­piti katoa o Hamuera iho anō, tae mai ki ō muri nei, ko te hunga katoa i kōrero, i whaka­atu anō hoki rātou i ngā rā nei. <verse eid="ACT 3:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 3:25" />Ko koutou aua tama a ngā poro­piti, a te kawe­nata hoki i whaka­takoto­ria e te Atua ki ō koutou mātua, i mea rā ia ki a Āperahama, ‘Mā tōu uri ka manaaki­tia ai ngā hapū katoa o te ao.’ <verse eid="ACT 3:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 3:26" />Mō koutou kē hoki i te tua­tahi, i tāna whaka­aranga ake ai i tāna Tama, i te tono­nga mai nei a te Atua i a ia ki a koutou hei manaaki i a koutou, hei i whaka­tahuri i tēnei, i tēnei o koutou i ō koutou kino.”<verse eid="ACT 3:26" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 3" />
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="ACT 4" />
  <para style="s1">Ko Pita rāua ko Hoani i mua i te Rūnanga</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 4:1" />Ā, i a rāua e kōrero ana ki te iwi, ka puta oho­rere mai ki a rāua ngā tohu­nga, te ranga­tira o te teme­para me ngā Haruki <verse eid="ACT 4:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 4:2" />he nui te pāwera mō tā rāua ako i te iwi, mō te kauwhau hoki i runga i a Īhu i te aranga mai i te hunga mate. <verse eid="ACT 4:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 4:3" />Nā, ka mau ō rātou ringa ki a rāua, meinga ana kia tiaki­na kia ao rā anō te rā, i te mea hoki kua ahi­ahi. <verse eid="ACT 4:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 4:4" />Otirā, he toko­maha o te hunga i rongo i te kupu i whaka­pono, ā, ko te toko­maha o ngā tāngata me te mea e rima mano.<verse eid="ACT 4:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 4:5" />Nā, i te aonga ake ka hui­hui ō rātou ranga­tira, ngā kaumātua, me ngā kara­ipi ki Hiruhārama, <verse eid="ACT 4:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 4:6" />rātou ko te tino tohu­nga, ko Anaha, ko Kaiapa, ko Hoani, ko Arēhanara, me ngā whanau­nga katoa o te tohu­nga nui. <verse eid="ACT 4:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 4:7" />Ā, nō ka whaka­tū­ria rāua ki waenga­nui, ka ui rātou, “Tēnā koa te mana, te ingoa rānei, i meatia ai tēnei e kōrua?”<verse eid="ACT 4:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 4:8" />Kātahi a Pita, kī tonu i te Wairua Tapu, ka mea ki a rātou, “E ngā ranga­tira o te iwi, e ngā kaumātua: <verse eid="ACT 4:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 4:9" />me­he­mea ki te uiuia māua āia­nei mō te mahi pai i mahia ki te tangata hauā, i pēhea­tia taua tangata i ora ai. <verse eid="ACT 4:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 4:10" />Kia mōhio koutou katoa, me te iwi katoa o Īharaira, nā te ingoa o Īhu Karaiti o Nahareta, i rīpeka­tia nā e koutou, i whaka­ara­hia rā e te Atua i te hunga mate, nāna tēnei i tū ora ai i tō koutou aro­aro. <verse eid="ACT 4:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 4:11" />Ko ia</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 4:11">‘te kōhatu i whaka­kāhore­tia nā e koutou, e ngā kai­hanga,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:11">ā, kua meinga nei hei ūpoko mō te koko­nga.’<verse eid="ACT 4:11" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 4:12" />Kāhore hoki he ora i tētahi atu; kāhore hoki he ingoa kē atu i raro o te rangi kua hōmai ki ngā tāngata, e ora ai tātou.”<verse eid="ACT 4:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 4:13" />Nā, ka kite rātou i te māia o Pita rāua ko Hoani, ā, ka mātau ki a rāua ehara i te mea whaka­ako, engari, he hunga kūware, ka mīharo rātou; ka mōhio hoki he hoa rāua nō Īhu. <verse eid="ACT 4:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 4:14" />Ka kite hoki i te tangata i whaka­ora­ngia e tū tahi ana rātou, kāhore rawa i taea tētahi kupu whaka­hē mā rātou. <verse eid="ACT 4:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 4:15" />Nā, ka tono rātou i a rāua kia haere ki waho o te rū­nanga, ā, ka kōrero­rero ki a rātou anō, <verse eid="ACT 4:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 4:16" />ka mea, “Me aha e tātou ēnei tāngata? Ka kite katoa nei hoki te hunga e noho ana i Hiruhārama, he mere­kara nui kua meinga nei, ā, e kore e āhei te whākore­kore e tātou. <verse eid="ACT 4:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 4:17" />Otiia, kia kaua ai e hōrapa atu ki roto ki te iwi, kia kaha tā tātou whaka­wehi i a rāua kei kōrero ki tētahi tangata ā muri nei i runga i tēnei ingoa.”<verse eid="ACT 4:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 4:18" />Ā, karanga­tia ana rāua e rātou, ka mea ki a rāua “Kia kaua rawa e kōrero, kia kaua e whaka­ako, i runga i te ingoa o Īhu.” <verse eid="ACT 4:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 4:19" />Nā, ka whaka­hoki a Pita rāua ko Hoani ki a rātou, ka mea, “Whaka­aroa e koutou, ka tika rānei ki te aro­aro o te Atua ko koutou kia whaka­rangona, kaua te Atua? <verse eid="ACT 4:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 4:20" />E kore hoki e āhei kia kaua e kōrero­tia e māua ngā mea i kite ai, i rongo ai mātou.” <verse eid="ACT 4:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 4:21" />Heoi, whaka­wehi ana anō rātou i a rāua, ā, tukua ana kia haere, kīhai hoki i kitea he mea e whiua ai rāua, i wehi i te iwi; i whaka­korōria katoa nei ngā tāngata i te Atua mō taua mea i meatia. <verse eid="ACT 4:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 4:22" />Nō te mea kua neke atu i te whā tekau ngā tau o te tangata i meinga nei ki a ia tēnei mere­kara whaka­ora.<verse eid="ACT 4:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Īnoi te Hunga Whakapono kia Māia</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 4:23" />Ā, ka oti rāua te tuku, ka haere ki ō rāua hoa, ā, kōrero­tia ana ngā mea katoa i kōrero ai ngā tohu­nga nui me ngā kaumātua ki a rāua. <verse eid="ACT 4:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 4:24" />Ā, i tō rātou rongo­nga, ka karanga ake rātou ki te Atua, he kotahi te reo, ka mea: “E te Ariki, nāu nei i hanga te rangi me te whenua, te moana, me ō reira mea katoa; <verse eid="ACT 4:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 4:25" />nāu te kupu i kōrero­tia e te Wairua Tapu, nā te māngai o tō mātou matua, o tāu pono­nga, o Rāwiri:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 4:25">‘He aha ka nana ai ngā tauiwi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:25">ka whaka­aro hori­hori ai ngā iwi?<verse eid="ACT 4:25" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 4:26" />I whaka­tika ake ngā kīngi o te whenua,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:26">i hui­hui ngā­tahi ngā ranga­tira,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:26">ki te whawhai ki te Ariki rāua ko tāna Karaiti.’<verse eid="ACT 4:26" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 4:27" />He pono nei hoki te hui­hui­nga ki tēnei pā o Herora, o Ponotio Pirato, o ngā tauiwi, rātou ko te iwi o Īharaira, ki tāu tama tapu, ki a Īhu i whaka­wahia nei e koe, <verse eid="ACT 4:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 4:28" />ki te mea i tā tōu ringa, i tā tōu whaka­aro i whaka­takoto ai i mua kia meatia. <verse eid="ACT 4:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 4:29" />Nā, ti­tiro iho, e te Ariki, āia­nei ki ā rātou kupu whaka­wehi. Tukua mai hoki ki au pono­nga kia tino māia te kōrero i tāu kupu. <verse eid="ACT 4:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 4:30" />Ko koe ia e totoro mai ana tōu ringa ki te whaka­ora; kia meatia hoki he tohu, he mea whaka­mīharo i runga i te ingoa o tāu Pono­nga tapu, o Īhu.”<verse eid="ACT 4:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 4:31" />I te mutu­nga o tā rātou īnoi, ka ngā­ueue te wāhi i mine ai rātou, ā, kī katoa rātou i te Wairua Tapu, nā, māia noa atu rātou ki te kōrero i te kupu a te Atua.<verse eid="ACT 4:31" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Tuwhaia te Hunga Whakapono i ā Rātou Taonga</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 4:32" />Kotahi anō ngākau, kotahi anō wairua o te mano o te hunga whaka­pono. Kīhai anō tētahi o rātou i mea, māna ake tētahi o āna taonga; heoi he mea hui­hui ā rātou mea katoa. <verse eid="ACT 4:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 4:33" />Ā, nui atu te kaha i whaka­pua­kina ai e ngā āpō­toro te aranga o te Ariki, o Īhu; he nui anō te aroha noa i runga i a rātou katoa. <verse eid="ACT 4:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 4:34" />Kāhore hoki tētahi o rātou i hapa; ko te hunga hoki he kāinga, he whare ō rātou, hokona atu ana e rātou, ā, mauria ana mai ngā utu o ngā mea i hokona, <verse eid="ACT 4:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 4:35" />whaka­takoto­ria ana ki ngā wae­wae o ngā āpō­toro. Nā, ka tu­whai­na mā ia tangata, mā ia tangata, he mea whaka­rite ki te mate o ia tangata.<verse eid="ACT 4:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 4:36" />Ā, ko Hohi i huaina e ngā āpō­toro ko Pānapa, (ko te tikanga tēnei ina whaka­māori­tia, ko te Tama a te Whaka­mārie­tanga,) he Rīwaiti, ko Kai­peru tōna kāinga. <verse eid="ACT 4:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 4:37" />He wāhi whenua tōna, nā, hokona atu ana, mauria ana ngā moni, whaka­takoto­ria ana ki ngā wae­wae o ngā āpō­toro.<verse eid="ACT 4:37" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 4" />
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="ACT 5" />
  <para style="s1">Ko Anania rāua ko Hapaira</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 5:1" />Nā, ko tētahi tangata ko Anania tōna ingoa, rāua ko tāna wahine, ko Hapaira, i hoko atu i tētahi whenua. <verse eid="ACT 5:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 5:2" />Ā, puri­tia ana e ia tētahi wāhi o te utu, ko tāna wahine hoki i mōhio ki taua mea huna, mauria ana tētahi wāhi, whaka­takoto­ria ana ki ngā wae­wae o ngā āpō­toro. <verse eid="ACT 5:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 5:3" />Nā, ko te mea­tanga atu a Pita, “E Anania, nā te aha i whaka­kīa ai tōu ngākau e Hātana kia teka koe ki te Wairua Tapu, kia puri­tia atu ai tētahi wāhi o te utu o te whenua? <verse eid="ACT 5:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 5:4" />I te mea kāhore anō i riro, he teka ianei nāu ake tāu mea? Ā, ka oti te hoko atu he teka ianei kei a koe tonu te tikanga? Nā te aha tēnei mea i whaka­aroa ai i roto i tōu ngākau? Kīhai hoki koe i teka ki te tangata, engari ki te Atua.” <verse eid="ACT 5:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 5:5" />Ā, nō te rongo­nga o Anania i ēnei kupu, hinga ana ki raro, mate rawa. He nui anō te wehi i tau ki te hunga katoa i rongo i ēnei mea. <verse eid="ACT 5:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 5:6" />Nā, ka whaka­tika ngā tai­tama­riki, takai ana i a ia, ā, maua atu ana ia ki waho, tanu­mia ana.<verse eid="ACT 5:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 5:7" />Ā, pātata ki te toru hāora i muri, ka tomo mai tāna wahine, kīhai hoki i mōhio he aha te mea kua meatia. <verse eid="ACT 5:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 5:8" />Nā, ko te mea­tanga a Pita ki a ia, “Kōrero mai ki ahau, ko te utu rānei tērā i hokona atu ai e kōrua te whenua?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 5:8">Ka mea ia, “Āe, koia tēnā.”<verse eid="ACT 5:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 5:9" />Ka mea a Pita ki a ia, “He aha kōrua i whaka­aro tahi ai ki te whaka­mā­tau­tau i te Wairua o te Ariki? Nana, kei te kūwaha ngā wae­wae o te hunga i tanu­mia ai tāu tāne, mā rātou koe e kawe ki waho.” <verse eid="ACT 5:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 5:10" />Nā, hinga tonu iho ia ki ōna wae­wae, hemo rawa. Ā, ko te tomo­nga mai o ngā tai­tama­riki, roko­hanga mai kua mate, nā kawea ana ia ki waho, tanu­mia ana ki te taha o tāna tāne. <verse eid="ACT 5:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 5:11" />Ā, nui atu te wehi o te hāhi katoa, o te hunga katoa anō i rangona ai ēnei mea.<verse eid="ACT 5:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ngā Tohu me ngā Mea Whakamīharo</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 5:12" />Ā, nā ngā ringa o ngā āpō­toro i mahi ngā tohu maha, me ngā mea whaka­mīharo, i roto i te iwi; i noho hoki rātou katoa ki te whaka­mahau o Horomona, kotahi anō te whaka­aro. <verse eid="ACT 5:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 5:13" />Tēnā ko ērā atu tāngata kīhai rawa tētahi i māia ki te whaka­uru mai ki a rātou; otirā, whaka­nuia ana rātou e te iwi. <verse eid="ACT 5:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 5:14" />Ā, he nui noa atu te hunga whaka­pono i honoa mai ki te Ariki, tōna tini o te tāne, o te wāhine. <verse eid="ACT 5:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 5:15" />Nā reira hoki, ka mauria e rātou ngā tūroro ki ngā ara, whaka­takoto­ria ana ki runga i ngā moenga, i ngā whā­riki, me kore noa e tau­maru­maru iho ki tētahi o rātou te ātā­rangi o Pita, i a ia e haere ana. <verse eid="ACT 5:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 5:16" />I hui katoa mai anō te mano i ngā pā katoa e pātata ana ki Hiruhārama, me te mau mai i ngā tūroro, i te hunga e whaka­pō­rea­rea­tia ana e ngā wairua poke; ā, whaka­ora­ngia ana rātou katoa.<verse eid="ACT 5:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Whakawhiungia ngā Āpōtoro</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 5:17" />Me i reira ka whaka­tika te tohu­nga nui rātou ko ōna hoa katoa, arā te wehe­nga ki ngā Haruki, kī tonu hoki rātou i te hae. <verse eid="ACT 5:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 5:18" />Ā, ka pā ō rātou ringa ki ngā āpō­toro, makā ana rātou ki te whare here­here nui. <verse eid="ACT 5:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 5:19" />Otirā, nā tētahi ana­hera a te Ariki i uaki ngā tatau o te whare here­here i te pō; āra­hina mai ana rātou e ia ki waho, ka mea, <verse eid="ACT 5:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 5:20" />“Haere, e tū i roto i te teme­para, ka kōrero ki te iwi i ngā kupu katoa o tēnei ora.” <verse eid="ACT 5:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 5:21" />Ā, ka rongo rātou i tēnei, ka tomo ki te teme­para i te atatū, ka whaka­ako.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 5:21">Nā, ko te haere­nga o te tohu­nga nui rātou ko ōna hoa, karanga­tia ana kia hui­hui te rū­nanga me ngā kaumātua katoa o ngā tama a Īharaira, ā, tonoa ana he tangata ki te whare here­here hei tiki i a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 5:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 5:22" />Otirā, ko ngā kātipa i tae mai, kīhai i kite i a rātou i roto i te whare here­here, nā, ka hoki mai, ka kōrero, <verse eid="ACT 5:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 5:23" />ka mea, “Rokohina atu e mātou e tūtaki tonu ana te whare here­here ū tonu, me ngā kai­tiaki e tū ana i waho o ngā tatau; nō te hua­kanga atu, kāhore he tangata i kitea e mātou i roto.” <verse eid="ACT 5:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 5:24" />Ā, nō ka rongo te ranga­tira o te teme­para rātou ko ngā tohu­nga nui ki ēnei kupu, ka poro­raru rātou, he aha rā te tuku­nga iho o taua mea. <verse eid="ACT 5:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 5:25" />Nā, ko te haere­nga mai o tētahi, ka kōrero ki a rātou, ka mea, “Nana, ko te hunga i makā rā e koutou ki te whare here­here, e tū mai nei i te teme­para, e whaka­ako ana i te iwi!” <verse eid="ACT 5:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 5:26" />Kātahi, ka haere te ranga­tira rātou ko ngā kātipa, ā, āra­hina mai ana rātou, otirā, kīhai i taka­kino­tia; i wehi hoki rātou i te iwi, kei ākina rātou ki te kōhatu.<verse eid="ACT 5:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 5:27" />Ā, ka oti rātou te ārahi mai, ka whaka­tū­ria ki mua i te rū­nanga. Nā, ka ui te tohu­nga nui ki a rātou, <verse eid="ACT 5:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 5:28" />ka mea, “Kīhai ianei mātou i āta whaka­tūpato i a koutou kia kaua e whaka­ako i runga i tēnei ingoa? Nā, kua kī nei Hiruhārama i tā koutou whaka­ako­ranga, ā, e mea ana koutou kia whaka­iria ngā toto o tēnei tangata ki runga i a mātou.”<verse eid="ACT 5:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 5:29" />Nā, ka whaka­hoki a Pita rātou ko ngā āpō­toro, ka mea, “Me whaka­rongo rā mātou ki te Atua, kaua ki te tangata. <verse eid="ACT 5:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 5:30" />Nā te Atua o ō tātou tūpuna i whaka­ara ake a Īhu, i whaka­matea nā e koutou, he mea whaka­iri ki te rākau. <verse eid="ACT 5:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 5:31" />Kua oti ia te whaka­noho e te ringa matau o te Atua ki runga, hei Piriniha, hei Kai­whaka­ora, hei hōmai i te rīpe­netā, i te muru­nga hara ki a Īharaira. <verse eid="ACT 5:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 5:32" />Ko mātou anō ngā kai­whaka­atu i ēnei mea; ko te Wairua Tapu hoki, i hōmai nei e te Atua ki te hunga e rongo ana ki a ia.”<verse eid="ACT 5:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 5:33" />Otirā, i tō rātou rongo­nga i tēnei, tū tonu ki ō rātou ngākau, ā, ka whaka­aro kia whaka­matea rātou. <verse eid="ACT 5:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 5:34" />Nā, ka whaka­tika tētahi o ngā Parihi i roto i te rū­nanga, ko Kamariera te ingoa, he kai­whaka­ako i te ture, he tangata e whaka­nuia ana e te iwi katoa, ka mea, kia neke­hia atu aua tāngata ki waho mō tētahi wā poto nei. <verse eid="ACT 5:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 5:35" />Nā, ko tāna mea­tanga ki a rātou, “E ngā tāngata o Īharaira, kia tūpato ki tā koutou e mea ai ki ēnei tāngata. <verse eid="ACT 5:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 5:36" />I ngā rā ki muri ka whaka­tika ake a Teura, me te whaka­ari i a ia, ko ia he tangata nui; piri atu ana ki a ia ētahi tāngata, pātata ki te whā rau. Nā patua iho ia; ā, ko te hunga katoa i whaka­rongo ki a ia, whaka­marara­tia atu ana, ā, kore ake. <verse eid="ACT 5:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 5:37" />Ā muri iho i taua tangata ka whaka­tika ake ko Hūrā o Kariri i ngā rā o te tatau­ranga, ā, kūmea atu ana e ia ētahi o te iwi ki te whai i a ia; i ngaro anō hoki tēnā; ā, ko te hunga katoa i whaka­rongo ki a ia, whaka­marara­tia atu ana. <verse eid="ACT 5:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 5:38" />Nā, ko tāku kupu tēnei ki a koutou, kāti te mea ki ēnei tāngata. Waiho noa iho rātou! Ki te mea hoki nā te tangata tēnei whaka­aro, tēnei mahi, tērā e whaka­kāhore­tia, <verse eid="ACT 5:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 5:39" />otirā, me­he­mea nā te Atua, e kore rawa e taea e koutou te whaka­kāhore. Kei tūpono hoki e whawhai kē ana koutou ki te Atua!”<verse eid="ACT 5:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 5:40" />Ā, whaka­ae ana rātou ki a ia; nā, ka karanga­tia ngā āpō­toro ki a rātou, ka whiua, ka whaka­tūpato­ria kia kaua rawa e kōrero i runga i te ingoa o Īhu, ā, tukua ana rātou kia haere. <verse eid="ACT 5:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 5:41" />Heoi, haere hari atu ana rātou i te aro­aro o te rū­nanga, mō rātou kua meinga e pai ana kia whaka­tau­reka­reka­tia mō te Ingoa. <verse eid="ACT 5:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 5:42" />Ā, i ngā rā katoa, i roto i te teme­para, i ngā kāinga rānei, kāhore e mutu ana tā rātou whaka­ako, tā rātou kauwhau i a Īhu, ko te Karaiti ia.<verse eid="ACT 5:42" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 5" />
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="ACT 6" />
  <para style="s1">Ngā Kaiāwhina Tokowhitu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 6:1" />Nā, i aua rā, i te mea ka toko­maha haere ngā ākonga ka amu­amu ngā Hūrai Kariki ki ngā Hiperu, nō te mea i mahue ō rātou pouaru i ngā tūw­hanga mea o tēnei rā, o tēnei rā. <verse eid="ACT 6:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 6:2" />Kātahi, ka karanga­tia e te tekau mā rua te mano o ngā ākonga, ka mea, “E kore e pai kia whaka­rērea e mātou te kupu a te Atua, ā, kia mahi tēpu. <verse eid="ACT 6:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 6:3" />Nō reira, e ngā tēina, tiro­hia mai i roto i a koutou kia toko­whitu ngā tāngata e kōrero­tia paitia ana, e kī ana i te Wairua Tapu, i te mātau­ranga, ā, mā mātou rātou e whaka­tū ki tēnei mahi. <verse eid="ACT 6:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 6:4" />Ko mātou ia ka ū tonu ki te īnoi, ki te mahi i te kupu.”<verse eid="ACT 6:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 6:5" />Ā, pai katoa te mano ki taua kōrero; nā, whiri­whiria ana e rātou a Tepene, he tangata e kī ana i te whaka­pono, i te Wairua Tapu, rātou ko Piripi, ko Porokoru, ko Nikanora, ko Timona, ko Paramena, ko Nīkora, he poro­hira­iti nō Anatioka. <verse eid="ACT 6:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 6:6" />Nā, whaka­tū­ria ana rātou ki te aro­aro o ngā āpō­toro; ka īnoi ērā, ka whaka­pā i ngā ringa ki runga ki a rātou.<verse eid="ACT 6:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 6:7" />Heoi, tupu ana te kupu a te Atua. Tino nui haere ana te toko­maha o ngā ākonga i Hiruhārama; ā, he ope nui o ngā tohu­nga i tahuri mai ki te whaka­pono.<verse eid="ACT 6:7" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Hopukanga o Tepene</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 6:8" />Ā, ko Tepene, kī tonu i te whaka­pono, i te mana, nui atu ngā mere­kara me ngā tohu i meatia e ia i roto i te iwi. <verse eid="ACT 6:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 6:9" />Nā, ka whaka­tika ētahi o te whaka­mine­nga, e kīa nei ko te whaka­mine­nga o ngā Riperetini, ētahi hoki o te whaka­mine­nga o te hunga o Hairini, o te hunga o Arehāna­ria, o te hunga hoki o Kiri­kia, o Āhia, ka totohe ki a Tepene. <verse eid="ACT 6:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 6:10" />Otirā, kīhai i taea e rātou te tū atu ki tōna mātau­ranga me te wairua i kōrero ai ia. <verse eid="ACT 6:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 6:11" />Nā, ka whaka­kīkī rātou i ētahi tāngata hei mea, “I rongo mātou i a ia e kōrero kohu­kohu ana mō Mohi, mō te Atua anō hoki.” <verse eid="ACT 6:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 6:12" />Nā, ka tahuri rātou ki te whaka­oho­oho i te iwi, i ngā kaumātua, me ngā kara­ipi hoki, nā, ka mau ia i a rātou, hopu­kia ana, kawea atu ana ki te rū­nanga. <verse eid="ACT 6:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 6:13" />Ā, whaka­tū­ria ana e rātou ētahi kai­whaka­pae teka, nāna i mea, “Kāhore e mutu te kōrero kino a tēnei tangata mō tēnei kāinga tapu, mō te ture hoki; <verse eid="ACT 6:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 6:14" />i rongo hoki mātou ki a ia e mea ana, ‘Mā tēnei Īhu o Nahareta e whaka­ngaro te kāinga nei, e whaka­puta kē hoki ngā rite­nga i hōmai e Mohi ki a tātou.’ ” <verse eid="ACT 6:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 6:15" />Ā, ko te hunga katoa e noho ana i te rū­nanga, ka ti­tiro pū ki a ia, ka kite i tōna mata, ānō he mata nō te ana­hera.<verse eid="ACT 6:15" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 6" />
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="ACT 7" />
  <para style="s1">Te Whaikōrero a Tepene</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 7:1" />Kātahi, ka mea te tohu­nga nui, “He pono rānei ēnei mea?”<verse eid="ACT 7:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 7:2" />Nā, ka mea ia, “E ngā tēina, e ngā mātua, whaka­rongo mai. I puta te Atua o te korōria ki tō tātou matua, ki a Āperahama, i a ia i Mehopotamia, ā, kīanō i noho ki Harana, <verse eid="ACT 7:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 7:3" />ka mea ki a ia, ‘Haere atu i tōu whenua, i ōu whanau­nga, ā, e tomo ki te whenua e whaka­kitea e ahau ki a koe.’ <verse eid="ACT 7:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 7:4" />Nā, puta mai ana ia i te whenua o ngā Karari, noho ana ki Harana. Ā, nō te mate­nga o tōna pāpā, ka whaka­hekea mai ia i reira e te Atua ki tēnei whenua e noho nei koutou. <verse eid="ACT 7:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 7:5" />Ā, kīhai i hoatu tētahi kāinga mōna i konei, kore rawa, ahakoa he tū­ranga wae­wae noa; heoi, i oati ia, tērā e hōmai a konei hei kāinga mōna, mō tōna uri hoki i muri i a ia, ahakoa rā i taua wā kāhore āna tama­riki. <verse eid="ACT 7:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 7:6" />Ā, i pēnei te kōrero a te Atua, ‘Tērā tōna uri e noho manene ki te whenua kē; ka meinga hoki hei pono­nga, ā, e whā rau tau e tūkino­tia ana. <verse eid="ACT 7:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 7:7" />Nā, ko te iwi e meinga ai rātou hei pono­nga, ka whaka­wā­kia e ahau,’ e ai tā te Atua, ‘muri iho i tēnei ka puta mai rātou, ā, ka mahi ki ahau i tēnei wāhi.’ <verse eid="ACT 7:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 7:8" />Ā, i hōmai anō e ia ki a ia te kawe­nata o te kotinga. Ā, whānau ake tā Āperahama ko Īhaka, ā, i te waru o ngā rā ka kotia; ā, nā Īhaka ko Hākopa; nā Hākopa hoki ngā tūpuna kotahi tekau mā rua.<verse eid="ACT 7:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 7:9" />“Nā, ka hae ngā tūpuna ki a Hōhepa, ā, hokona ana ia ki Īhipa; otirā i a ia te Atua; <verse eid="ACT 7:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 7:10" />nāna ia i whaka­ora i ōna mate­nga katoa, ā, hoatu ana ki a ia he pai, he mātau­ranga i te aro­aro o Parao kīngi o Īhipa; ā, meinga ana ia e tērā hei kāwana mō Īhipa, mō tōna whare katoa hoki. <verse eid="ACT 7:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 7:11" />Nā, i reira ka puta he matekai ki te whenua katoa o Īhipa, o Kanaana, ā, he mate nui; kīhai rawa i kitea he oranga e ō tātou mātua. <verse eid="ACT 7:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 7:12" />Ā, nō te rongo­nga o Hākopa, e whai wīti ana a Īhipa, ka tonoa e ia ō tātou mātua, ko te tono­nga tua­tahi. <verse eid="ACT 7:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 7:13" />Ā, nō te tono­nga tuarua, ka whaka­mōhio­tia a Hōhepa ki ōna tuā­kana; ā, ka whaka­atu­ria ki a Parao te iwi o Hōhepa. <verse eid="ACT 7:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 7:14" />Nā, ka tono tāngata a Hōhepa ki te karanga i tōna pāpā, i a Hākopa ki a ia, i ōna huānga katoa hoki, e whitu tekau mā rima ngā wairua. <verse eid="ACT 7:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 7:15" />Nā, heke ana a Hākopa ki Īhipa, ā, ka mate a ia, me ō tātou mātua. <verse eid="ACT 7:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 7:16" />Ā, kawea atu ana rātou ki Hekeme, whaka­takoto­ria ana ki te urupā i hokona mai rā e Āperahama, he moni hiriwa te utu, i ngā tama a Hāmora i Hekeme.<verse eid="ACT 7:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 7:17" />“Ā, nō ka tata mai te wā mō te mea i kōrero­tia rā i mua, i oati­tia rā e te Atua ki a Āperahama, ka tupu te iwi, ka tini haere ki Īhipa, <verse eid="ACT 7:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 7:18" />ā, tae noa ki te pu­tanga ake o tētahi atu kīngi mō Īhipa, kīhai nei i mōhio ki a Hōhepa. <verse eid="ACT 7:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 7:19" />Ko ia te mea nāna i tini­hanga tō tātou iwi, i whaka­tupu kino ō tātou mātua, i meatia ai kia makā atu ā rātou tama­riki kei puta ki te ora. <verse eid="ACT 7:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 7:20" />Nō taua wā, ka whānau a Mohi, he tangata tino āta­ahua. E toru ngā marama i whaka­tupu­ria ai ia i roto i te whare o tōna pāpā, <verse eid="ACT 7:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 7:21" />ā, nō ka makā atu ia, ka tango­hia ake ia e te tamā­hine a Parao, ā, ata­whai­tia ana hei tama­iti ake māna. <verse eid="ACT 7:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 7:22" />Nā, i āta whaka­akona a Mohi ki ngā mea katoa o te mātau­ranga o ngā Īhipiana; ā, he mana rawa ia, i te kupu, i te mahi.<verse eid="ACT 7:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 7:23" />“Ā, ka tata ōna tau ki te whā tekau, ka uru mai te whaka­aro ki tōna ngākau kia haere ia ki ōna tuā­kana, ki ngā tama a Īharaira. <verse eid="ACT 7:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 7:24" />Ā, i tōna kite­nga i tētahi o rātou e tūkino­tia ana, ka āwhina ia i a ia, a patua iho e ia te Īhipiana, ā, ka whai utu mōna i tūkino­tia rā. <verse eid="ACT 7:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 7:25" />Hua noa e mōhio ōna tuā­kana, nōna te ringa e hōmai ai e te Atua te whaka­ora­nga mō rātou, heoi, kīhai rātou i mōhio. <verse eid="ACT 7:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 7:26" />Nā, i te aonga ake ka puta atu ia ki ētahi e whawhai ana ki a rāua, ka tahuri ki te wawao i a rāua, ka mea, ‘E hoa mā, he teina, he tua­kana kōrua; he aha kōrua ka kino ai ki a kōrua anō?’ <verse eid="ACT 7:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 7:27" />Otirā, peia atu ana ia e te tangata nāna te hē ki tōna hoa; i mea ia, ‘Nā wai koe i mea hei ranga­tira, hei kai­whaka­wā mō māua? <verse eid="ACT 7:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 7:28" />E mea ana koe ki te whaka­mate i ahau, me koe i whaka­mate rā i te Īhipiana ina­nahi?’ <verse eid="ACT 7:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 7:29" />Nā, ka tahuti a Mohi i taua kōrero, ā, noho manene ana i Miriana. Ā, toko­rua āna tama i whānau ki reira.<verse eid="ACT 7:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 7:30" />“Ā, nō ka tutuki ngā tau e whā tekau, ka puta ki a ia tētahi ana­hera a te Ariki i te koraha o Maunga Hinai, i roto i te mura ahi i te rākau. <verse eid="ACT 7:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 7:31" />Ā, nō te kite­nga o Mohi, ka mīharo ki taua whaka­kite­nga; ā, i a ia ka whaka­tata atu ki te mā­taki­taki, ka puaki mai te reo o te Ariki ki a ia, <verse eid="ACT 7:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 7:32" />‘Ko te Atua ahau o ōu mātua, ko te Atua o Āperahama, o Īhaka, o Hākopa.’ Nā, wiri ana a Mohi, kore rawa i kaha ki te ti­tiro atu. <verse eid="ACT 7:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 7:33" />Ā, ka mea mai te Ariki ki a ia, ‘Wete­kia atu ngā hū i ōu wae­wae; ko te wāhi hoki e tū nā koe he one­one tapu. <verse eid="ACT 7:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 7:34" />Kua tino kite hoki ahau i te mate o tōku iwi e noho nei i Īhipa, kua rongo hoki i tā rātou auē, ā, kua heke iho nei ahau ki te whaka­ora i a rātou. Nā, haere mai, ka tonoa koe e ahau ki Īhipa.’<verse eid="ACT 7:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 7:35" />“Nā ko taua Mohi i whaka­kāhore­tia rā e rātou, i mea rā rātou, ‘Nā wai koe i mea hei ranga­tira, hei kai­whaka­wā?’ Ko ia anō i tonoa e te Atua hei ranga­tira, hei kai­whaka­ora, he mea nā te ringa o te ana­hera i puta mai rā ki a ia i te rākau. <verse eid="ACT 7:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 7:36" />Nā, taua tangata rātou i ārahi atu, i muri iho i tāna mahi­nga i ngā mea whaka­mīharo, i ngā tohu, ki te whenua o Īhipa, ki te Moana Whero, ki te koraha hoki i ngā tau e whā tekau. <verse eid="ACT 7:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 7:37" />Ko taua Mohi anō tēnei i mea atu rā ki ngā tama­riki a Īharaira, ‘Mā te Atua e whaka­ara ake he poro­piti mō koutou i roto i ō koutou tēina, he pēnei me ahau.’ <verse eid="ACT 7:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 7:38" />Ko ia anō tēnei i te whaka­mine­nga i te koraha, rāua ko te ana­hera i kōrero rā ki a ia i Maunga Hinai, ko ō tātou mātua hoki; i riro mai ai i a ia ngā kupu ora hei hōmai ki a tātou.<verse eid="ACT 7:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 7:39" />“Kīhai nei ō tātou mātua i pai ki te whaka­rongo ki a ia, heoi, peia atu ana ia e rātou, ā, hoki ana ō rātou ngākau ki Īhipa. <verse eid="ACT 7:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 7:40" />Ā, mea ana rātou ki a Ārona, ‘Hangā mā tātou ētahi atua hei haere ki mua i a tātou; ko tēnei Mohi hoki i āra­hina mai nei tātou i te whenua o Īhipa, kāhore tātou e mātau kua ahatia rānei.’ <verse eid="ACT 7:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 7:41" />Heoi, hangā ana e rātou he kūao kau i aua rā, tāpaea ana he patu­nga tapu mā taua whaka­pakoko, ā, koa ana ō rātou ngākau ki ngā mahi a ō rātou ringa. <verse eid="ACT 7:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 7:42" />Nā, ka tahuri kē te Atua, tukua atu ana rātou kia kara­kia ki te ope o te rangi; kia pērā me te mea i tuhia ki te puka­puka a ngā poro­piti:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 7:42">‘I hōmai koia e koutou ki ahau</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:42">ngā patu­nga tapu me ngā whaka­here</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:42">i ngā tau e whā tekau i te koraha, e te whare o Īharaira?<verse eid="ACT 7:42" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 7:43" />Nā, kua mau koutou ki te ta­pe­nā­kara o Moroko,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:43">ki te whetū o tō koutou atua o Reipana,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:43">ki ngā whaka­pakoko i hangā e koutou hei koro­piko atu;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 7:43">nā, māku koutou e kawe atu ki tāwāhi o Papurōna.’<verse eid="ACT 7:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 7:44" />“I ō tātou mātua te ta­pe­nā­kara o te whaka­atu­ranga i te koraha, tāna hoki i whaka­rite ai, i mea ai ki a Mohi kia hangā e ia, kia rite ki te tauira i kite ai ia. <verse eid="ACT 7:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 7:45" />Ā, i ō rātou nā rā, nā ō tātou mātua i mau mai, i a rātou ko Hohua i haere mai ai ki te noho i te whenua o ngā tauiwi, i peia atu nei e te Atua i te aro­aro o ō tātou mātua, ā, taea noatia ngā rā i a Rāwiri; <verse eid="ACT 7:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 7:46" />i pai­ngia nei ia e te Atua, ā, i īnoi hoki māna e rapu he nohoa­nga mō te Atua o Hākopa. <verse eid="ACT 7:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 7:47" />Nā, Horomona ia i hanga he whare mōna.<verse eid="ACT 7:47" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" sid="ACT 7:48" />“He ahakoa rā, e kore te Runga Rawa e noho ki ngā whare i hangā e te ringa; ko tā te poro­piti hoki tēnā i mea ai:<verse eid="ACT 7:48" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="ACT 7:49" />‘Ko te rangi tōku torōna,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:49">ko te whenua tōku tū­ranga wae­wae.</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 7:49">He whare pēhea tā koutou e hanga ai mōku?’</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:49">e ai tā te Ariki;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:49">‘ā, ko tēhea te wāhi e oki­oki ai ahau?<verse eid="ACT 7:49" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="50" style="v" sid="ACT 7:50" />Ehara ianei i tōku ringa nāna ēnei mea katoa i hanga?’<verse eid="ACT 7:50" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" sid="ACT 7:51" />“E te hunga kakī mārō, kāhore nei i kotia te ngākau me ngā tari­nga, he whaka­keke tonu tā koutou ki te Wairua Tapu; rite tonu tā koutou ki tā ō koutou mātua. <verse eid="ACT 7:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="ACT 7:52" />Ko tēhea o ngā poro­piti kīhai i whaka­tupu­ria kino­tia e ō koutou mātua? Whaka­matea iho e rātou te hunga i poro­piti­tia ai te haere­nga mai o te Mea Tika; ko koutou nei ōna kai­tuku, ōna kai­kōhuru. <verse eid="ACT 7:52" /><verse number="53" style="v" sid="ACT 7:53" />Ko koutou, kua riro nā i a koutou te ture, i tā ngā ana­hera i whaka­takoto mai ai, heoi, kīhai i puri­tia e koutou.”<verse eid="ACT 7:53" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Ākina o Tepene ki te Kōhatu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" sid="ACT 7:54" />Ā, ka rongo rātou ki ēnei mea, nā tū rawa ki roto ki ō rātou ngākau, tetēā ana ō rātou niho ki a ia. <verse eid="ACT 7:54" /><verse number="55" style="v" sid="ACT 7:55" />Otiia ko ia, kī tonu i te Wairua Tapu, ti­tiro mata­tau atu ana ki te rangi, ka kite i te korōria o te Atua, i a Īhu hoki e tū ana i te ringa matau o te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 7:55" /><verse number="56" style="v" sid="ACT 7:56" />Ā, ka mea, “Nana, e kite ana ahau ko ngā rangi e tūhāhā ana, ā, ko te Tama a te tangata e tū ana i te ringa matau o te Atua!”<verse eid="ACT 7:56" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" sid="ACT 7:57" />Kātahi, rātou ka hāmama, he nui te reo, ka puru i ō rātou tari­nga, ā, kotahi tonu te omanga atu ki a ia, <verse eid="ACT 7:57" /><verse number="58" style="v" sid="ACT 7:58" />ka makā ia e rātou ki waho o te pā, ā, ākina ana ki te kōhatu. Ko ngā kai­titiro i whaka­takoto i ō rātou kākahu ki ngā wae­wae o tētahi tai­tama, ko Haora te ingoa. <verse eid="ACT 7:58" /><verse number="59" style="v" sid="ACT 7:59" />Heoi, ākina ana e rātou a Tepene ki te kōhatu, me ia e karanga ana ki te Ariki, e mea ana, “E te Ariki, e Īhu, tōku wairua ki a koe.” <verse eid="ACT 7:59" /><verse number="60" style="v" sid="ACT 7:60" />Kātahi, ia ka tūturi ki raro, ka karanga, he nui te reo, “E te Ariki, kaua tēnei mea e whaka­iria ki a rātou.” Ā, i tāna kōrero­tanga i tēnei, ka moe.<verse eid="ACT 7:60" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 7" />
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="ACT 8" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 8:1" />Ā, i reira a Haora e whaka­ae ana ki tōna mate­nga.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="ACT 8:1">Te Whakatoinga o Hoara i te Hāhi</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 8:1">Nā, i taua rā ka oho he whaka­toi­nga nui ki te hāhi i Hiruhārama, ā, marara katoa ana rātou, puta noa i ngā wāhi o Hūria, o Hamaria; kāhore ia ngā āpō­toro. <verse eid="ACT 8:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 8:2" />Ā, nā te hunga whaka­aro a Tepene i tanu, ā, he nui tā rātou tangi­hanga mōna.<verse eid="ACT 8:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 8:3" />Ko Haora ia, tā­horoa ana e ia te hāhi, tomo ana ki tēnā whare, ki tēnā whare, tōia atu ana ngā tāne me ngā wāhine, hoatu ana ki roto ki te whare here­here.<verse eid="ACT 8:3" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Kauwhautia te Rongopai ki Hamaria</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 8:4" />Nō reira ko rātou tonu, ko ngā mea i whaka­marara­tia rā, i hāere­ere ki te kauwhau i te kupu. <verse eid="ACT 8:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 8:5" />Nā, ko Piripi i heke atu ki te pā o Hamaria, ā, kauwhau ana i a te Karaiti ki a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 8:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 8:6" />Ā, kotahi tonu te whaka­aro o ngā mano ki te whaka­rongo ki ngā mea i kōrero ai a Piripi, i a rātou e rongo ana, e kite ana i ngā tohu i mea ai ia. <verse eid="ACT 8:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 8:7" />I puta mai hoki ngā wairua poke i roto i te tini o ngā mea e nohoia ana, he nui te reo ki te karanga. He toko­maha anō ngā pararūtiki, ngā kopa i whaka­ora­ngia. <verse eid="ACT 8:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 8:8" />Ā, nui atu te hari o taua pā.<verse eid="ACT 8:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 8:9" />Nā, i reira tētahi tangata, ko Haimona te ingoa, he mahi mākutu tāna i mua atu i roto i taua pā, ā, mīharo ana te iwi o Hamaria, i mea hoki ia i a ia he tangata nui. <verse eid="ACT 8:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 8:10" />I whaka­rongo katoa hoki rātou ki a ia te iti me te rahi, i mea, “Ko taua kaha o te Atua tēnei tangata, e kīa nei ko te Nui.” <verse eid="ACT 8:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 8:11" />Ā, i whaka­rongo rātou ki a ia, nō te mea kua roa kē rātou e mīharo ana ki āna mahi mākutu. <verse eid="ACT 8:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 8:12" />Ā, nō rātou ka whaka­pono ki a Piripi; e kauwhau ana i te rongo­pai o te ranga­tira­tanga o te Atua, i te ingoa hoki o Īhu Karaiti, ka iri­iria rātou, ngā tāne me ngā wāhine. <verse eid="ACT 8:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 8:13" />Ko Haimona tonu tētahi i whaka­pono. Ā, ka iri­iria ka piri tahi ki a Piripi; ā, nō tōna kite­nga i ngā tohu me ngā mere­kara nunui i mahia, ka mīharo.<verse eid="ACT 8:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 8:14" />Ā, i te rongo­nga o ngā āpō­toro i Hiruhārama kua tango a Hamaria i te kupu a te Atua, ka tonoa atu e rātou a Pita rāua ko Hoani ki a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 8:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 8:15" />Nō tō rāua taenga iho, ka īnoi mō rātou, kia riro te Wairua Tapu i a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 8:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 8:16" />Kāhore anō hoki ia i tau noa ki tētahi o rātou; he mea iri­iri kau i runga i te ingoa o te Ariki, o Īhu. <verse eid="ACT 8:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 8:17" />Me i reira ka whaka­pā­kia iho ō rātou ringa ki a rātou, ā, ka riro mai te Wairua Tapu i a rātou.<verse eid="ACT 8:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 8:18" />Ā, nō te kite­nga o Haimona, nā te whaka­pā­nga iho o ngā ringa o ngā āpō­toro i hōmai ai te Wairua Tapu, ka mea ki te hoatu moni ki a rāua, <verse eid="ACT 8:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 8:19" />ka kī, “Hōmai hoki ki ahau tēnei mana, kia riro ai te Wairua Tapu i te tangata e whaka­pā­kia iho ai e ahau ōku ringa.”<verse eid="ACT 8:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 8:20" />Nā, ko te mea­tanga a Pita ki a ia, “Kia pirau ngā­tahi kōrua ko tāu moni, ina koe ka whaka­aro mā te moni ka whi­whi ai ki te mea hōmai noa a te Atua! <verse eid="ACT 8:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 8:21" />Kāhore he wāhi māu, kāhore he taunga mōu i tēnei mea; kāhore hoki i tika tōu ngākau i te aro­aro o te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 8:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 8:22" />Nā, rīpenetā­tia tēnei kino ōu, ā, īnoi ki te Atua, me kore noa e murua te whaka­aro o tōu ngākau. <verse eid="ACT 8:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 8:23" />Kua kite hoki ahau i a koe, kei roto koe i te au kawa, kei te here o te kino.”<verse eid="ACT 8:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 8:24" />Nā, ka whaka­hoki a Haimona, ka mea, “Mā kōrua e īnoi mōku ki te Ariki, kei pā ki ahau tētahi o ngā mea kua kōrero­tia mai nā e kōrua.”<verse eid="ACT 8:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 8:25" />Ā, ka mutu tā rāua whaka­atu, tā rāua kauwhau i te kupu a te Ariki, ka hoki ki Hiruhārama, he maha hoki ngā kāinga o ngā Hamari i kauwhau­tia ai e rāua te rongo­pai.<verse eid="ACT 8:25" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ko Piripi rāua ko te Āpiha Etiopiana</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 8:26" />Nā, ka kōrero tētahi ana­hera a te Ariki ki a Piripi, ka mea, “Whaka­tika, haere ki te tonga, ki te ara e heke atu ana i Hiruhārama ki Kaha”; he koraha tērā. <verse eid="ACT 8:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 8:27" />Whaka­tika ana ia, haere ana. Nā, ko tētahi tangata o Etiopia, he ūnaka, he tangata nui nā Kanarahi, kuīni o ngā Etiopiana, ko te kai­tiaki ia o āna taonga katoa, i haere ki Hiruhārama ki te kara­kia; <verse eid="ACT 8:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 8:28" />ā, e hoki mai ana, e noho ana i runga i tōna hāri­ata, e kōrero ana i a Ihāia poro­piti. <verse eid="ACT 8:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 8:29" />Nā, ka mea te Wairua ki a Piripi, “Whaka­tata atu, ka haere atu koe ki te hāri­ata rā.” <verse eid="ACT 8:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 8:30" />Kātahi a Piripi ka oma atu ki a ia, ka rongo i a ia e kōrero ana i a Ihāia poro­piti, ka mea atu, “E mātau ana rānei koe ki tāu e kōrero nā?”<verse eid="ACT 8:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 8:31" />Anō rā ko ia, “Me pēhea koia, ki te kore tētahi hei ara­taki i ahau?” Nā, ka mea ia ki a Piripi kia eke ki runga kia noho tahi me ia. <verse eid="ACT 8:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 8:32" />Nā, ko te wāhi o te karaipi­ture e kōrero nei ia, ko tēnei,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 8:32">“I āra­hina ia ānō he hipi kia patua;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:32">ā, me te reme e wa­hangū ana i te aro­aro o tōna kai­kuti­kuti,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:32">kīhai i kuihi tōna waha.<verse eid="ACT 8:32" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 8:33" />I tōna whaka­iti­nga i whaka­korea he whaka­wā mōna.</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:33">Mā wai hoki tōna whaka­tupu­ranga e kōrero?</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:33">Kua tango­hia atu nei tōna ora i te whenua.”<verse eid="ACT 8:33" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 8:34" />Nā, ka whaka­hoki te ūnaka ki a Piripi, ka mea, “Tēnā koa, mō wai tēnei kōrero a te poro­piti? Mōna ake anō, mō tētahi atu rānei?” <verse eid="ACT 8:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 8:35" />Nā, ka puaki te māngai o Piripi, ā, tīmata mai i taua karaipi­ture, kauwhau­tia ana e ia a Īhu ki a ia. <verse eid="ACT 8:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 8:36" />Ā, i a rāua e haere ana i te ara, ka tae atu rāua ki tētahi wai, ka mea te ūnaka, “Nā, he wai tēnei! He aha te mea e kore ai ahau e iri­iria?” <verse eid="ACT 8:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 8:37" />Mea atu ana a Piripi, “Ki te whaka­pono tōu ngākau katoa, e āhei anō koe.” Nā, ka whaka­hoki ia, ka mea, “E whaka­pono ana ahau ko Īhu Karaiti te Tama a te Atua.”<verse eid="ACT 8:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 8:38" />Kātahi ia ka whaka­hau i te hāri­ata kia tū; ka haere atu rāua toko­rua ki roto i te wai, a Piripi rāua ko te ūnaka; ā, iri­iria ana ia e ia. <verse eid="ACT 8:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 8:39" />Ā, i tō rāua pu­tanga ake i te wai, kā­hakina atu ana a Piripi e te Wairua o te Ariki; ā, mutu tonu te kite­nga atu o te ūnaka i a ia, heoi, haere hari atu ana ia i tōna ara. <verse eid="ACT 8:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 8:40" />Ko Piripi ia i kitea ki Ahota; ā, i a ia e haere ana, kauwhau­tia ana e ia te rongo­pai ki ngā pā katoa, ā tae noa ia ki Hiha­ria.<verse eid="ACT 8:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 8" />
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="ACT 9" />
  <para style="s1">Te Huringa o Haora ki te Whakapono</para>
  <para style="r">(<ref loc="ACT 22:6-16">Ngā Mahi 22.6-16</ref>; <ref loc="ACT 26:12-18">26.12-18</ref>)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 9:1" />Ko Haora ia kei te kupu­kupu tonu i te whaka­wehi, i te mate mō ngā ākonga a te Ariki, ā, haere ana ki te tohu­nga nui, <verse eid="ACT 9:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 9:2" />kei te tono puka­puka i a ia ki ngā whaka­mine­nga i Ramahiku, ina kitea e ia tētahi nō te Huarahi, ahakoa tāne, wāhine rānei, kia mauria here­here­tia mai e ia ki Hiruhārama.<verse eid="ACT 9:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 9:3" />Nā, i a ia e haere ana, ka whaka­tata ia ki Ramahiku; nā, oho­rere ana te whiti­nga mai ki a ia, huri noa, o tētahi mārama nō te rangi. <verse eid="ACT 9:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 9:4" />Ā, hinga ana ia ki te whenua, ka rongo ake i tētahi reo e mea ana ki a ia, “E Hāora, e Haora, he aha tāu e whaka­toi nei i ahau?”<verse eid="ACT 9:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 9:5" />Anō rā ko ia, “Ko wai koe, e te Ariki?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 9:5">Ka mea ia, “Ko Īhu ahau, e whaka­toia nei e koe; ehara tāu, te whana ki ngā koi­koi.” <verse eid="ACT 9:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 9:6" />Nā, wiri ana ia, ihi­ihi ana, ka mea, “E te Ariki, kia aha ahau?” Anō rā ko te Ariki ki a ia, “Whaka­tika, tomo atu ki te pā, ā, ka kōrero­tia ki a koe tāu e mea ai.”<verse eid="ACT 9:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 9:7" />Nā, ko ngā tāngata i haere tahi i a ia, tū reo­kore ana, rongo kau ana ki te reo, kāhore ia i kite tangata. <verse eid="ACT 9:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 9:8" />Nā, ka whaka­tika ake a Haora i te whenua, ā, i te tu­whera­tanga o ōna kanohi, kīhai rawa ia i kite aha; nā, āra­hina ā ringa­tia ana ia e rātou, mauria ana ia ki Ramahiku. <verse eid="ACT 9:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 9:9" />Ā, e toru ōna rā e kore ana e kite, kīhai hoki i kai, kīhai i inu.<verse eid="ACT 9:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 9:10" />Nā, i Ramahiku tētahi ākonga, ko Anania te ingoa; ka mea te Ariki ki a ia, he kite, “E Anania.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 9:10">Ka mea tērā, “Tēnei ahau, e te Ariki.”<verse eid="ACT 9:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 9:11" />Anō rā ko te Ariki ki a ia, “Whaka­tika, haere ki te ara e kīa nei ko Torotika, ka ui i te whare o Hūrā mō tētahi ko Haora te ingoa, nō Tarahu. Nā, kei te īnoi ia. <verse eid="ACT 9:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 9:12" />Ā, kua kite ia i tētahi tangata, ko Anania te ingoa, e tomo mai ana, e whaka­pā ana i ōna ringa ki a ia, kia kite ai ia.”<verse eid="ACT 9:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 9:13" />Otirā, ka whaka­hoki a Anania, “E te Ariki, he toko­maha āku i rongo ai mō tēnei tangata, ki te nui o te kino i mea ai ia ki tāu hunga tapu i Hiruhārama; <verse eid="ACT 9:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 9:14" />ā, tēnei anō kei a ia he mana nā ngā tohu­nga nui, kia herea te hunga katoa e karanga ana ki tōu ingoa.”<verse eid="ACT 9:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 9:15" />Heoi, ka mea te Ariki ki a ia, “Haere; nō te mea he kaupapa whiri­whiri ia nāku, hei mau i tōku ingoa ki te aro­aro o ngā tauiwi, o ngā kīngi, o ngā tama hoki a Īharaira. <verse eid="ACT 9:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 9:16" />Ka whaka­kitea hoki e ahau ki a ia te nui o ngā mea e mamae ai ia mō tōku ingoa.”<verse eid="ACT 9:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 9:17" />Nā, haere ana a Anania, tomo ana ki roto ki te whare. Ka whaka­pā i ōna ringa ki a ia, ka mea, “E tōku teina, e Haora, nā te Ariki, nā Īhu, i puta rā ki a koe i te ara i haere mai nā koe, nāna ahau i tono mai, kia kite ai koe, ā, kia kī ai hoki i te Wairua Tapu.” <verse eid="ACT 9:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 9:18" />Nā, marere tonu iho ētahi mea, ānō he unahi, i ōna kanohi, ā, kite ana ia, ka whaka­tika, ka iri­iria. <verse eid="ACT 9:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 9:19" />Nā, ka kai ia, ka whai kaha.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="ACT 9:19">Ka Kauwhau a Haora i Ramahiku</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 9:19">Nā, noho ana a Haora ki ngā ākonga i Ramahiku mō ētahi rā. <verse eid="ACT 9:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 9:20" />Ā, i reira tonu kauwhau­tia ana e ia a te Karaiti i roto i ngā whare kara­kia, ko te Tama ia a te Atua.<verse eid="ACT 9:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 9:21" />Ā, mīharo ana te hunga katoa i rongo, ka mea, “Ehara ianei tēnei i te kai­tūkino o te hunga i karanga ki tēnei ingoa i Hiruhārama? Ā, ko te mea anō tēnei i haere mai ai ia, kia herea rātou, kia āra­hina ki ngā tohu­nga nui?”<verse eid="ACT 9:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 9:22" />Ko Haora ia ka nui haere kē atu tōna kaha, ā, whaka­poro­raru­tia ana e ia ngā Hūrai e noho ana i Ramahiku, i a ia e whaka­kite ana ko te Karaiti tēnei.<verse eid="ACT 9:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 9:23" />Ā, ka maha ngā rā ka pahure, ka rū­nanga ngā Hūrai kia whaka­matea ia. <verse eid="ACT 9:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 9:24" />Heoi, i mātau a Haora ki tā rātou whaka­papa­nga mōna. Ā, whanga ana rātou ki ngā tatau i te ao, i te pō, kia whaka­matea ia; <verse eid="ACT 9:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 9:25" />otiia, i mau ngā ākonga ki a ia i te pō, tukua iho ana e rātou rā te taiepa i roto i te kete.<verse eid="ACT 9:25" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ko Haora kei Hiruhārama</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 9:26" />Ā, nō tōna taenga mai ki Hiruhārama, ka whai ia kia uru atu ia ki ngā ākonga; heoi, wehi katoa ana rātou i a ia, kīhai i whaka­pono he ākonga ia. <verse eid="ACT 9:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 9:27" />Ko Pānapa ia i tango i a ia, ā, mauria ana ia ki ngā āpō­toro, kōrero­tia ana e ia ki a rātou tōna kite­nga i te Ariki i te ara, tāna kōrero­tanga ki a ia, tōna māia hoki ki te kauwhau i Ramahiku i runga i te ingoa o Īhu. <verse eid="ACT 9:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 9:28" />Nā, ka noho ia ki a rātou, hāere­ere atu ana, hāere­ere mai ana i Hiruhārama. <verse eid="ACT 9:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 9:29" />Me te māia hoki ki te kauwhau i runga i te ingoa o te Ariki; ā, kōrero ana ia, totohe ana ki ngā Hūrai Kariki. Otirā ka whaka­ngākau rātou kia whaka­matea ia. <verse eid="ACT 9:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 9:30" />Nō te mōhio­tanga o ngā tuā­kana, ka mauria ia e rātou ki raro ki Hiha­ria, ā, tonoa atu ana ia ki Tarahu.<verse eid="ACT 9:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 9:31" />Nā, ka whai tānga manawa te hāhi, puta noa i Hūria katoa, i Kariri, i Hamaria, ā tupu ana; haere ana i runga i te wehi o te Ariki, i te whaka­mārie hoki a te Wairua Tapu, nō ka whaka­roaka.<verse eid="ACT 9:31" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ko Pita kei Raira kei Hopa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 9:32" />Nā, i a Pita e hāere­ere ana puta noa ngā wāhi katoa, ka tae iho hoki ia ki te hunga tapu e noho ana i Raira. <verse eid="ACT 9:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 9:33" />Ka kitea e ia i reira tētahi tangata ko Inia te ingoa, kua waru ōna tau e takoto ana i runga i tōna moenga; he pararūtiki hoki ia. <verse eid="ACT 9:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 9:34" />Nā, ko te mea­tanga a Pita ki a ia, “E Inia, ka ora koe i a Īhu Karaiti; whaka­tika, whā­riki­tia tōu moenga.” Nā, whaka­tika tonu ake ia. <verse eid="ACT 9:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 9:35" />I kite katoa hoki i a ia te hunga e noho ana i Raira, i Harona, ā, tahuri ana ki te Ariki.<verse eid="ACT 9:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 9:36" />Nā, tērā tētahi ākonga i Hopa e noho ana, ko Tapita te ingoa, ko te whaka­māori­tanga ko Roka. He wahine tēnei i aro nui ki ngā mahi pai, ki ngā mahi ata­whai rawa­kore. <verse eid="ACT 9:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 9:37" />Ā, i aua rā ka tū­roro­tia ia, ka mate. Ā, ka oti ia te horoi e rātou, ka whaka­takoto­ria ia ki tētahi rūma i runga. <verse eid="ACT 9:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 9:38" />Nā, i te mea e tata atu ana a Raira ki Hopa, ka rongo ngā ākonga kei reira a Pita, ā, ka tonoa e rātou toko­rua ngā tāngata ki a ia, hei mea, “Kaua e whaka­roa te haere mai ki a mātou.” <verse eid="ACT 9:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 9:39" />Nā, whaka­tika ana a Pita, haere ana i a rāua. Ā, i tōna taenga atu ka āra­hina e rātou ki te rūma i runga. Ā, tū ana ngā pouaru katoa i tōna taha, tangi ana, ka whaka­kite ki a ia i ngā koti, i ngā kākahu i hangā e Roka, i a ia e noho ana i a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 9:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 9:40" />Otiia, ka tonoa rātou katoa e Pita ki waho, ka tuku ia i ōna turi, ka īnoi; kātahi ka tahuri ake ia ki te tū­pā­paku, ka mea, “Tapita, e ara.” Nā, ka ti­tiro ōna kanohi, ā, i tōna kite­nga i a Pita, ka noho ia ki runga. <verse eid="ACT 9:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 9:41" />Kātahi, ka hoatu e ia tōna ringa ki a ia, ka whaka­ara ake i a ia. Ā, karanga­tia ana e ia te hunga tapu me ngā pouaru, ā, tukua oratia atu ana ia. <verse eid="ACT 9:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 9:42" />Ā, i mōhio­tia tēnei mea puta noa i Hopa katoa; he toko­maha hoki i whaka­pono ki te Ariki. <verse eid="ACT 9:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 9:43" />Ā, he maha ōna rā i noho ai ia ki Hopa, ki a Haimona kai­mahi hiako.<verse eid="ACT 9:43" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 9" />
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="ACT 10" />
  <para style="s1">Ko Pita rāua ko Koroniria</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 10:1" />Nā, i Hiha­ria tētahi tangata, ko Koroniria te ingoa, he kene­turio nō te pū i kīa nei ko tō Itari. <verse eid="ACT 10:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 10:2" />He tangata kara­kia ia, e wehi ana i te Atua, rātou ko tōna whare katoa, he maha āna mahi ata­whai ki te iwi, me te īnoi tonu ki te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 10:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 10:3" />I kite nui ia, he whaka­rehu, i te mea ka tata ki te iwa o ngā hāora o te rā, i tētahi ana­hera a te Atua, e haere mai ana ki a ia, e mea ana hoki ki a ia, “E Koroniria!”<verse eid="ACT 10:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 10:4" />Nā, ka ti­tiro mata­tau atu ia ki a ia, ka wehi, ka mea, “He aha, e te Ariki?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 10:4">Ka kī tērā ki a ia, “Kua puta ake āu īnoi me āu mahi ata­whai, hei whaka­mahara ki te aro­aro o te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 10:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 10:5" />Nā, tonoa āia­nei he tangata ki Hopa, ki te tiki i a Haimona, ko te rua nei o ōna ingoa ko Pita. <verse eid="ACT 10:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 10:6" />He manu­hiri ia nā Haimona kai­mahi hiako, i te taha nei o te moana tōna whare.” <verse eid="ACT 10:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 10:7" />Ā, nō te riro­nga atu o te ana­hera i kōrero nei ki a ia, ka karanga­tia e ia toko­rua o āna pono­nga tāne, me tētahi hōia kara­kia nō te hunga e mahi tonu ana ki a ia; <verse eid="ACT 10:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 10:8" />ā, ka oti ngā mea katoa te kōrero ki a rātou, ka tonoa rātou e ia ki Hopa.<verse eid="ACT 10:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 10:9" />Nā i te aonga ake, i a rātou e haere ana, e whaka­tata atu ana ki te pā, ka kake a Pita ki runga ki te tuanui, i te ono o ngā hāora, ki te īnoi. <verse eid="ACT 10:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 10:10" />Nā ka pā ki a ia te matekai, ka mea ki te kai; otirā, i a rātou e taka mai ana, ka tau iho te wairua mata­kite ki a ia. <verse eid="ACT 10:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 10:11" />Nā, ka kite ia i te rangi kua tu­whera, me tētahi mea e heke iho ana, he mea tuku iho mā ngā pito e whā, ki te whenua. <verse eid="ACT 10:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 10:12" />I roto i taua mea ngā momo kararehe wae­wae whā katoa, ngā mea ngōki­ngōki katoa o te whenua, me ngā manu o te rangi. <verse eid="ACT 10:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 10:13" />I reira, ka puta mai he reo ki a ia, “Whaka­tika, e Pita; patua, kainga.”<verse eid="ACT 10:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 10:14" />Ko Pita ia i mea, “Kāhore, e te Ariki; kīanō ahau i kai i te mea noa, i te mea poke rānei.”<verse eid="ACT 10:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 10:15" />Ka puta mai anō he reo ki a ia, ka tua­rua­tia, “Ko ā te Atua i mea ai kia mā, kaua e whaka­noa­tia e koe.” <verse eid="ACT 10:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 10:16" />E toru mea­tanga o tēnei, ā, i reira tonu ka tango­hia atu taua mea ki te rangi.<verse eid="ACT 10:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 10:17" />I taua wā tonu, i a Pita e whaka­aro­aro ana i roto i a ia ki te tikanga o tēnei whaka­kite­nga, nā, ko ngā tāngata i tonoa mai rā e Koroniria, tērā kua uiui ki te whare o Haimona, tū ana i mua i te kūwaha. <verse eid="ACT 10:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 10:18" />Karanga ana mai, ui ana, kei reira rānei e noho ana a Pita, te rua nei o ōna ingoa ko Haimona.<verse eid="ACT 10:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 10:19" />Ā, i a Pita e whaka­aro ana mō taua whaka­kite­nga, ka mea te Wairua ki a ia, “Nana, toko­toru ēnei tāngata e rapu ana i a koe. <verse eid="ACT 10:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 10:20" />Nā, whaka­tika, heke atu, haere tahi koutou, kei rua­rua; nāku hoki rātou i tono mai.” <verse eid="ACT 10:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 10:21" />Nā, ka heke atu a Pita ki aua tāngata, ka mea, “Nā, ko ahau tēnei e rapu nei koutou. He aha te take o tā koutou haere mai?”<verse eid="ACT 10:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 10:22" />Nā, ka mea rātou, “Ko Koroniria rā, he kene­turio, he tangata tika, e wehi ana i te Atua, e kōrero­tia paitia ana e te iwi katoa o ngā Hūrai, kua whaka­mahara­tia ia e te Atua nā tētahi ana­hera tapu kia tīkina atu koe ki tōna whare, kia rongo ia ki ētahi kupu i a koe.” <verse eid="ACT 10:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 10:23" />Nā, karanga ana ia i a rātou ki roto hei manu­hiri māna.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 10:23">Ā, i te aonga ake, ka whaka­tika ia ka haere atu me rātou, ā, ko ētahi o ngā tēina nō Hopa i haere tahi me ia. <verse eid="ACT 10:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 10:24" />Ā, ao ake ka tomo rātou ki Hiha­ria. Nā, ko Koroniria e tatari mai ana ki a rātou, he mea karanga nāna kia hui­hui mai ōna whanau­nga me ōna hoa tupu. <verse eid="ACT 10:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 10:25" />Ā, nō ka tomo atu a Pita, ka tūtaki a Koroniria ki a ia, ka hinga ki ōna wae­wae, ka koro­piko ki a ia. <verse eid="ACT 10:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 10:26" />Otirā, ka whaka­ara ake a Pita i a ia, ka mea, “E tū ki runga; he tangata nei anō ahau.” <verse eid="ACT 10:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 10:27" />Nā, i a ia e kōrero ana ki a ia, ka tomo atu ia ki roto, ka kite i te mene­nga toko­maha, <verse eid="ACT 10:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 10:28" />ka mea atu ki a rātou, “E mātau ana koutou e kore e tika kia hui­hui te tangata o ngā Hūrai, kia haere atu rānei ki te tangata iwi kē; otiia, kua whaka­kitea e te Atua ki ahau kia kaua e kīa tētahi tangata he noa, he poke. <verse eid="ACT 10:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 10:29" />Koia ahau i haere mai ai, kīhai i aha i te tiki­nga ake i ahau. Nā, ka ui nei ahau, he aha te take i tīkina ake ai ahau?”<verse eid="ACT 10:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 10:30" />Ka mea a Koroniria, “Ka whā ngā rā ināia­nei tae mai ki tēnei hāora, e whaka­rite ana ahau i te īnoi­nga o te iwa o ngā hāora i roto i tōku whare; nā, ko te tangata e tū ana i tōku aro­aro, kanapa tonu te kākahu, <verse eid="ACT 10:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 10:31" />e mea ana, ‘E Koroniria, kua rangona tāu īnoi, ā, e mahara­tia ana āu mahi ata­whai i te aro­aro o te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 10:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 10:32" />Nā, tonoa he tangata ki Hopa, ka karanga ki a koe i a Haimona, te rua nei o ōna ingoa ko Pita; he manu­hiri ia i roto i te whare o Haimona kai­mahi hiako, i te taha moana.’ <verse eid="ACT 10:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 10:33" />I reira tonu ka tono tāngata atu ahau ki a koe. Nā, he pai rawa tōu haere­nga mai. Nō reira, kei konei katoa mātou kei te aro­aro o te Atua, whaka­rongo ai ki ngā mea katoa kua whaka­haua e te Ariki ki a koe.”<verse eid="ACT 10:33" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Whaikōrero a Pita</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 10:34" />Nā, ka puaki te māngai o Pita, ka mea: “He pono ka kite ahau kāhore a te Atua whaka­pai kanohi, <verse eid="ACT 10:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 10:35" />otiia, i roto i ngā tini iwi ko te tangata e wehi ana ki a ia, ā, e mahi ana i te tika, ka pai­ngia e ia. <verse eid="ACT 10:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 10:36" />Ko te kupu i tukua mai e ia ki ngā tama­riki a Īharaira, he kauwhau i te rongo­pai o te rangi­mārie nā Īhu Karaiti; ko ia nei te Ariki o te katoa. <verse eid="ACT 10:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 10:37" />Ko taua kupu, kei te mōhio koutou, i kauwhau­tia rā puta noa i Hūria katoa, i tīmata mai i Kariri, i muri o te iri­iri i kauwhau­tia e Hoani; <verse eid="ACT 10:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 10:38" />arā, ko Īhu o Nahareta, tā te Atua whaka­wahinga i a ia ki te Wairua Tapu, ki te kaha; ā, hāere­ere ana ia ki te mahi i te pai, ki te whaka­ora i te hunga katoa i pēhia e te rēwera; nō te mea i a ia te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 10:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 10:39" />Ko mātou hoki ngā kai­whaka­atu o ngā mea katoa i mea ai ia ki te whenua o ngā Hūrai, ki Hiruhārama hoki. Ā, whaka­matea ana ia e rātou, he mea whaka­iri ki runga ki te rākau. <verse eid="ACT 10:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 10:40" />Nā, ko ia i whaka­ara­hia ake e te Atua i te toru o ngā rā, ā, meinga ana ia kia kitea nuitia, <verse eid="ACT 10:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 10:41" />ehara i te mea e te iwi katoa, engari e te hunga i whiri­whiria i mua e te Atua, arā e mātou, i kai tahi nei, i inu tahi nei me ia, i muri i tōna aranga ake i te hunga mate. <verse eid="ACT 10:41" /><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 10:42" />I whai kupu hoki ia ki a mātou kia kauwhau ki te iwi, kia whaka­atu, ko ia tā te Atua i whaka­rite ai hei Kai­whaka­wā mō ngā tāngata ora, mō ngā tāngata mate. <verse eid="ACT 10:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 10:43" />He kai­whaka­atu ngā poro­piti katoa mōna, arā mā tōna ingoa ka whi­whi ai ki te muru­nga hara ngā tāngata katoa e whaka­rongo, ana ki a ia.”<verse eid="ACT 10:43" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Whiwhinga o ngā Tauiwi ki te Wairua Tapu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 10:44" />I a Pita anō e kōrero ana i ēnei kupu, ka tau iho te Wairua Tapu ki te hunga katoa e whaka­rongo ana ki te kupu. <verse eid="ACT 10:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 10:45" />Ā, ko te hunga o te kotinga i whaka­pono nei, ko ngā mea i haere tahi mai me Pita, mīharo ana nō te mea kua ringi­hia tahi­tia iho te Wairua Tapu ki ngā tauiwi. <verse eid="ACT 10:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 10:46" />I rongo hoki rātou ki ngā reo i kōrero ai rātou, i whaka­nui ai i te Atua. I reira ka whaka­hoki a Pita, <verse eid="ACT 10:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 10:47" />“E āhei rānei te whaka­kāhore e tētahi te wai, kei iri­iria ēnei kua whi­whi tahi nei me tātou ki te Wairua Tapu?” <verse eid="ACT 10:47" /><verse number="48" style="v" sid="ACT 10:48" />Nā, ka whaka­hau ia kia iri­iria rātou i runga i te ingoa o Īhu Karaiti. I reira ka tohe rātou ki a ia kia noho mō ētahi rā.<verse eid="ACT 10:48" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 10" />
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="ACT 11" />
  <para style="s1">Te Kōrero Whakatepe a Pita ki te Hāhi i Hiruhārama</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 11:1" />Ā, ka rongo ngā āpō­toro me ngā tuā­kana i Hūria, kua tango hoki ngā tauiwi i te kupu a te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 11:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 11:2" />Ā, nō te taenga ake o Pita ki Hiruhārama, ka whaka­wā­kia ia e te hunga o te kotinga, <verse eid="ACT 11:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 11:3" />i mea rātou, “I haere koe ki roto ki ngā tāngata kīhai i kotia, i kai tahi me rātou!” <verse eid="ACT 11:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 11:4" />Nā, ka tīmata a Pita, ka kōrero whaka­tepe atu ki a rātou, ka mea:<verse eid="ACT 11:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 11:5" />“I te pā ahau, i Hopa, e īnoi ana; ā, ka kite moe­moeā ahau i tētahi whaka­kite­nga, ko tētahi mea e heke iho ana, ānō he kākahu nui, he mea tuku iho i te rangi mā ngā pito e whā; ā, tae tonu mai ki ahau. <verse eid="ACT 11:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 11:6" />Nō te whaka­mau­nga atu o ōku kanohi ki taua mea, ka whaka­aro ahau, ā, ka kite i ngā kararehe wae­wae whā o te whenua, i ngā kararehe mohoao me ngā mea ngōki­ngōki me ngā manu o te rangi. <verse eid="ACT 11:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 11:7" />Ā, ka rongo hoki ahau he reo e mea mai ana ki ahau, ‘E ara, e Pita; patua, kainga.’ <verse eid="ACT 11:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 11:8" />Otirā, ka kī atu ahau, ‘Kāhore, e te Ariki; kīanō hoki tētahi mea noa, poke rānei, i tapoko noa ki tōku māngai.’ <verse eid="ACT 11:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 11:9" />Nā, ka whaka­hoki tuarua mai he reo nō te rangi, ‘Ko ā te Atua i mea ai kia mā, kaua e meinga e koe kia noa.’ <verse eid="ACT 11:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 11:10" />E toru ngā mea­tanga o tēnei; ka hūtia katoa­tia atu anō ki te rangi. <verse eid="ACT 11:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 11:11" />Nā, i taua wā anō kua tū ngā tāngata toko­toru ki mua i te whare i noho ai ahau, he mea tono mai nō Hiha­ria ki ahau. <verse eid="ACT 11:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 11:12" />Nā, ka mea te Wairua ki ahau kia haere tahi mātou, kia kaua ahau e rua­rua. I haere tahi anō i ahau ēnei tēina toko­ono, ā, tomo ana mātou ki te whare o taua tangata. <verse eid="ACT 11:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 11:13" />Nā, ka kōrero­tia mai e ia ki a mātou tōna kite­nga i te ana­hera i tōna whare e tū ana, e mea ana ki a ia, ‘Tonoa ētahi tāngata ki Hopa, tīkina a Haimona, te rua nei o ōna ingoa ko Pita. <verse eid="ACT 11:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 11:14" />Māna e kōrero ki a koe ētahi kupu, e ora ai koutou ko tōu whare katoa.’ <verse eid="ACT 11:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 11:15" />Ā, nōku ka tīmata ki te kōrero, ka tau iho te Wairua Tapu ki a rātou, ka pērā anō me ia ki a tātou i te tīma­tanga. <verse eid="ACT 11:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 11:16" />Kātahi ahau ka mahara ki te kupu a te Ariki, ki tāna i mea ai, ‘I iri­iri rā a Hoani ki te wai; ko koutou ia ka iri­iria ki te Wairua Tapu.’ <verse eid="ACT 11:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 11:17" />Nā, me­he­mea rite tonu tā te Atua mea i hoatu ai ki a rātou ki tāna i hōmai ai hoki ki a tātou, i a tātou i whaka­pono ai ki te Ariki, ki a Īhu Karaiti; ko wai ahau, kia āhei te tū atu ki te Atua?”<verse eid="ACT 11:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 11:18" />Ā, nō ka rongo rātou ki ēnei mea, mutu pū tā rātou kōrero, heoi, ka whaka­korōria i te Atua, ka mea, “Koia anō, kua hōmai hoki e te Atua ki ngā tauiwi te rīpe­netā e ora ai.”<verse eid="ACT 11:18" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Hāhi i Anatioka</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 11:19" />Nā, ko te iwi i whaka­marara­tia atu i runga i te tūkino­tanga i puta ake i tō Tepene, hāere­ere ana rātou ā tae noa ki Pini­kia, ki Kai­peru, ki Anatioka, me te kauwhau anō i te kupu ki ngā Hūrai anake, kāhore ki ētahi atu. <verse eid="ACT 11:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 11:20" />Otirā, ko ētahi o rātou, he tāngata nō Kai­peru, nō Hairini, i tō rātou taenga ki Anatioka, ka kōrero ki ngā Kariki hoki, ka kauwhau i te Ariki, i a Īhu. <verse eid="ACT 11:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 11:21" />Ko te ringa hoki o te Ariki i a rātou; ā, he toko­maha rawa i whaka­pono, i tahuri ki te Ariki.<verse eid="ACT 11:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 11:22" />Nā, ka tae tō rātou rongo ki ngā tari­nga o te hāhi i Hiruhārama, ā, ka tonoa e rātou a Pānapa kia haere ki Anatioka. <verse eid="ACT 11:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 11:23" />Nō tōna taenga atu, ka kite i te aroha noa o te Atua, ka hari, ka whaka­hau i a rātou katoa kia ū te ngākau, kia piri ki te Ariki. <verse eid="ACT 11:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 11:24" />He tangata pai hoki ia, kī tonu i te Wairua Tapu, i te whaka­pono. He nui anō te hunga i honoa ki te Ariki.<verse eid="ACT 11:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 11:25" />Me i reira ka haere atu a Pānapa ki Tarahu, ki te rapu i a Haora, <verse eid="ACT 11:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 11:26" />ā, nō ka kitea ia e ia, ka kawea mai ia e ia ki Anatioka. Ā, kotahi tino tau i hui­hui tahi ai rāua ki te hāhi, ā, he nui te hunga i whaka­akona. I mātua huaina hoki ngā ākonga he Karaiti­ana ki Anatioka.<verse eid="ACT 11:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 11:27" />Nā, i aua rā ka heke mai ētahi poro­piti i Hiruhārama ki Anatioka. <verse eid="ACT 11:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 11:28" />Ā, ka tū ake tētahi o rātou, ko Akapu te ingoa, ka whaka­kite, he mea nā te Wairua, tērā ka pā he mate nui i te hia­kai ki te whenua katoa; i puta anō tēnei i ngā rā o Karau­ria. <verse eid="ACT 11:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 11:29" />Nā, ka whaka­takoto tikanga ngā ākonga i runga i te mea e taea e tēnā, e tēnā, kia tukua atu he āwhina mō ngā tuā­kana e noho ana i Hūria. <verse eid="ACT 11:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 11:30" />Pērā ana hoki rātou, tukua atu ana ki ngā kaumātua mā te ringa o Pānapa rāua ko Haora.<verse eid="ACT 11:30" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 11" />
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="ACT 12" />
  <para style="s1">Te Whakatoinga Anō</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 12:1" />Nā, i taua wā, ka totoro atu ngā ringa o Kīngi Herora ki te tūkino i ētahi o te hāhi. <verse eid="ACT 12:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 12:2" />Ā, whaka­matea ana e ia ki te hoari a Hēmi, te tua­kana o Hoani. <verse eid="ACT 12:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 12:3" />Ā, nō tōna kite­nga e pai ana ki ngā Hūrai, ka anga ia ki te hopu hoki i a Pita. Nā, ko ngā rā ēnā o te Taro Rēwenakore. <verse eid="ACT 12:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 12:4" />Ā, nō ka mau ia, ka makā ki te whare here­here, ka tukua ki ngā hōia kotahi tekau mā ono kia tiaki­na; ko te whaka­aro mō muri iho i te Kape­nga ka whaka­puta mai ai i a ia ki te iwi. <verse eid="ACT 12:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 12:5" />Nā, ka puri­tia a Pita ki roto ki te whare here­here; otiia, kīhai i mutu­mutu te īnoi a te hāhi ki te Atua mōna.<verse eid="ACT 12:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Putanga mai o Pita i te Whare Herehere</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 12:6" />Ā, nō ka tata a Herora te whaka­puta mai i a ia, i taua pō anō e moe ana a Pita i waenga­nui o ngā hōia toko­rua, he mea here ki ngā meka­meka e rua; me ngā kai­tiaki i mua i te tatau e tiaki ana i te whare here­here. <verse eid="ACT 12:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 12:7" />Nā, tū ana tētahi ana­hera nā te Ariki i tōna taha, ā, tīaho ana te mārama i roto i te rūma. Nā, ka papaki ia i te kao­kao o Pita, ka whaka­ara i a ia, ka mea, “E ara, hohoro.” Ā, marere iho ōna meka­meka i ōna ringa. <verse eid="ACT 12:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 12:8" />Ka mea atu anō te ana­hera ki a ia, “Whī­tiki i a koe, ka here i ōu pā­reke­reke.” Ā, meinga ana e ia. Ka mea anō ki a ia, “Kākahu­ria tōu kākahu, haere mai i muri i ahau.” <verse eid="ACT 12:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 12:9" />Nā, ka haere ia ki waho, ka aru i a ia, ā, kīhai ia i mahara he pono tā te ana­hera i mea ai; hua noa he reka­nga kanohi tāna i kite ai. <verse eid="ACT 12:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 12:10" />Ā, nō ka mahue i a rāua te tua­tahi, te tuarua o ngā kai­tiaki, ka tae rāua ki te tatau rino i te pu­tanga atu ki te pā; tu­whera noa ana tērā ki a rāua. Puta ana rāua ki waho, haere ana, puta rawa i tētahi ara, mawehe tonu atu te ana­hera i a ia.<verse eid="ACT 12:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 12:11" />Ā, i te hoki­nga ake o ngā whaka­aro o Pita, ka mea ia, “Kātahi ahau ka tino mōhio, kua tono mai te Ariki i tāna ana­hera, hei tango i ahau i roto i te ringa o Herora, i ngā mea katoa hoki e tāria nei e te iwi o ngā Hūrai.”<verse eid="ACT 12:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 12:12" />Ā, nō ka whaka­aro­aro ia ki taua mea, ka haere ia ki te whare o Meri, whaea o Hoani, ko te rua nei o ōna ingoa ko Māka; he toko­maha hoki kua hui­hui ki reira ki te īnoi. <verse eid="ACT 12:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 12:13" />Ā, nō te pātōtō­tanga a Pita i te tatau o te whati­toka, ka tae mai he kōtiro ki te whaka­rongo, ko Rora te ingoa. <verse eid="ACT 12:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 12:14" />Ā, nō ka mōhio ia ki te reo o Pita, kīhai i uakina te tatau i te hari, heoi, oma ana ki roto, ki te kōrero kei te tatau a Pita e tū ana. <verse eid="ACT 12:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 12:15" />Nā, ka mea rātou ki a ia, “E hau­rangi ana koe!” Heoi, ka tohe tonu ia he pono. Nā, ka mea rātou, “Ko tōna ana­hera.”<verse eid="ACT 12:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 12:16" />Me te pātuki tonu anō tērā a Pita; ā, i tā rātou ua­kanga, ka kite i a ia, ka mīharo. <verse eid="ACT 12:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 12:17" />Nā, ka pēpehi atu tōna ringa i a rātou kia kaua e kuihi, ka kōrero­tia ki a rātou tōna whaka­puta­nga mai e te Ariki i te whare here­here. Ka mea, “Kōrero­tia ēnei mea ki a Hēmi rātou ko ngā tēina.” Nā, ka puta ia ki waho, haere ana he wāhi kē.<verse eid="ACT 12:17" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 12:18" />Nā, i te aonga ake anō o te rā, kīhai i iti te poro­raru o ngā hōia, i ahatia rānei a Pita. <verse eid="ACT 12:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 12:19" />Nā, ka rapu a Herora i a ia, ā, nō te kore­nga i kitea, ka whaka­wā i ngā kai­tiaki, ka whaka­hau kia whaka­matea.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 12:19">Nā, haere atu ana ia i Hūria ki raro ki Hiha­ria noho ai.<verse eid="ACT 12:19" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Matenga o Herora</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 12:20" />Nā, tino nui te riri o Herora ki te hunga o Tāira, o Hairona. Otirā, ka hui­hui mai rātou ki a ia, ā, ka oti a Parahitu, te kai­tiaki o te whare moenga o te kīngi, te whaka­kīkī e rātou, ka tono rātou kia houhia te rongo, nō te mea ko ngā kai i whāngaia ai tō rātou whenua nō te whenua o te kīngi.<verse eid="ACT 12:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 12:21" />Ā, i tētahi rā i whaka­ritea ka kākahu a Herora i te kākahu kīngi, ka noho ki runga ki te torōna, ā, whaka­tū ana ki a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 12:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 12:22" />Nā, ko te karanga­tanga a te hui­hui, “He reo atua, ehara i tō te tangata!” <verse eid="ACT 12:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 12:23" />I reira, pū anō ka patua ia e tētahi ana­hera a te Ariki, nō te mea kīhai i hoatu e ia te korōria ki te Atua, ā, kainga ana ia e te kutu­kutu, hemo ake.<verse eid="ACT 12:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 12:24" />Ko te kupu ia a te Atua i tupu, i nui haere.<verse eid="ACT 12:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 12:25" />Ā, ka hoki a Pānapa rāua ko Haora i Hiruhārama, i te otinga o tā rāua mahi, ka mauria a Hoani, ko te rua nei o ōna ingoa ko Māka.<verse eid="ACT 12:25" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 12" />
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="ACT 13" />
  <para style="s1">Ka Whiriwhiria, ka Tonoa ko Pānapa rāua ko Haora</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 13:1" />Nā, tērā ētahi poro­piti me ētahi kai­whaka­ako i Anatioka, i te hāhi i reira, ko Pānapa, ko Himiona i huaina nei ko Nikera, ko Rukiu nō Hairini, ko Manaena, he mea whaka­tupu ngā­tahi nei rāua ko Herora teta­raki, me Haora. <verse eid="ACT 13:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 13:2" />Ā, i a rātou e kara­kia ana ki te Ariki, e noho­puku ana, ka mea te Wairua Tapu, “Motu­hia mai ki ahau a Pānapa rāua ko Haora ki te mahi i karanga­tia ai rāua e ahau.”<verse eid="ACT 13:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 13:3" />Nā, ka mutu tā rātou noho­puku me te īnoi, ā, ka popoki iho i ō rātou ringa ki a rāua ka tonoa atu rāua kia haere.<verse eid="ACT 13:3" /></para>
  <para style="s1">I Kaiperu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 13:4" />Nā, ka tonoa nei rāua e te Wairua Tapu, ka haere ki Herukia; ā, rere atu ana i reira ki Kai­peru. <verse eid="ACT 13:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 13:5" />Nā, i a rāua i Harami, ka kauwhau­tia e rāua te kupu a te Atua i roto i ngā whare kara­kia o ngā Hūrai. I a rāua anō a Hoani hei kai­mahi.<verse eid="ACT 13:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 13:6" />Ā, nō tō rātou pu­tanga i te motu katoa ki Papaho, ka kitea tētahi tangata mākutu, he poro­piti teka, he Hūrai, ko Paraīhu te ingoa. <verse eid="ACT 13:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 13:7" />I te tino kāwana ia, i a Herekiu Paora; he tangata mahara a Herekiu. Ā, karanga­tia ana e ia a Pānapa rāua ko Haora, ā, ka whai kia rongo i te kupu a te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 13:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 13:8" />Otirā, i tau­tohe ki a rāua a Erima te kai­mākutu, ko te whaka­māori­tanga hoki tēnei o tōna ingoa, i mea kia tahuri kē te tino kāwana i te whaka­pono. <verse eid="ACT 13:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 13:9" />Otirā, ko Haora, e huaina nei anō ko Paora, kī tonu i te Wairua Tapu, i whaka­mau i ōna kanohi ki a ia, <verse eid="ACT 13:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 13:10" />ā, i mea, “E te tangata kī tonu i te tini­hanga, i ngā tini mahi poka­noa, e te tama a te rēwera, hoa­riri o ngā mahi tika katoa, e kore ianei e mutu tāu whaka­puta kē i ngā ara tika a te Ariki? <verse eid="ACT 13:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 13:11" />Nana, āia­nei pā ai te ringa o te Ariki ki a koe, ka matapō­tia koe, e kore e kite i te rā ā taka noa tētahi wā.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 13:11">Nā, taka tonu iho ki a ia he kohu, he pōuri; ā, hāere­ere noa ia ki te rapu kai­ārahi mōna. <verse eid="ACT 13:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 13:12" />Ā, nō te kite­nga o te tino kāwana i taua mea­tanga, ka whaka­pono ia, i mīharo hoki ki te ako a te Ariki.<verse eid="ACT 13:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">I Anitioka o Pihiria</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 13:13" />Nā, ka rere atu a Paora rātou ko ōna hoa i Papaho, ka ū ki Pereka i Pamapu­ria. Ā, whaka­rere ana a Hoani i a rāua, hoki ana ki Hiruhārama. <verse eid="ACT 13:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 13:14" />Ko rāua ia haere atu ana i Pereka, tae tonu atu ki Anatioka i Pihi­ria, ā, tomo ana ki te whare kara­kia i te rā hāpati, noho ana. <verse eid="ACT 13:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 13:15" />Ā, ka mutu te kōrero­tanga o te ture, o ngā poro­piti, ka tono tāngata ngā ranga­tira o te whare kara­kia ki a rāua, ka mea, “E hoa mā, ki te mea he kupu whaka­ako tā kōrua ki te hunga nei, kōrero­tia.”<verse eid="ACT 13:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 13:16" />Nā, ka tū a Paora ki runga, ka tā­whiri tōna ringa, ka mea:</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 13:16">“E ngā tāngata o Īharaira, e te hunga e wehi ana ki te Atua, whaka­rongo mai. <verse eid="ACT 13:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 13:17" />Nā, te Atua o tēnei iwi, o Īharaira i whiri­whiri ō tātou mātua, ā, whaka­nuia ana e ia tēnei iwi, i a rātou e noho manene ana i te whenua o Īhipa, i runga tonu anō te ringa i āra­hina mai ai rātou e ia i reira. <verse eid="ACT 13:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 13:18" />Nā, me te mea e whā tekau ngā tau i whaka­manawa­nui ai ki tō rātou āhua i te koraha. <verse eid="ACT 13:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 13:19" />Ā, ka whitu ngā iwi ka ngaro i a ia i te whenua o Kanaana, ka hoatu e ia ki a rātou tō rātou whenua hei whenua pūmau, mō ngā tau me te mea e whā rau e rima tekau.<verse eid="ACT 13:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 13:20" />“Ā muri iho i ēnei mea, ka hoatu e ia ki a rātou he kai­whaka­wā, taea noatia a Hamuera poro­piti. <verse eid="ACT 13:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 13:21" />Ā muri iho ka tono rātou ki tētahi kīngi; ā, hoatu ana e te Atua ki a rātou a Haora, tama a Kihi, he tangata nō te pū o Pineamine, ā, e whā tekau ngā tau. <verse eid="ACT 13:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 13:22" />Ā, ka oti ia te whaka­taka, ka whaka­ara­hia ake e ia a Rāwiri hei kīngi mō rātou; i whaka­atu­ria hoki ia e ia, i kōrero­tia, ‘Kua kitea e ahau a Rāwiri tama a Hehe, he tangata e whaka­ae­tia ana e tōku ngākau; ka meatia e ia ngā mea katoa e pai ai ahau.’ <verse eid="ACT 13:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 13:23" />He uri nō tēnei tangata tā te Atua i hōmai ai ki a Īharaira, he Kai­whaka­ora, ko Īhu, hei whaka­rite i te mea i kōrero­tia ai i mua. <verse eid="ACT 13:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 13:24" />Nō mua tata anō hoki i tōna haere­nga mai te kauwhau­tanga a Hoani i te iri­iri rīpe­netā, ki te iwi katoa o Īharaira. <verse eid="ACT 13:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 13:25" />Ā, ka tutuki a Hoani ki tōna tutuki­tanga, ka mea ia, ‘Ko wai koia ahau ki tō koutou whaka­aro? Ehara rā ahau i a ia. Engari, tērā te haere mai ana tētahi i muri i ahau, ko ōna hū e kore ahau e tau hei wewete.’<verse eid="ACT 13:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 13:26" />“E ōku tuā­kana, e ngā tama o te kāwei o Āperahama, e te hunga i roto i a koutou e wehi ana ki te Atua, kua hōmai te kupu o tēnei ora kia whaka­pua­kina ki a tātou. <verse eid="ACT 13:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 13:27" />Nā, ko te hunga e noho ana Hiruhārama, me ō rātou ranga­tira, i te mea kīhai rātou i mōhio ki a ia, ki ngā reo rānei o ngā poro­piti e kōrero­tia ana i ngā hāpati katoa, nā rātou i whaka­rite aua reo, i a rātou i tuku i a ia ki te mate. <verse eid="ACT 13:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 13:28" />Ahakoa kīhai i kitea e rātou he mea e mate ai ia, ka tohe rātou ki a Pirato kia whaka­matea ia. <verse eid="ACT 13:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 13:29" />Ā, nō ka rite i a rātou ngā mea katoa i tuhi­tuhia mōna, tango­hia iho ana ia i te rākau, whaka­takoto­ria ana ki roto ki te urupā. <verse eid="ACT 13:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 13:30" />Heoi, nā te Atua ia i whaka­ara ake i te hunga mate. <verse eid="ACT 13:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 13:31" />Ā, he maha ngā rā i kitea ai ia e te hunga i haere tahi i a ia i Kariri ki Hiruhārama, ko rātou nei ngā kai­whaka­atu mōna ki te iwi. <verse eid="ACT 13:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 13:32" />Nā, he kauwhau tēnei nā māua ki a koutou i te rongo­pai, i kōrero­tia i mua ki ngā mātua, <verse eid="ACT 13:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 13:33" />arā, kua mana tēnei i te Atua, hei mea mā ā tātou tama­riki, i a ia whaka­ara nei i a Īhu; ko te mea hoki tēnā i tuhi­tuhia i te rua o ngā waiata:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:33">‘Ko tāku Tama koe;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:33">nō nāia­nei koe whaka­tupu­ria ai e ahau.’<verse eid="ACT 13:33" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 13:34" />Ko tāna kōrero anō tēnei mōna whaka­ara­hia nei e ia i te hunga mate, tē hoki anō ki te pirau i muri iho:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:34">‘Ka hoatu e ahau ki a koutou ngā mea tapu,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:34">ngā manaaki­tanga pono o Rāwiri.’<verse eid="ACT 13:34" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 13:35" />Koia hoki ia i mea ai i tētahi atu waiata:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:35">‘E kore koe e tuku i tāu Mea Tapu kia kite i te pirau.’<verse eid="ACT 13:35" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 13:36" />Ko Rāwiri hoki i mahi i tā te Atua i pai ai i tōna whaka­tupu­ranga anō, ā, moe iho, whaka­takoto­ria ana ki ōna mātua, kite ana i te pirau. <verse eid="ACT 13:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 13:37" />Ko tēnei ia i whaka­ara­hia ake nei e te Atua, kīhai ia i kite i te pirau. <verse eid="ACT 13:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 13:38" />Nā, kia mōhio koutou, e ōku tuā­kana, nā tēnei tangata te muru­nga hara e kauwhau­tia nei ki a koutou. <verse eid="ACT 13:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 13:39" />Māna hoki ngā tāngata katoa e whaka­pono ana, ka whaka­tikaia ai i ngā mea katoa, e kore nei koutou e whaka­tikaia i runga i tā Mohi ture. <verse eid="ACT 13:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 13:40" />Nā, kia mahara, kei pā ki a koutou te mea i kōrero­tia rā e ngā poro­piti:<verse eid="ACT 13:40" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 13:41" />‘Ti­tiro mai, e te hunga whaka­hāwea,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:41">ka mīharo ai, ā, whaka­ngaro­mia iho!</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:41">Ka mahia hoki e ahau he mahi i ō koutou rā,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:41">he mahi e kore e whaka­pono­hia e koutou,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:41">ki te whaka­pua­kina e te tangata ki a koutou!’ ”<verse eid="ACT 13:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 13:42" />Nā, i a rātou e puta ana ki waho, ka tohe rātou kia kauwhau­tia anō aua kupu ki a rātou i tō muri iho hāpati. <verse eid="ACT 13:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 13:43" />Heoi, ka pākaru­karu te hui­hui, he toko­maha ngā Hūrai me ngā poro­hira­iti kara­kia i aru i a Paora rāua ko Pānapa, ā, ka kōrero rāua ki a rātou, ka ako kia mau tonu rātou ki te aroha noa o te Atua.<verse eid="ACT 13:43" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 13:44" />Nā, i tō muri iho hāpati ka hui­hui mai te pā, me te mea ko rātou katoa, ki te whaka­rongo ki te kupu a te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 13:44" /><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 13:45" />Nō te kite­nga ia o ngā Hūrai i te hui­hui, ka kī rātou i te hae, ka whaka­kāhore ki ngā mea i kōrero­tia e Paora, ka whaka­teka, ka kohu­kohu. <verse eid="ACT 13:45" /><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 13:46" />Kātahi a Paora rāua ko Pānapa ka kōrero māia atu, ka mea: “I takoto te tikanga kia mātua kōrero­tia te kupu a te Atua ki a koutou. Nā, ka peia nei e koutou, ka whaka­aro koutou e kore koutou e tau mō te ora tonu, nā, ka tahuri atu nei māua ki ngā tauiwi. <verse eid="ACT 13:46" /><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 13:47" />I pēnei hoki te ako a te Ariki ki a mātou:</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:47">‘Kua waiho koe e ahau hei mārama ki ngā tauiwi,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:47">kia ai koe hei oranga puta noa i ngā pito o te whenua.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 13:47" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" sid="ACT 13:48" />Nā, i te rongo­nga o ngā tauiwi, ka hari, ka whaka­korōria i te kupu a te Ariki; ka whaka­pono anō te hunga i rite mō te ora tonu.<verse eid="ACT 13:48" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" sid="ACT 13:49" />Ā, pakū ana te kupu a te Ariki puta noa i taua whenua. <verse eid="ACT 13:49" /><verse number="50" style="v" sid="ACT 13:50" />Otirā, i whaka­oho­kia e ngā Hūrai ngā wāhine kara­kia, ranga­tira, me ngā tāngata nunui o te pā, ā, ara ana i a rātou he whaka­toi mō Paora rāua ko Pānapa, peia ana rāua i ō rātou wāhi. <verse eid="ACT 13:50" /><verse number="51" style="v" sid="ACT 13:51" />Heoi, ruia atu ana e rāua te puehu o ō rāua wae­wae ki a rātou, ā, haere ana ki Ikoniuma. <verse eid="ACT 13:51" /><verse number="52" style="v" sid="ACT 13:52" />Nā, kī tonu ngā ākonga i te hari, i te Wairua Tapu.<verse eid="ACT 13:52" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 13" />
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="ACT 14" />
  <para style="s1">I Ikoniuma</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 14:1" />Ā, i Ikoniuma ka haere tahi rāua ki roto ki te whare kara­kia o ngā Hūrai, ā, ka kōrero, nō ka whaka­pono tōna tini o ngā Hūrai, o ngā Kariki. <verse eid="ACT 14:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 14:2" />Nā, ngā Hūrai whaka­teka ia i whaka­oho, i whaka­kino ngā ngākau o ngā tauiwi ki ngā tēina. <verse eid="ACT 14:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 14:3" />Nā, he nui te wā i noho ai rāua i reira, i māia ai te kōrero i ngā mea a te Ariki, nāna i whaka­ae te kupu o tōna aroha noa, me te hōmai anō e ia ngā tohu me ngā mea whaka­mīharo kia meatia e ō rāua ringa. <verse eid="ACT 14:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 14:4" />Otiia, i wehe­wehea ngā tāngata o te pā; ko ētahi i ū ki ngā Hūrai, ko ētahi ki ngā āpō­toro.<verse eid="ACT 14:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 14:5" />Ā, i ngā tauiwi rātou ko ngā Hūrai, ko ō rātou ranga­tira hoki e huaki ana ki te whaka­tupu kino, ki te āki i a rāua ki te kōhatu. <verse eid="ACT 14:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 14:6" />Ka tūpato rāua, ā, rere ana ki Raihitara, ki Rerepe, ki ngā pā o Raikaonia, ki pahaki tata atu anō hoki. <verse eid="ACT 14:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 14:7" />Ā, kauwhau­tia ana e rāua te rongo­pai ki reira.<verse eid="ACT 14:7" /></para>
  <para style="s1">I Raihitara me Rerepe</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 14:8" />I Raihitara hoki e noho ana tētahi tangata wae­wae ngoi­kore, he kopa nō te kōpū mai o tōna whaea, kāhore i haere i mua iho. <verse eid="ACT 14:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 14:9" />I rongo tēnei i a Paora e kōrero ana; ko te tiro­hanga pu­tanga atu o tērā ki a ia, ka kite he whaka­pono tōna e ora ai, <verse eid="ACT 14:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 14:10" />he nui noa atu tōna reo ki te karanga atu, “E tū ōu wae­wae ki runga.” Nā, moko­whiti ake ana ia, haere ana. <verse eid="ACT 14:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 14:11" />Nō te kite­nga o ngā tāngata i tā Paora i mea ai, ka ara tō rātou reo, ka mea i te reo o Raikaonia, “Kua heke iho ngā atua ki a tātou, nō ngā tāngata te āhua!” <verse eid="ACT 14:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 14:12" />Ā, huaina ana e rātou a Pānapa ko Hupita, a Paora ko Merekurai, nō te mea ko ia te pū kōrero. <verse eid="ACT 14:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 14:13" />Nā, ka kawea mai e te tohu­nga o Hupita, i te ngutu nei o te pā tōna teme­para, he pūru, he tūpare ki ngā kūwaha, ka mea kia patua he whaka­here e rātou ko ngā mano.<verse eid="ACT 14:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 14:14" />Otirā, i te rongo­nga o ngā āpō­toro, o Pānapa rāua ko Paora, ka hae­hae i ō rāua kākahu, ā, rere ana ki roto ki ngā tāngata, ka karanga atu, <verse eid="ACT 14:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 14:15" />ka mea, “E mara mā, he aha koutou ka mea ai i ēnei mea? He tāngata anō māua, he rite tahi ki a koutou te tū, e kauwhau ana hoki i te rongo­pai, kia tahuri kē koutou i ēnei mea teka­teka noa ki te Atua ora, nāna nei i hanga te rangi me te whenua, te moana me ō reira mea katoa. <verse eid="ACT 14:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 14:16" />I ngā whaka­tupu­ranga hoki kua pahemo atu, i tukua e ia ngā iwi katoa kia haere i ō rātou ake ara. <verse eid="ACT 14:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 14:17" />Otiia, kīhai i tukua e ia kia kāhore he kai­whaka­atu mōna; i ata­whai hoki ia, i hōmai anō e ia ki a koutou te ua o te rangi, me ngā pō hua, i mākona ai ō koutou ngākau i te kai, i te koa.” <verse eid="ACT 14:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 14:18" />Ā, ka kōrero­tia ēnei kupu, nā, mutu whaka­uaua i a rāua te mea a ngā tāngata ki te patu whaka­here mā rāua.<verse eid="ACT 14:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 14:19" />Otirā, ka haere mai ētahi Hūrai i Anatioka, i Ikoniuma; ā, ka whaka­kīkī rātou i ngā mano, ā, ākina ana a Paora ki te kōhatu, tōia ana ki waho o te pā, hua noa kua mate. <verse eid="ACT 14:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 14:20" />Otiia, i ngā ākonga e tū ana i tōna taha, ka whaka­tika ia, haere ana ki roto ki te pā. Ā, i te aonga ake ka haere rāua ko Pānapa ki Rerepe.<verse eid="ACT 14:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Hokinga ki Anitioka i Hīria</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 14:21" />Ā, nō ka kauwhau rāua i te rongo­pai ki taua pā, ā, he toko­maha ka meinga hei ākonga, ka hoki rāua ki Raihitara, ki Ikoniuma, ki Anatioka; <verse eid="ACT 14:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 14:22" />whakaū ana i ngā wairua o ngā ākonga, whaka­hau ana i a rātou kia mau tonu ki te whaka­pono, kua takoto hoki te tikanga, me nā runga i ngā mate­nga maha he ara atu mō tātou ki te ranga­tira­tanga o te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 14:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 14:23" />Ā, nō ka whaka­ritea e rāua he kaumātua mō rātou i tēnei hāhi, i tēnei hāhi, me te īnoi anō rāua me te noho­puku, ka tukua atu rātou e rāua ki te Ariki, i whaka­pono nei rātou.<verse eid="ACT 14:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 14:24" />Nā, ka haere rāua nā waenga­nui o Pihi­ria, tae tonu atu ki Pamapu­ria. <verse eid="ACT 14:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 14:25" />Ā, ka oti te kauwhau e rāua te kupu ki Pereka, ka haere rāua ki raro ki Ataria. <verse eid="ACT 14:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 14:26" />Ā, rere atu ana i reira ki Anatioka, ki te wāhi i tukua ai rāua ki te aroha noa o te Atua, mō te mahi ka oti nei i a rāua.<verse eid="ACT 14:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 14:27" />Nā, ka tae rāua ka hui­huia te hāhi, ka kōrero­tia ngā mea i mahi tahi ai te Atua me rāua ko tāna ua­kanga hoki i te tatau o te whaka­pono ki ngā tauiwi. <verse eid="ACT 14:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 14:28" />Ā, kīhai i iti te wā i noho ai rāua i reira ki ngā ākonga.<verse eid="ACT 14:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 14" />
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="ACT 15" />
  <para style="s1">Te Hui i Hiruhārama</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 15:1" />Nā, ka tae iho ētahi tāngata i Hūria ka whaka­ako i ngā tēina, “Ki te kore koutou e kotia, kia rite ki tā Mohi, e kore koutou e taea te whaka­ora.” <verse eid="ACT 15:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 15:2" />Nā, kīhai i iti te whawhai, te uiui a Paora rāua ko Pānapa ki a rātou, ka whaka­ritea ko Paora, ko Pānapa, ko ētahi atu hoki o rātou, e haere ki ngā āpō­toro, ki ngā kaumātua ki Hiruhārama, mō tēnei pūtake.<verse eid="ACT 15:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 15:3" />Heoi, āra­hina ana rātou e te hāhi haere ana rā Pini­kia, rā Hamaria kōrero ana i te tahuri­tanga o ngā tauiwi, ā, hoatu ana e rāua he hari nui ki ngā tēina katoa. <verse eid="ACT 15:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 15:4" />Ā, nō tō rāua taenga ki Hiruhārama ka whaka­manu­hiri­tia rāua e te hāhi, e ngā āpō­toro hoki rātou ko ngā kaumātua, ka kōrero­tia ngā mea i mahi tahi ai te Atua me rāua. <verse eid="ACT 15:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 15:5" />Nā, ko te whaka­tikanga o ētahi tāngata whaka­pono nō te tītore­hanga ki ngā Parihi, ka mea, “Me kokoti rātou, me ako hoki kia whaka­ritea te ture a Mohi.”<verse eid="ACT 15:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 15:6" />Nā, ka hui­hui ngā āpō­toro rātou ko ngā kaumātua ki te whaka­aro ki tēnei mea. <verse eid="ACT 15:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 15:7" />Ā, ka nui te tau­tohe­tohe, ka whaka­tika a Pita, ka mea ki a rātou, “E ngā tuā­kana, e mātau ana koutou ki te whiri­whiringa a te Atua i mua rawa i roto i a koutou, ko tōku māngai e rongo ai ngā tauiwi i te kupu o te rongo­pai, e whaka­pono ai hoki. <verse eid="ACT 15:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 15:8" />I whaka­ae hoki ki a rātou te Atua e mātau nei ki ngā ngākau, i a ia i hoatu ai i te Wairua Tapu ki a rātou, rite tahi ki tāna ki a tātou; <verse eid="ACT 15:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 15:9" />kāhore hoki i puta kē tōna whaka­aro ki a tātou, ki a rātou, i ō rātou ngākau kua mā i a ia i runga i te whaka­pono. <verse eid="ACT 15:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 15:10" />Ko tēnei, he aha koutou ka whaka­mā­tau­tau ai i te Atua, ka whaka­takoto ioka ai ki te kakī o ngā ākonga, he mea kīhai nei i taea te mau e ō tātou mātua, e tātou rānei? <verse eid="ACT 15:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 15:11" />Heoi, ka whaka­pono nei tātou, tērā tātou e ora i runga i te aroha noa o te Ariki, o Īhu Karaiti, ka pērā tahi hoki me rātou.”<verse eid="ACT 15:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 15:12" />Nā, noho puku ana te mano katoa, whaka­rongo ana ki a Pānapa rāua ko Paora e kōrero ana i ngā tohu, i ngā mea whaka­mīharo i mea ai te Atua kia mahia e rāua i roto i ngā tauiwi. <verse eid="ACT 15:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 15:13" />Ā, ka mutu tā rāua ka whaka­hoki a Hēmi, ka mea: “E ngā tuā­kana, whaka­rongo ki ahau! <verse eid="ACT 15:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 15:14" />Kua kōrero­tia e Himiona tā te Atua tiro­hanga mai i mua, tāna tango­hanga i tētahi iwi i roto i ngā tauiwi mō tōna ingoa. <verse eid="ACT 15:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 15:15" />E rite ana anō ki tēnei ngā kōrero a ngā poro­piti; i tuhi­tuhia rā:<verse eid="ACT 15:15" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 15:16" />‘I muri o ēnei mea ka hoki mai ahau,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:16">ka hangā anō e ahau te ta­pe­nā­kara o Rāwiri,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:16">kua hinga nei;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 15:16">ka hangā anō e ahau ōna wāhi kua horoa,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:16">ā, ka whaka­ara­hia e ahau.<verse eid="ACT 15:16" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 15:17" />Kia rapu ai ngā toenga o ngā tāngata ki te Ariki,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:17">me ngā tauiwi katoa hoki i karanga­tia nei tōku ingoa ki runga ki a rātou,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:17">e ai tā te Ariki, e mahi nei i ēnei mea katoa.<verse eid="ACT 15:17" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 15:18" />Nāna nei i mea kia mōhio­tia ēnei mea katoa</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:18">nō te tīma­tanga rā anō o te ao.’<verse eid="ACT 15:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 15:19" />“Nā, ko tōku whaka­aro tēnei; kia kaua e whaka­rarua te hunga e tahuri ana mai ki te Atua i roto i ngā tauiwi; <verse eid="ACT 15:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 15:20" />engari, kia tuhi atu tātou ki a rātou, kia mawehe atu rātou i ngā poke o ngā whaka­pakoko, i te moe tāhae, i te mea kua nōtia te kakī, i te toto. <verse eid="ACT 15:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 15:21" />Nō ngā whaka­tupu­ranga hoki ō mua ngā kai­kauwhau i a Mohi i tēnei pā, i tēnei pā, he mea kōrero i roto i ngā whare kara­kia i ngā hāpati katoa.”<verse eid="ACT 15:21" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Pukapuka ki ngā Tauiwi Whakapono</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 15:22" />Kātahi, ka pai ngā āpō­toro rātou ko ngā kaumātua me te hāhi katoa, kia whiri­whiria ētahi tāngata i roto i a rātou kia tonoa hei hoa mō Paora rāua ko Pānapa ki Anatioka; a Hūrā, i huaina nei ko Pāhapa, rāua ko Hira, he hunga ingoa nui i roto i ngā tēina, <verse eid="ACT 15:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 15:23" />ka tuhia hoki ēnei mea hei mau­ranga:</para>
  <para style="pi" vid="ACT 15:23">“Nā ngā āpō­toro rātou ko ngā kaumātua, ko ngā tuā­kana, ki ngā tēina o roto i ngā tauiwi, i Anatioka, i Hīria, i Kiri­kia; tēnā koutou. <verse eid="ACT 15:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 15:24" />Nā, ka rongo nei mātou, tērā ētahi i haere atu nei i a mātou, i whaka­raru i a koutou ki ngā kōrero, i whaka­pōhēhē i ō koutou ngākau, kāhore nei ā mātou kupu ki a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 15:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 15:25" />Kotahi tonu tō mātou whaka­aro he pai kia whiri­whiria ētahi tāngata, kia tonoa atu ki a koutou, hei hoa mō ā mātou tāngata e aroha nei, mō Pānapa rāua ko Paora; <verse eid="ACT 15:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 15:26" />he hunga i tuku nei i a rāua ki te mate hei mea mō te ingoa o tō tātou Ariki, o Īhu Karaiti. <verse eid="ACT 15:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 15:27" />Nā, kua tonoa atu nei e mātou a Hūrā rāua ko Hira, mā rāua hoki e kōrero a kupu atu aua mea anō. <verse eid="ACT 15:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 15:28" />I pai hoki ki te Wairua Tapu, ki a mātou hoki, kia kaua e utaina ki a koutou tētahi atu whaka­tai­maha, ko ēnei mea tika anake; <verse eid="ACT 15:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 15:29" />kia mawehe koutou i ngā mea e patua ana mā ngā whaka­pakoko, i te toto, i te mea kua nōtia te kakī, i te moe tāhae. Ka tiaki koutou i a koutou i ēnei mea, ka pai tā koutou mahi. Kia ora koutou.”<verse eid="ACT 15:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 15:30" />Ā, nō tō rātou tuku­nga atu, ka haere ki Anatioka. Nā, ka hui­huia te mano, ka hoatu te puka­puka. <verse eid="ACT 15:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 15:31" />Ā, ka oti te kōrero, ka koa rātou mō te kupu whaka­hauora. <verse eid="ACT 15:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 15:32" />Nā, he maha ngā kupu a Hūrā rāua ko Hira i whaka­hau ai, i whakaū ai i ngā tēina; he poro­piti hoki rāua. <verse eid="ACT 15:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 15:33" />Ā, ka roa iho rāua ki reira, ka tukua rāua e ngā tēina i runga i te rangi­mārie ki te hunga nāna rāua i tono atu. <verse eid="ACT 15:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 15:34" />Heoi, i pai a Hira kia noho ki reira.<verse eid="ACT 15:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 15:35" />Ko Paora ia rāua ko Pānapa i noho i Anatioka, i whaka­ako, i kauwhau i te kupu a te Ariki, rātou tahi ko tērā hunga toko­maha.<verse eid="ACT 15:35" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Wehe a Paora rāua ko Pānapa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 15:36" />Nā, muri iho i ētahi rā ka kī atu a Paora ki a Pānapa, “Tāua ka hoki, ka tiro­tiro i ngā tēina i ngā pā katoa i kauwhau­tia ai e tāua te kupu a te Ariki, i tō rātou pēhea­tanga.” <verse eid="ACT 15:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 15:37" />Ā, ka mea a Pānapa kia mauria hei hoa a Hoani, e huaina nei ko Māka. <verse eid="ACT 15:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 15:38" />Otiia, kīhai a Paora i pai kia haere i tō rāua tira te tangata i whaka­rere rā i a rāua i Pamapu­ria, kīhai hoki i haere tahi me rāua ki te mahi. <verse eid="ACT 15:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 15:39" />Heoi, nui atu tō rāua nga­ngare, mawehe ai rāua i a rāua, ā, mauria ana e Pānapa a Māka, rere ana ki Kai­peru. <verse eid="ACT 15:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 15:40" />Nā, tango ana a Paora i a Hira, haere ana, he mea tuku ki te aroha noa o te Atua e ngā tēina. <verse eid="ACT 15:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 15:41" />Ā, haere ana ia rā Hīria, rā Kiri­kia, whakaū ana i ngā hāhi.<verse eid="ACT 15:41" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 15" />
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="ACT 16" />
  <para style="s1">Ka Haere a Tīmoti ki te taha o Paora rāua ko Hira</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 16:1" />Nā, ka tae atu hoki ia ki Rerepe, ki Raihitara, ā, i reira tētahi ākonga, ko Tīmoti te ingoa, he tama nā tētahi wahine whaka­pono, he Hūrai, ko tōna pāpā ia he Kariki. <verse eid="ACT 16:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 16:2" />He pai te kōrero mōna a ngā tēina i Raihitara, i Ikoniuma. <verse eid="ACT 16:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 16:3" />I mea a Paora kia haere ia hei hoa mōna, ā, tango­hia ana ia, kotia ana, he mea hoki mō ngā Hūrai e noho ana i aua wāhi; i mātau hoki rātou katoa he Kariki tōna pāpā. <verse eid="ACT 16:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 16:4" />Ā, i a rātou e hāere­ere ana i ngā pā, ka tukua e rātou hei pupuri mā rātou ngā tikanga i whaka­ritea e ngā āpō­toro, e ngā kaumātua, i Hiruhārama. <verse eid="ACT 16:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 16:5" />Nā, ka whaka­ū­kia ngā hāhi ki te whaka­pono, ka nui haere hoki i tēnei rā, i tēnei rā.<verse eid="ACT 16:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Whakakitenga ki a Paora i Toroa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 16:6" />Nā, haere ana rātou nā waenga­nui o te whenua o Pirikia, o Karatia, kua āraia hoki e te Wairua Tapu kei kōrero i te kupu ki Āhia. <verse eid="ACT 16:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 16:7" />Ā, i te taenga atu ki Maihia, ka whaka­mātau rātou ki te haere ki Pitinia; heoi, kīhai i tukua e te Wairua o Īhu; <verse eid="ACT 16:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 16:8" />nā, kapea ana Maihia, ka haere ki Toroa. <verse eid="ACT 16:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 16:9" />Ā, ka kitea e Paora he kite­nga i te pō: He tangata nō Makeronia e tū ana, e tohe ana ki a ia, e mea ana, “Whiti mai ki Makeronia, āwhina­tia mātou.” <verse eid="ACT 16:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 16:10" />Ā, nō ka kitea te kite­nga, ka mea tonu mātou kia haere ki Makeronia, i whaka­aro hoki, nā te Atua mātou i karanga ki te kauwhau i te rongo­pai ki a rātou.<verse eid="ACT 16:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">I Piripai: Te Huringa o Riria ki te Whakapono</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 16:11" />Heoi, ko te rere­nga atu i Toroa, ka tika tonu mātou ki Hamotarakia, ā, ao ake te rā ki Neapori. <verse eid="ACT 16:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 16:12" />I reira atu ki Piripai, ko te pā nui ia o taua wāhi o Makeronia, he koroni nō Roma. Ā, noho ana mātou i taua pā ā taka noa ētahi rā. <verse eid="ACT 16:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 16:13" />Nā, i te rā hāpati ka haere mātou ki waho o te pā, ki te taha o tētahi awa, he whaka­aro ko te wāhi tērā hei karakia­tanga; ā, ka noho, ka kōrero ki ngā wāhine i haere tahi ake. <verse eid="ACT 16:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 16:14" />Nā, ka whaka­rongo tētahi wahine, ko Riria te ingoa, he kai­hoko pāpura, nō te pā o Taiataira, he wahine kara­kia ki te Atua. He mea whaka­puare tōna ngākau e te Ariki, i rongo ai ia ki ngā mea i kōrero­tia e Paora. <verse eid="ACT 16:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 16:15" />Ā, nō ka oti ia te iri­iri, rātou ko tōna whare, ka tohe ia, ka mea, “Ki te mea kua Whaka­aro koutou he pono tāku mahi ki te Ariki, tomo mai koutou, e noho ki tōku whare.” Nā, ka tohea mātou e ia.<verse eid="ACT 16:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">I te Whare Herehere i Piripai</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 16:16" />Nā, i a mātou e haere ana ki te wāhi īnoi, ka tūtaki ki a mātou tētahi kōtiro, he wairua mata­kite nei tōna, he nui te utu i riro i a ia mā ōna ranga­tira, i a ia e poro­piti ana. <verse eid="ACT 16:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 16:17" />Ka whai ia i a mātou ko Paora, ka karanga, ka mea, “He pono­nga ēnei tāngata nā te Atua, nā te Runga Rawa, e whaka­pua­kina ana e rātou te ara o te ora ki a koutou.” <verse eid="ACT 16:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 16:18" />Nā, he maha ngā rā i mea ai ia tēnei. Otiia, ka hōhā a Paora, ka tahuri, ka mea ki te wairua, “Ko tāku kupu tēnei ki a koe i runga i te ingoa Īhu Karaiti, puta mai i roto i a ia.” Puta mai ana i taua hāora anō.<verse eid="ACT 16:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 16:19" />Otirā, nō te kite­nga o ōna ranga­tira kua kore he mahi­nga moni mā rātou, ka mau ki a Paora rāua ko Hira, ka tōia ki te kāinga hoko ki ngā ranga­tira. <verse eid="ACT 16:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 16:20" />Ā, ka oti rāua te mau ki ngā kai­whaka­wā, ka mea, “Ko ēnei tāngata he Hūrai nei, e tino whaka­raru­raru ana i tō tātou pā, <verse eid="ACT 16:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 16:21" />e whaka­pua­kina ana hoki e rāua he rite­nga e kore nei e tika kia whaka­ae­tia, kia mahia e tātou, e ngā tāngata o Roma.” <verse eid="ACT 16:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 16:22" />Nā, ko te whaka­tikanga o te mano ki a rāua.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 16:22">Ka huhua ō rāua kākahu e ngā kai­whaka­wā, ka mea kia whiua ki te rākau. <verse eid="ACT 16:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 16:23" />Ā, ka maha ō rāua whiu­nga e rātou, ka makā rāua ki te whare here­here, ka tohu­tohu­tia te kai­tiaki here­here, kia mau tāna pupuri i a rāua. <verse eid="ACT 16:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 16:24" />Nō te riro­nga i a ia o taua kupu, ka makā rāua e ia ki te whare here­here i roto rawa, ka whaka­ūria ō rāua wae­wae ki te rākau.<verse eid="ACT 16:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 16:25" />Nā, i waenga­nui pō ka īnoi a Paora rāua ko Hira, ka waiata atu ki te Atua, me te whaka­rongo anō ngā here­here ki a rāua. <verse eid="ACT 16:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 16:26" />Nā, ka pā whaka­rere he rū nui, i ngarue ai ngā tū­ranga o te whare here­here. Ā, puare tonu atu ngā tatau katoa, whaka­koro­koroa ana ngā here­nga o ngā tāngata katoa. <verse eid="ACT 16:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 16:27" />Ā, ka oho te kai­tiaki here­here i te moe, ka kite i ngā tatau o te whare here­here e puare ana, nā, ka unu i tāna hoari, ka mea ki te patu i a ia anō, hua noa kua oma ngā here­here. <verse eid="ACT 16:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 16:28" />Nā, ka nui te reo o Paora ki te karanga, ka mea, “Kauaka tētahi mea kino e meatia ki a koe; ina tonu hoki mātou katoa.”<verse eid="ACT 16:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 16:29" />Ā, karanga­tia ana e ia he rama, ka rere ki roto, ka haere wiri, ka takoto ki te aro­aro o Paora rāua ko Hira. <verse eid="ACT 16:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 16:30" />Ka āra­hina hoki rāua ki waho, ka mea, “E hoa mā, me aha ka ora ai ahau?”<verse eid="ACT 16:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 16:31" />Ka mea rāua “Me whaka­pono ki te Ariki, ki a Īhu Karaiti, ka ora ai koe, koutou tahi ko tōu whare.” <verse eid="ACT 16:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 16:32" />Nā, ka kōrero­tia te kupu a te Ariki ki a ia, ki ngā tāngata katoa hoki i roto tōna whare. <verse eid="ACT 16:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 16:33" />Ā, ka mauria rāua e ia i taua hāora o te pō, ka horoia ō rāua whiu­nga; nā, iri­iria tonu­tia iho, a ia me āna tāngata katoa. <verse eid="ACT 16:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 16:34" />Ā, ka āra­hina rāua e ia ki tōna whare, ka whaka­tū­ria he tēpu kai ki mua i a rāua, ā, nui atu tōna hari, me tōna whare katoa, i te mea kua whaka­pono nei ki te Atua.<verse eid="ACT 16:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 16:35" />I te aonga ake ia o te rā, ka tonoa, ngā kātipa e ngā kai­whaka­wā, i mea, “Tukua aua tāngata kia haere.”<verse eid="ACT 16:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 16:36" />Nā, ka kōrero­tia e te kai­tiaki here­here ēnei kupu ki a Paora, ka mea, “Kua tono tāngata mai ngā kai­whaka­wā, kia tukua kōrua. Tēnā rā puta mai, haere i runga i te rangi­mārie.”<verse eid="ACT 16:36" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 16:37" />Nā, ko te kīanga atu a Paora, “Kua whiua nuitia nei māua e rātou, ahakoa kāhore i whaka­wā­kia, he tāngata hoki nō Roma, ā, kua makā māua ki te whare here­here. Ā, kei te makā puku­tia atu māua āia­nei e rātou? Kāhore rāpea; engari, mā rātou tonu e haere mai, e whaka­puta i a māua ki waho.”<verse eid="ACT 16:37" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 16:38" />Nā, ka kōrero­tia ēnei kupu e ngā kātipa ki ngā kai­whaka­wā; ā, ka wehi, i tō rātou rongo­nga nō Roma rāua. <verse eid="ACT 16:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 16:39" />Nā, ka haere mai rātou, ka tohe ki a rāua, ā, ka oti rāua te ārahi ki waho, ka mea rātou kia haere atu rāua i te pā. <verse eid="ACT 16:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 16:40" />Ā, ka puta atu rāua i te whare here­here, ka tomo ki te whare o Riria, ā, nō ka kite rāua i ngā tēina, ka whaka­mārie i a rātou, ka haere.<verse eid="ACT 16:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 16" />
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="ACT 17" />
  <para style="s1">I Teharonika</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 17:1" />Nā, ka hāere­ere rāua i Amapipori, Aporonia, ka tae ki Teharonika; he whare kara­kia nō ngā Hūrai i reira. <verse eid="ACT 17:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 17:2" />Ā, ka tomo atu a Paora ki a rātou, he tikanga hoki nāna, ā, e toru ngā hāpati i kōrero­rero ai ki a rātou i roto i ngā karaipi­ture, <verse eid="ACT 17:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 17:3" />i whaka­puaki ai, i kōrero ai, kua takoto hoki te tikanga kia mamae a te Karaiti, kia ara mai hoki i te hunga mate; ā, “Ko tēnei Īhu, e kauwhau­tia nei e ahau ki a koutou, ko ia te Karaiti.” <verse eid="ACT 17:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 17:4" />Nā, ka whaka­pono ētahi o rātou, ka piri hoki ki a Paora rāua ko Hira; he toko­maha hoki o ngā Kariki kara­kia, kīhai hoki i rua­rua ngā wāhine ranga­tira.<verse eid="ACT 17:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 17:5" />Heoi, ka hae ngā Hūrai, ka tango ki a rātou i ētahi tāngata kikino o te hunga māngere, ka hui­huia ngā tāngata, ka whaka­oho­tia te pā; nā, ko te hua­kanga ki te whare o Hahona, ka mea kia whaka­puta­ina rāua ki te iwi. <verse eid="ACT 17:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 17:6" />Ā, nō te kore­nga i kitea rāua ka tōia e rātou a Hahona rātou ko ētahi tēina ki ngā ranga­tira o te pā, ka karanga, “Kua tae mai ki konei ngā tāngata i whaka­tutū­ngia ai te ao; <verse eid="ACT 17:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 17:7" />kua puri­tia hoki e Hahona; e tika kē ana ngā mahi a tēnei hunga katoa i ngā ture a Hīhā, e mea ana, tērā atu tētahi kīngi, ko Īhu.” <verse eid="ACT 17:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 17:8" />Nā, ka rongo te mano rātou ko ngā ranga­tira o te pā ki ēnei mea, ka poro­raru. <verse eid="ACT 17:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 17:9" />Nā, ka tango rātou i ētahi moni pupuri i a Hahona rātou ko ērā atu, ā, tukua atu ana rātou.<verse eid="ACT 17:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">I Peria</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 17:10" />Nā, tonoa tonu­tia atu e ngā tēina a Paora rāua ko Hira i te pō ki Peria; i tō rāua taenga atu, ka haere ki te whare kara­kia o ngā Hūrai. <verse eid="ACT 17:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 17:11" />Engari, ēnei i nui atu te āhua ranga­tira i tō ngā tāngata o Teharonika, i hohoro tonu rātou te tango i te kupu, ā, i tēnei rā, i tēnei rā, i rapu i roto i ngā karaipi­ture i te tikanga o ēnei mea. <verse eid="ACT 17:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 17:12" />Nā, he toko­maha o rātou i whaka­pono; kīhai hoki i toko­iti ngā wāhine ranga­tira o ngā Kariki, me ngā tāne hoki. <verse eid="ACT 17:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 17:13" />Otirā, i te mōhio­tanga o ngā Hūrai o Teharonika, tērā te kupu a te Atua te kauwhau­tia ana e Paora ki Peria, ka haere hoki rātou ki reira ki te whaka­oho, ki te whaka­raru­raru i ngā mano. <verse eid="ACT 17:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 17:14" />Nā, tonoa tonu­tia atu e ngā tēina a Paora kia haere tae noa ki te moana; ko Hira ia rāua ko Tīmoti i noho ki reira. <verse eid="ACT 17:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 17:15" />Nā, ka kawea a Paora e ōna kai­ārahi ki Atene; ā, ka riro he kupu ki a Hira rāua ko Tīmoti kia hohoro te haere ki a ia, ka hoki rātou.<verse eid="ACT 17:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">I Atene</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 17:16" />Nā, i a Paora e tatari ana ki a rāua i Atene, ka oho tōna wairua i roto i a ia, i tāna kite­nga i te pā e kī ana i te whaka­pakoko. <verse eid="ACT 17:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 17:17" />Nā, totohe ana ia i roto i te whare kara­kia ki ngā Hūrai rātou ko ngā tāngata kara­kia, i te kāinga hoko hoki i ngā rā katoa ki ngā tāngata i pono ki a ia. <verse eid="ACT 17:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 17:18" />Ā, ka nga­ngare ki a ia ētahi tohu­nga o ngā Epikureana, o ngā Toika. Ko ētahi i mea, “He aha tā tēnei tangata kōrero­rero e mea nei?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 17:18">I mea ētahi, “Me te mea he kai­whaka­puaki ia i ētahi atua tauhou.” Mō tāna kauwhau i a Īhu, i te aranga, ki a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 17:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 17:19" />Nā, ka mau rātou ki a ia, ka kawea ki Areopaka, ka mea, “Kia mōhio mātou, he aha rānei tēnei ako hou e kōrero­tia nei e koe? <verse eid="ACT 17:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 17:20" />Poka kē hoki ngā mea e mauria mai nei e koe ki ō mātou tari­nga; koia mātou i mea ai kia mōhio, he aha ēnei mea.” <verse eid="ACT 17:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 17:21" />Ka mutu hoki tā ngā tāngata katoa o Atene, rātou ko ngā manu­hiri e noho ana i reira, e wātea ai, ko te kōrero rānei, ko te whaka­rongo rānei ki tētahi mea hou.<verse eid="ACT 17:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 17:22" />Nā, ka tū a Paora i waenga­nui o Areopaka, ka mea, “E ngā tāngata o Atene, i ngā mea katoa ka kite ahau he āhua nui kē tō koutou wehi ki ngā atua māori. <verse eid="ACT 17:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 17:23" />I ahau hoki e hāere­ere ana, e mā­taki­taki ana i ngā mea e kara­kia nei koutou, ka kite ahau i tētahi āta, i tuhia nei a runga, ‘Ki te Atua Ngaro’. Heoi, ko tā koutou e kara­kia kūware nei, ko ia tāku e whaka­atu nei ki a koutou. <verse eid="ACT 17:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 17:24" />Ko te Atua, nāna nei i hangā te ao me ngā mea katoa i roto, ko ia nei te Ariki o te rangi, o te whenua, e kore ia e noho ki ngā whare i hangā e te ringa. <verse eid="ACT 17:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 17:25" />E kore anō e mahia he mea māna e te ringa tāngata, me te mea he mate nōna ki tētahi aha rānei, ko ia hoki hei hōmai i te ora, i te manawa, i ngā mea katoa, ki ngā tāngata katoa. <verse eid="ACT 17:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 17:26" />Kotahi anō te toto i hangā ai e ia ngā iwi katoa o ngā tāngata, hei noho ki te mata katoa o te whenua, nāna hoki i whaka­takoto ō rātou wā i whaka­ritea i mua, me ngā kaha o tō rātou nohoa­nga. <verse eid="ACT 17:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 17:27" />Kia rapu ai rātou i te Atua, me kore e whā­whā, e kite i a ia, ahakoa rā kāhore ia i matara atu i a tātou katoa.<verse eid="ACT 17:27" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 17:28" />‘Nāna hoki tātou i ora ai, i kori­kori ai, i noho ai.’</para>
  <para style="m" vid="ACT 17:28">I pērā hoki te kōrero a ētahi o ō koutou kai­tito,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 17:28">‘Ko tātou hoki tōna uri.’<verse eid="ACT 17:28" /></para>
  <para style="m">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 17:29" />Nā, he uri nei tātou nō te Atua, e kore e tika kia mea tātou, kei te rite te Atua ki te kōura, ki te hiriwa, ki te kōhatu, ki te mea i whaka­iroa e te mōhio, e te whaka­aro o te tangata. <verse eid="ACT 17:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 17:30" />Nā, kāhore i whaka­aroa e te Atua ngā wā o te kūware­tanga; ināia­nei ia kua whaka­hau ia i ngā tāngata katoa o ngā wāhi katoa kia rīpe­netā. <verse eid="ACT 17:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 17:31" />Kua rite hoki i a ia he rā e whaka­wā ai ia i te ao i runga i te tika, arā mā te tangata kua whaka­ritea nei e ia; kua tukua nei hoki he tohu ki ngā tāngata katoa, i tāna whaka­ara­hanga i a ia i te hunga mate!”<verse eid="ACT 17:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 17:32" />Nā, ka rangona e rātou te aranga o te hunga mate, ka tāwai ētahi; ko ētahi i mea, “Taihoa mātou e whaka­rongo anō ki tēnei mea i a koe.” <verse eid="ACT 17:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 17:33" />Heoi, puta atu ana a Paora i waenga­nui i a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 17:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 17:34" />Ko ētahi tāngata ia i piri ki a ia, i whaka­pono; i roto i a rātou a Rionaihia nō Areopaka, ko tētahi wahine, ko Ramari te ingoa, rātou ko ētahi atu.<verse eid="ACT 17:34" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 17" />
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="ACT 18" />
  <para style="s1">I Koroniti</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 18:1" />Muri iho i ēnei mea ka haere atu a Paora i Atene, ka tae ki Koriniti. <verse eid="ACT 18:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 18:2" />Nā, ka kite ia i tētahi Hūrai ko Akuira te ingoa, i whānau ki Ponoto, he mea tae hou mai i Itari, rāua ko tāna wahine, ko Pirihira; kua whaka­haua hoki e Karau­ria kia haere atu ngā Hūrai katoa i Roma. Ā, ka haere ia ki a rāua, <verse eid="ACT 18:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 18:3" />ā, nō te mea kotahi tā rātou mahi, ka noho ia ki a rāua ka mahi rātou; he tui tēneti hoki tā rāua mahi. <verse eid="ACT 18:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 18:4" />Nā, ka kōrero­rero ia i roto i te whare kara­kia i ngā hāpati katoa, e tohe ana ki ngā Hūrai rātou ko ngā Kariki.<verse eid="ACT 18:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 18:5" />Nō te taenga mai ia o Hira rāua ko Tīmoti i Makeronia, ka tākare te ngākau o Paora, ka whaka­puaki ki ngā Hūrai ko Īhu te Karaiti. <verse eid="ACT 18:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 18:6" />Heoi, i a rātou ka whaka­tika, ka kohu­kohu, ka ruia e ia ōna kākahu, ka mea ki a rātou, “Hei runga i ō koutou māte­nga ō koutou toto; ka mā ahau. Ko tēnei ka haere ahau ki ngā tauiwi.” <verse eid="ACT 18:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 18:7" />Nā, ka haere atu ia i reira, ka tomo ki te whare o tētahi tangata, ko Taituha Hutuha te ingoa, he tangata kara­kia ki te Atua; ko tōna whare i tata tonu ki te whare kara­kia. <verse eid="ACT 18:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 18:8" />Nā, ka whaka­pono a Kirihipu, te ranga­tira o te whare kara­kia, me tōna whare katoa ki te Ariki; he toko­maha hoki ngā Koriniti, i a rātou ka rongo, i whaka­pono, i iri­iria hoki.<verse eid="ACT 18:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 18:9" />Ā, ka kōrero moe­moeā te Ariki ki a Paora i te pō, “Kaua e wehi, engari me kōrero, kei noho puku; <verse eid="ACT 18:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 18:10" />kei a koe hoki ahau, e kore hoki tētahi tangata e pā ki a koe, e hoatu i te kino ki a koe. He nui hoki āku tāngata i tēnei pā.” <verse eid="ACT 18:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 18:11" />Nā, kotahi te tau e ono marama i noho ai ia i reira, i whaka­ako ai i te kupu a te Atua i roto i a rātou.<verse eid="ACT 18:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 18:12" />Nā, i a Kario e noho ana hei kāwana mō Akāia, kotahi tonu whaka­tikanga o ngā Hūrai ki a Paora, ā, kawea ana ia ki te nohoa­nga whaka­wā, <verse eid="ACT 18:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 18:13" />ka mea, “E kukume ana tēnei i ngā tāngata ki tētahi kara­kia ki te Atua e poka kē ana i tā te ture.”<verse eid="ACT 18:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 18:14" />Ā, e mea tonu ana te māngai o Paora ki te puaki, ka mea a Kario ki ngā Hūrai, “E ngā Hūrai, me­he­mea ko tētahi hanga hē, ko tētahi mahi kino rānei, he tika kia āta whaka­rongo ahau ki a koutou. <verse eid="ACT 18:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 18:15" />Ko tēnei he totohe kōrero, he mea ki ngā ingoa, ki tā koutou ture, kei a koutou te whaka­aro; e kore hoki ahau e pai kia waiho ahau hei kai­whaka­wā mō ēnā mea.” <verse eid="ACT 18:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 18:16" />Nā, peia atu ana rātou e ia i te nohoa­nga whaka­wā. <verse eid="ACT 18:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 18:17" />Nā, ka mau ngā Kariki katoa ki a Hotene, ranga­tira o te whare kara­kia, ā, whiua ana ia i mua o te nohoa­nga whaka­wā. Heoi, kīhai a Kario i whaka­aro ki tētahi o ēnei mea.<verse eid="ACT 18:17" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Hokinga ki Anatioka</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 18:18" />Ā, ka maha ngā rā i noho ai a Paora, ka poro­poro­aki ia ki ngā tēina, ā, rere ana ki Hīria, rātou ko Pirihira ko Akuira. He mea more­more tōna ūpoko i Kenekerea; he kī tau­rangi hoki nāna. <verse eid="ACT 18:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 18:19" />Ā, ka tae rātou ki Epeha, ka mahue rāua i a ia ki reira. Ko ia i tomo ki te whare kara­kia, kōrero­rero ai ki ngā Hūrai. <verse eid="ACT 18:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 18:20" />Ā, i tā rātou mea­tanga kia roa atu te wā e noho ai ia ki a rātou, kīhai ia i whaka­ae. <verse eid="ACT 18:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 18:21" />Heoi, poro­poro­aki ana ki a rātou, ka mea, “E hoki mai anō ahau ki a koutou, ki te pai te Atua.” Ā, rere atu ana ia i Epeha.<verse eid="ACT 18:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 18:22" />Ā, nō ka ū ia ki Hiha­ria, ka haere atu ka oha ki te hāhi, ā, haere ana ki Anatioka. <verse eid="ACT 18:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 18:23" />Ā, roa­roa iho ki reira, ka haere, ā, hāere­erea mārie­tia ana e ia te whenua Karatia, o Pirikia, me te whakaū i ngā ākonga katoa.<verse eid="ACT 18:23" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ko Aporo kei Epeha kei Koriniti</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 18:24" />Nā, ka haere mai tētahi Hūrai ki Epeha, ko Aporo te ingoa, i whānau ki Arēhānaria, he pū kōrero, he tangata kaha ki ngā karaipi­ture. <verse eid="ACT 18:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 18:25" />I whaka­akona tēnei tangata ki te ara o te Ariki; he tangata ia e toko tonu ake ana te ngākau, ka kōrero ia, tika tonu hoki tāna whaka­ako i ngā mea mō Īhu; heoi anō, tāna i mātau ai ko te iri­iri a Hoani. <verse eid="ACT 18:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 18:26" />Ka anga ia ka kōrero nui i roto i te whare kara­kia. Nō te rongo­nga o Akuira rāua ko Pirihira ki a ia, ka mau rāua ki a ia, ka āta whaka­atu ki a ia i te ara o te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 18:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 18:27" />Ā, nō ka mea ia kia haere ki Akāia, ka tau­tokona ia e ngā tēina, ā, ka tuhi­tuhi rātou ki ngā ākonga kia whaka­manu­hiri­tia ia e rātou. Ā, nō tōna taenga atu, ka whaka­kaha­ngia e ia te hunga i meinga nei e te aroha noa kia whaka­pono. <verse eid="ACT 18:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 18:28" />Kaha rawa hoki tāna whawhati i tā ngā Hūrai i roto i te hui­hui; whaka­atu­ria ana e ia tā ngā karaipi­ture mō Īhu, ko te Karaiti ia.<verse eid="ACT 18:28" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 18" />
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="ACT 19" />
  <para style="s1">Ko Paora kei Epeha</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 19:1" />I a Aporo i Koriniti, ka puta atu a Paora nā ngā wāhi o runga, ka tae ki Epeha, ā, tūpono atu ko ētahi ākonga. <verse eid="ACT 19:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 19:2" />Ā, ka mea ki a rātou, “I riro rānei te Wairua Tapu i a koutou i tō koutou whaka­pono­tanga?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 19:2">Anō rā, ko rātou ki a ia, “Kāhore, kīanō mātou i rongo noa me­he­mea te Wairua Tapu i hōmai.”<verse eid="ACT 19:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 19:3" />Ka mea ia ki a rātou, “I iri­iria oti koutou ki roto ki te aha?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 19:3">Ka mea rātou, “Ki roto ki tā Hoani iri­iri.”<verse eid="ACT 19:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 19:4" />Nā, ka mea a Paora, “Ko tā Hoani iri­iri he iri­iri rīpe­netā. I mea ia ki te iwi, kia whaka­pono rātou ki tētahi e haere mai ana i muri i a ia, arā ki a Īhu.”<verse eid="ACT 19:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 19:5" />Ā, ka rongo rātou i tēnei, ka iri­iria i runga i te ingoa o te Ariki, o Īhu. <verse eid="ACT 19:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 19:6" />Nā, ka oti te whaka­pā e Paora ōna ringa ki runga ki a rātou, ka tae mai te Wairua Tapu ki a rātou; nā, ka kōrero­tia e rātou ngā reo, ka poro­piti hoki. <verse eid="ACT 19:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 19:7" />Ā, ko tō rātou toko­maha kei te tekau mā rua.<verse eid="ACT 19:7" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 19:8" />Nā, ka tomo ia ki te whare kara­kia, ka kōrero māia atu, e toru ngā marama i kōrero­rero ai, i kukume ai ki ngā mea o te ranga­tira­tanga o te Atua. <verse eid="ACT 19:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 19:9" />Ā, ka pakeke ētahi, ka whaka­teka, ka whaka­hāwea ki taua rite­nga i te aro­aro o te mano, ka mawehe atu ia i roto i a rātou, ka wehea kētia ngā ākonga, ka kōrero­rero i tēnei rā, i tēnei rā, i roto i te kura o Tairanu. <verse eid="ACT 19:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 19:10" />Nā, e rua ōna tau i pēnei ai; ā, ka rongo katoa te hunga e noho ana i Āhia, ngā Hūrai, ngā Kariki, i te kupu a te Ariki, a Īhu.<verse eid="ACT 19:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ngā Tama a Hewa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 19:11" />Nā, ehara i te mere­kara noa ake a te Atua i mea ai kia meatia e ngā ringa o Paora; <verse eid="ACT 19:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 19:12" />ina hoki, i te mau­ranga atu i ngā aikiha me ngā ārai i tōna tinana ki te hunga mate, mutu ake ō rātou mate, ā, puta atu ana ngā wairua kino i roto i a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 19:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 19:13" />Kātahi, ka anga ētahi o ngā Hūrai hāere­ere noa, he hunga pei wairua, ka whaka­hua i te ingoa o te Ariki, o Īhu ki runga ki ētahi i ngā wairua kino, ka mea, “He whaka­hua tēnei nā mātou ki a koutou i a Īhu, i tā Paora e kauwhau nei.” <verse eid="ACT 19:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 19:14" />Nā, i pērā anō ngā tama toko­whitu a tētahi Hūrai, a Hewa, he tohu­nga nui ia.<verse eid="ACT 19:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 19:15" />Nā, ka whaka­hoki te wairua kino, ka mea ki a rātou, “E mōhio ana ahau ki a Īhu, e mātau ana ki a Paora; ko koutou ia, ko wai rā?”<verse eid="ACT 19:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 19:16" />Nā, ko te tū­peke­tanga o te tangata i a ia nei te wairua kino ki a rātou, kua kaha i a rātou, taea ana rātou e ia, nō ka oma ta­ha­nga rātou, ka oma mamae atu i taua whare. <verse eid="ACT 19:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 19:17" />Ā, ka mōhio­tia tēnei e ngā tāngata katoa e noho ana i Epeha, e ngā Hūrai rātou tahi ko ngā Kariki; ā, ka tau te wehi ki a rātou katoa, ā, whaka­nuia ana te ingoa o te Ariki, o Īhu. <verse eid="ACT 19:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 19:18" />Ā, he toko­maha o te hunga whaka­pono i haere mai, i whāki, i whaka­kite i ā rātou mahi. <verse eid="ACT 19:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 19:19" />He toko­maha anō o te hunga i mahi i ngā mahi tini­hanga, i hui­hui i ā rātou puka­puka, ā, tahuna ana i te aro­aro o te katoa. Ā, ka taua ngā utu o aua puka­puka, ka kitea e rima tekau mano hiriwa. <verse eid="ACT 19:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 19:20" />Koia anō te nui o te tupu o te kupu a te Atua, te kaha.<verse eid="ACT 19:20" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Tutūtanga i Epeha</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 19:21" />Ā, nō ka rite ēnei mea, ka mea a Paora i roto i tōna wairua, kia tika nā Makeronia, nā Akāia, kia haere ki Hiruhārama; i mea ia, “Ka tae ahau ki reira, ko Roma anō tāku e tiki ai e ti­tiro.” <verse eid="ACT 19:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 19:22" />Ā, toko­rua āna i tono ai ki Makeronia o te hunga e mahi ana ki a ia, ko Tīmoti rāua ko Eratu; ko ia i noho iho i Āhia mō tētahi wā.<verse eid="ACT 19:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 19:23" />Nā, i taua wā kīhai i nohi­nohi te nga­ngau i puta ake mō taua Ara. <verse eid="ACT 19:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 19:24" />Tērā hoki tētahi tangata, ko Rimitiriu te ingoa, he kai­mahi hiriwa, nāna nei i hanga ngā teme­para hiriwa o Riana, kīhai hoki i no­nohi ngā utu i tika mai i tāna mahi ki ngā kai­hanga. <verse eid="ACT 19:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 19:25" />Nā, ka whaka­minea rātou e ia me ērā kai­mahi o ngā pērā, ā, ka mea, “E mara mā, e mātau ana koutou, nō tēnei mahi ā tātou rawa. <verse eid="ACT 19:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 19:26" />Nā, e kite ana, e rongo ana koutou, ehara i te mea ko Epeha anake, engari he iti te wāhi o Āhia katoa kua mahue nei i tēnei Paora te kukume, te whaka­peau kē i te tini o te tangata, e mea ana ia, ‘Ehara ēnei i te atua, e hangā nei e te ringa.’ <verse eid="ACT 19:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 19:27" />Nā, ehara i te mea ko tō tātou nei wāhi anake ka tata te kore noa iho; tērā anō hoki e whaka­kāhore­tia te teme­para o te atua nui, o Riana, ā, meāke memeha noa iho tōna nui, e karakia­tia nei e Āhia katoa, e te ao.”<verse eid="ACT 19:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 19:28" />Ā, nō tō rātou rongo­nga, ā, ka kī i te riri, ka karanga ake, ka mea, “He nui a Riana o ngā Epehi!” <verse eid="ACT 19:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 19:29" />Nā, ka tutū te puehu o te pā katoa, ā, ka oti te hopu e rātou a Kaiu rāua ko Aritaku, he hunga nō Makeronia, he hoa haere nō Paora, nā, kotahi tonu tā rātou kōkiri­tanga ki te whare mā­taki­taki. <verse eid="ACT 19:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 19:30" />Ā, i a Paora e mea ana kia tomo ki roto ki te iwi, kīhai ia i tukua e ngā ākonga. <verse eid="ACT 19:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 19:31" />Nā, ka unga tāngata mai ētahi o ngā ranga­tira o Āhia, i pai nei ki a ia, ka mea kia kaua ia e tuku i a ia ki roto ki te whare mā­taki­taki. <verse eid="ACT 19:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 19:32" />Heoi, puta kē te karanga a ētahi, puta kē a ētahi; tino raru­raru hoki taua whaka­mine­nga; ko te nuinga kīhai i mātau ki te mea i hui­hui ai rātou. <verse eid="ACT 19:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 19:33" />Nā, ka mauria e rātou a Arēhanara i roto i te hui, nā ngā Hūrai ia i mea kia whaka­tika atu. Ā, tā­whiri ana te ringa o Arēhānara, i mea hoki kia kōrero­tia e ia tā rātou ki te iwi. <verse eid="ACT 19:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 19:34" />Heoi, ka mātau rātou he Hūrai ia, kotahi tonu te reo o te katoa ki te karanga, ā tata noa ki te rua ngā hāora, “He nui a Riana o ngā Epehi!”<verse eid="ACT 19:34" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 19:35" />Ā, ka māriri iho te hui­hui i te kai­whaka­wā, ka mea ia, “E ngā Epehi, ko wai te tangata kāhore e mōhio ko te pā o ngā Epehi te kai­tiaki teme­para o te atua nui, o Riana, o te whaka­pakoko anō hoki i taka iho i a Hupita? <verse eid="ACT 19:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 19:36" />Nā, ka kore nei ēnei mea e taea te whākore­kore, heoi, kia āta noho, kaua hoki e hīkaka te mahi. <verse eid="ACT 19:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 19:37" />Kua āra­hina mai nei hoki e koutou ēnei tāngata ki konei, ehara nei i te hunga tāhae mea tapu, ehara hoki i te hunga kohu­kohu ki tō tātou atua. <verse eid="ACT 19:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 19:38" />Nā, ki te mea he kupu tā Rimitiriu rātou ko ōna hoa mahi mō tētahi tangata, e taea te whaka­wā, ā, tēnei anō ngā kāwana; mā rātou rātou e whaka­wā. <verse eid="ACT 19:38" /><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 19:39" />Nā, ki te mea he mea kē tā koutou e whai nā, waiho mā te rū­nanga tika te rite­nga. <verse eid="ACT 19:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 19:40" />Ko wai hoki ka tohu? Tērā pea tātou e whaka­wā­kia mō tēnei nga­ngau­tanga o nāia­nei, kāhore nei ōna take; kāhore hoki he take e tika ai tā tātou kōrero mō tēnei hui­hui.” <verse eid="ACT 19:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 19:41" />Ā, nō ka puaki ēnei kupu āna, ka tonoa atu e ia te whaka­mine­nga.<verse eid="ACT 19:41" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 19" />
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="ACT 20" />
  <para style="s1">Ki Makeronia me Kariki</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 20:1" />Ā, nō te mutu­nga o te nga­ngau, ka karanga­tia e Paora ngā ākonga, ka tohu­tohu i a rātou, ka poro­poro­aki, ā, tūria atu ana e ia, haere ana ki Makeronia. <verse eid="ACT 20:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 20:2" />Ā, ka hāere­erea e ia aua wāhi, me te whaka­hau i a rātou ki ngā kupu maha, ā, haere ana ia ki Kariki; <verse eid="ACT 20:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 20:3" />ā, ka toru ōna marama ki reira. I ngā Hūrai anō e whaka­takoto whaka­aro ana mōna, i a ia meāke rere ki Hīria, ka whaka­aro ia kia hoki mā Makeronia. <verse eid="ACT 20:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 20:4" />Ā, i haere tahi i a ia tae noa ki Āhia, a Hopate o Peria, te tama a Piru; a Aritaku rāua ko Hekunu o Teharonika; a Kaiu o Rerepe; a Tīmoti hoki rātou ko Tikiku, ko Toropimu o Āhia. <verse eid="ACT 20:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 20:5" />Otirā, kua haere atu ēnei i mua, ā, e tatari mai ana ki a mātou i Toroa. <verse eid="ACT 20:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 20:6" />Nā, i te mutu­nga o ngā rā o te Taro Rēwenakore ka rere atu mātou i Piripai, ā, pō rima ka tae atu ki a rātou ki Toroa, ā, e whitu ngā rā i noho ai ki reira.<verse eid="ACT 20:6" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Haerenga Whakamutunga o Paora ki Toroa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 20:7" />Nā i te rā tua­tahi o te wiki, i te mea kua hui­hui mātou ki te whawhati taro, ka kauwhau a Paora ki a rātou, e mea ana hoki ki te haere i te aonga ake; ā, ka kūmea roatia tāna kōrero ā waenga­nui pō rā anō. <verse eid="ACT 20:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 20:8" />Ā, he maha ngā rama i te rūma i runga, i te wāhi i hui­hui ai mātou. <verse eid="ACT 20:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 20:9" />Nā, tērā tētahi tai­tama­riki, ko Ūtiku te ingoa, i te mata­pihi e noho ana, kua tino para­ngia e te moe; ā, ka roa tonu te kauwhau a Paora, nā, ka pēhia rawa­tia ia e te moe, nā, ka taka iho i te toru o ngā whaka­papa­ranga o ngā rūma, tango­hia rawa­tia ake kua mate. <verse eid="ACT 20:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 20:10" />Nā, ka heke iho a Paora, ā, hinga ana ki runga ki a ia, awhi ana i a ia, ka mea, “Kei nga­ngau koutou; kei roto hoki i a ia tōna wairua.” <verse eid="ACT 20:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 20:11" />Nā, ka kake atu anō ia, ka whawhati taro, ka kai, ā, ka roa rawa te kōrero ā pūao noa, ka haere. <verse eid="ACT 20:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 20:12" />Heoi, āra­hina oratia atu ana e rātou taua tai­tama, kīhai hoki i nohi­nohi te koa.<verse eid="ACT 20:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mai i Toroa ki Miretu</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 20:13" />Nā, ko mātou kua riro i mua ki te kai­puke, ā, rere ana ki Aho, i mea kia utaina a Paora i reira; nāna hoki i whaka­rite, i mea hoki ko ia me rā uta. <verse eid="ACT 20:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 20:14" />Ā, ka tūtaki ki a mātou ki Aho, ka utaina ia, ā, rere ana mātou ki Mitirini. <verse eid="ACT 20:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 20:15" />Rere atu ana mātou i reira, ā, i te aonga ake ka taea te rite­nga atu o Kio; ao ake anō ka ū ki Hamo, ā, noho ana ki Torokiriuma; ao ake anō ka ū ki Miretu. <verse eid="ACT 20:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 20:16" />I mea hoki a Paora kia rere i waho ake o Epeha, kei roa ia ki Āhia; i pōrangi hoki me kore e roko­hanga atu ia e te rā o te Petekoha ki Hiruhārama.<verse eid="ACT 20:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Poroporoaki a Paora ki ngā Kaumātua o Epeha</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 20:17" />Nā, ka tono tāngata atu ia i Miretu ki Epeha, hei tiki i ngā kaumātua o te hāhi. <verse eid="ACT 20:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 20:18" />Ā, nō tō rātou taenga mai ki a ia, ka mea ia ki a rātou, “E mātau ana koutou ki tāku tikanga i roto i a koutou i ngā rā katoa, nō te rā tua­tahi iho anō o tōku taenga mai ki Āhia, <verse eid="ACT 20:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 20:19" />pāpaku noa iho te ngākau i mahi ai ahau ki te Ariki, he maha ia ngā roi­mata me ngā whaka­mā­tau­tau i pā ki ahau, i ngā Hūrai e whaka­takoto whaka­aro ana mōku. <verse eid="ACT 20:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 20:20" />Kīhai i puri­tia e ahau tētahi o ngā mea pai i whaka­kitea atu anō ki a koutou i ākona nuitia ki a koutou, i tēnei whare, i tēnei whare. <verse eid="ACT 20:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 20:21" />I kauwhau­tia hoki ki ngā Hūrai ki ngā Kariki, te rīpe­netā whaka te Atua, me te whaka­pono ki tō tātou Ariki, ki a Īhu Karaiti. <verse eid="ACT 20:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 20:22" />Nā, tēnei ahau te haere nei ki Hiruhārama, he here­here­nga nā te wairua, kāhore hoki e mōhio ki ngā mea e pā ki ahau i reira. <verse eid="ACT 20:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 20:23" />Heoi anō, ko tā te Wairua Tapu e whaka­atu nei ki ahau i tēnei pā, i tēnei pā, e mea ana, kei te tāria mai ahau e ngā meka­meka, e ngā mate. <verse eid="ACT 20:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 20:24" />Otirā, kāhore ahau e ihu­puku ki te ora, hei painga ki ahau ake, engari, kia taea tāku e whai nei, me te mahi i hōmai ki ahau e te Ariki, e Īhu, arā kia whaka­atu­ria te rongo­pai o te aroha noa o te Atua.<verse eid="ACT 20:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 20:25" />“Nā, e mōhio ana tēnei ahau, heoi anō, kite­nga o tōku mata e tētahi o koutou, e te hunga i kauwhau haere nei ahau i te ranga­tira­tanga o te Atua i roto i a koutou. <verse eid="ACT 20:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 20:26" />Koia ahau ka mea nei ki a koutou āia­nei, Kāhore ōku poke i ngā toto o tētahi tangata. <verse eid="ACT 20:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 20:27" />Kīhai hoki ahau i manawa­pā ki te kauwhau i te whaka­aro katoa o te Atua ki a koutou. <verse eid="ACT 20:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 20:28" />Nā, kia tūpato ki a koutou, ki te kāhui katoa anō i meinga ai koutou e te Wairua Tapu hei kai­tiro­tiro, whāngaia te hāhi a te Atua i hokona nei e ia ki ōna ake toto. <verse eid="ACT 20:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 20:29" />E mōhio ana hoki ahau ki tēnei ka riro ahau tērā e puta mai ki a koutou he wuruhi nana­kia, e kore nei e tohu i te kāhui. <verse eid="ACT 20:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 20:30" />Ā, ka whaka­tika ake ētahi tāngata i roto i a koutou anō, kōrero ai i ngā mea parori kē, hei kukume i ngā ākonga kia whai i a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 20:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 20:31" />Nā reira, kia mata­ara, kia mahara anō ki ngā tau e toru kīhai nei ahau i māngere i te pō, i te ao, ki te whaka­tūpato i tēnei, i tēnei o koutou, me te tangi anō ahau.<verse eid="ACT 20:31" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 20:32" />“Nā, tēnei ahau, te tuku nei i a koutou ki te Atua, ki te kupu hoki o tōna aroha noa, e kaha nei ki te whaka­tupu ake, ki te hoatu hoki i tētahi wāhi ki a koutou i roto i te hunga katoa kua oti te whaka­tapu. <verse eid="ACT 20:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 20:33" />Kīhai i hia­hia­tia e ahau te hiriwa, te kōura, te kākahu rānei, o tētahi. <verse eid="ACT 20:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 20:34" />E mōhio ana anō koutou, nā ēnei ringa i mahi ngā mea i matea e ahau, e ōku hoa hoki. <verse eid="ACT 20:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 20:35" />I ngā mea katoa i hoatu ahau he tauira ki a koutou, kia pēnei tā koutou mahi kia ata­whai­tia ai e koutou te hunga ngoi­kore, me te mahara ki ngā kupu a te Ariki, a Īhu, i mea rā ia, ‘Ko te whaka­whi­whi, nui atu te hari i tō te whi­whi.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 20:35" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 20:36" />I te mutu­nga o tēnei whai kupu āna ka tukua ōna turi ki raro, ka īnoi tahi ia me rātou katoa. <verse eid="ACT 20:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 20:37" />He nui hoki te tangi o te katoa; hinga iho rātou ki runga ki te kakī o Paora, ka kihi i a ia; <verse eid="ACT 20:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 20:38" />i tino mamae pū hoki rātou i te kupu i mea ai ia, heoi anō, tō rātou kite­nga i tōna mata. Nā, ka ārahi rātou i a ia ki te kai­puke.<verse eid="ACT 20:38" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 20" />
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="ACT 21" />
  <para style="s1">Ka Haere a Paora ki Hiruhārama</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 21:1" />Heoi, ka wehe mātou i a rātou, ka rere, ā, tika tonu atu, tae noa ki Koha, ā, ao ake te rā kei Roro, i reira atu ki Pātara. <verse eid="ACT 21:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 21:2" />Nā, ka roko­hanga tētahi kai­puke e whaka­whiti atu ana ki Pini­kia, ā, eke ana mātou ki runga, rere ana. <verse eid="ACT 21:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 21:3" />Ā, ka kitea Kai­peru, ka mahue ake i te taha ki mauī, ka rere atu mātou ki Hīria, ā, ka ū ki Tāira; hei reira hoki te kai­puke ruke ai i tōna utanga. <verse eid="ACT 21:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 21:4" />Ā, ka kitea ngā ākonga, e whitu ngā rā i noho ai mātou ki reira. Ka kōrero hoki rātou ki a Paora, he mea nā te Wairua, kia kaua ia e haere ki Hiruhārama. <verse eid="ACT 21:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 21:5" />Ā, ka rite aua rā o mātou, ka puta atu mātou, ka haere; me te kawe anō rātou katoa, me ngā wāhine, me ngā tama­riki, i a mātou ā waho rā anō o te pā. Nā, ka tukua ō mātou turi ki te taha­tai, ka īnoi; <verse eid="ACT 21:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 21:6" />kātahi ka poro­poro­aki mātou tētahi ki tētahi; ā, eke ana mātou ki te kai­puke; ko rātou ia i hoki ki ō rātou kāinga.<verse eid="ACT 21:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 21:7" />Ā, ka tutuki tō mātou rere­nga atu i Tāira, ka tae ki Toromai, nā, ka oha atu ki ngā tēina, ā, kotahi te rā i noho ai ki a rātou. <verse eid="ACT 21:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 21:8" />I te aonga ake ka tūria atu e mātou, ka haere ki Hiha­ria; ā, tomo ana ki te whare o Piripi kai­kauwhau, ko ia nei tētahi o ngā toko­whitu; noho ana i a ia. <verse eid="ACT 21:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 21:9" />Nā, toko­whā ngā tamā­hine a taua tangata, he wāhina, he poro­piti. <verse eid="ACT 21:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 21:10" />Ā, ka maha ō mātou rā i noho ai, ka haere mai tētahi poro­piti i Hūria, ko Akapu te ingoa. <verse eid="ACT 21:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 21:11" />Ā, nō tō rātou taenga mai ki a mātou, ka mau ki te whī­tiki o Paora, herea iho e ia ōna ake ringa me ōna wae­wae, ka mea, “Ko tā te Wairua Tapu kōrero tēnei, E pēnei­tia te here te tangata nōna tēnei whī­tiki e ngā Hūrai i Hiruhārama, e tukua atu anō ia ki ngā ringa o ngā tauiwi.”<verse eid="ACT 21:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 21:12" />Heoi, i tō mātou rongo­nga i ēnei mea, ka tohe mātou ko ngā tāngata o taua kāinga, kia kaua ia e haere ki Hiruhārama. <verse eid="ACT 21:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 21:13" />Nā, ko te whaka­hoki­nga a Paora, “He aha tā koutou e tangi, e whaka­ngākau­kore nei i ahau? Ehara hoki i te mea ko te here anake tāku e pai ai, engari ko te mate anō hoki ki Hiruhārama, mō te ingoa o te Ariki, o Īhu.”<verse eid="ACT 21:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 21:14" />Ā, nō tōna kore­nga i rongo, ka mutu tā mātou, ka mea, “Kia meatia tā te Ariki e pai ai.”<verse eid="ACT 21:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 21:15" />Ā, ka pahemo ēnei rā, ka takai mātou i ā mātou mea, ā, haere ana ki Hiruhārama. <verse eid="ACT 21:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 21:16" />I haere tahi anō i a mātou ētahi o ngā ākonga o Hiha­ria; nā rātou i mau ake a Nahona o Kai­peru, he ākonga tawhito hei tuku­nga atu mō mātou.<verse eid="ACT 21:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Haere a Paora ki a Hēmi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 21:17" />Ā, i tō mātou taenga ki Hiruhārama, ka koa ngā tēina ki a mātou. <verse eid="ACT 21:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 21:18" />I te aonga ake, ka haere tahi mātou ko Paora ki a Hēmi; i reira anō ngā kaumātua katoa. <verse eid="ACT 21:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 21:19" />Nā, ka oha ia ki a rātou, ka kōrero­tia taki­tahi­tia ngā mea i mea ai te Atua kia mahia e ia i roto i ngā tauiwi. <verse eid="ACT 21:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 21:20" />Nō tō rātou rongo­nga, ka whaka­korōria i te Atua, ka mea ki a ia, “Kua kite koe, e tō mātou teina, i ngā mano tini o ngā Hūrai kua whaka­pono nei; e uaua katoa ana hoki ki te ture. <verse eid="ACT 21:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 21:21" />Kua rongo anō hoki rātou ki a koe, e whaka­ako ana koe i ngā Hūrai katoa i roto i ngā tauiwi, kia whaka­rērea a Mohi, e mea ana kia kaua rātou e kokoti i ngā tama­riki, kia kaua anō e haere i runga i ngā rite­nga o mua. <verse eid="ACT 21:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 21:22" />Nā, me pēhea? E kore hoki e kore ka rongo rātou ki tōu taenga mai. <verse eid="ACT 21:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 21:23" />Nā, me mea e koe tēnei e kōrero­tia nei e mātou ki a koe. Toko­whā e mātou tāngata, he kupu tau­rangi tā rātou. <verse eid="ACT 21:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 21:24" />Tango­hia ēnei, kia purea ngā­tahi­tia koutou, māu anō e utu ā rātou mea, kia waru­hia ai ō rātou māte­nga. Ā, ka kite rātou katoa he teka noa ngā mea i kōrero­tia mōu; engari ko koe, he tika tāu haere, kei te whaka­rite anō koe i te ture. <verse eid="ACT 21:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 21:25" />Tēnā ko ngā tauiwi kua whaka­pono, kua tuhi­tuhi atu mātou, kua whaka­takoto tikanga atu, kia tūpato rātou i ngā mea e patua ana mā ngā whaka­pakoko, i te toto, i te mea kua nōtia te kakī, i te moe tāhae.”<verse eid="ACT 21:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 21:26" />Nā, ka mau a Paora ki aua tāngata, ā, i te aonga ake ka pure tahi, ka haere tahi rātou ki roto ki te teme­para, hei whaka­atu ka whaka­ritea ngā rā mō te pure­nga, kia whaka­herea rā anō he whaka­here mō tētahi, mō tētahi o rātou.<verse eid="ACT 21:26" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Mau a Paora i roto i te Temepara</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 21:27" />Heoi, ka tata ngā rā e whitu te taka, ka kitea ia i roto i te teme­para e ētahi Hūrai o Āhia; nā rātou i whaka­oho te mano katoa, ā, ka pā ō rātou ringa ki a ia, <verse eid="ACT 21:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 21:28" />ka karanga, “E ngā tāngata o Īharaira, āwhina­tia mai! Ko te tangata tēnei e whaka­ako nei i ngā tāngata katoa o ngā wāhi katoa ki ngā mea whaka­hē mō te iwi, mō te ture, mō tēnei kāinga hoki. Kua kawea mai anō e ia ētahi Kariki ki roto ki te teme­para, ā, ka noa nei i a ia tēnei wāhi tapu.” <verse eid="ACT 21:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 21:29" />I kite hoki rātou i mua he hoa nōna i roto i te pā, ko Toropimu o Epeha; tohu noa rātou, kua mauria mai ia e Paora ki roto ki te teme­para.<verse eid="ACT 21:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 21:30" />Nā, ka oho te pā katoa, ka oma ngā tāngata. Ā, ka mau rātou ki a Paora, tōia ana ia ki waho o te teme­para; tū­taki­na tonu­tia atu ngā tatau. <verse eid="ACT 21:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 21:31" />Nā, i a rātou e whai ana kia patua ia, ka tae te rongo ki te ranga­tira mano o te hapū hōia, kua tutū te puehu i Hiruhārama katoa. <verse eid="ACT 21:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 21:32" />Nā, hohoro tonu tāna mau ki ētahi hōia, ki ētahi kene­turio, ā, oma iho ana ki a rātou. Ā, nō tō rātou kite­nga i te ranga­tira mano, i ngā hōia hoki, ka mutu te patu i a Paora. <verse eid="ACT 21:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 21:33" />Nā, ka whaka­tata mai te ranga­tira mano, ka tango i a ia, ka mea kia herea ia ki ngā meka­meka e rua; ā, ka ui ko wai ia, i aha hoki ia. <verse eid="ACT 21:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 21:34" />Nā, he karanga anō tā ētahi, he karanga kē tā ētahi, i roto i te mano. Nā, kīhai ia i mōhio ki te tino tikanga, i te nga­ngau hoki, ā, whaka­haua ana kia āra­hina ia ki te pā. <verse eid="ACT 21:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 21:35" />Ā, nō tōna taenga ki te piki­tanga, ka hiki­tia ia e ngā hōia i te tau­tute­tute­nga hoki a te tāngata; <verse eid="ACT 21:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 21:36" />i aru hoki te hui­hui o te iwi, me te karanga, “Whaka­matea ia!”<verse eid="ACT 21:36" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Whakahoki Kōrero a Paora mōna anō</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 21:37" />Ā, nō ka whano a Paora te kawea ki roto ki te pā, ka mea ia ki te ranga­tira mano, “E pai ana rānei kia kōrero ahau i tētahi kupu ki a koe?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 21:37">Ka mea ia, “E mātau ana rānei koe ki te reo Kariki? <verse eid="ACT 21:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 21:38" />Ehara oti koe i te Īhipiana, nāna nei i whaka­tupu te tutū i mua ake rā, ā, mauria ana e ia ngā tāngata kōhuru e whā mano ki te koraha?”<verse eid="ACT 21:38" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 21:39" />Ka mea a Paora, “He Hūrai ahau, nō Tarahu o Kiri­kia, he tangata tupu nō taua pā, ehara hoki i te pā ingoa­kore. Nā, ko tāku īnoi tēnei ki a koe, tukua ahau kia kōrero ki te iwi.”<verse eid="ACT 21:39" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 21:40" />Nā, tukua ana e ia, ā tū ana a Paora ki te piki­tanga, ka tā­whiri tōna ringa ki te iwi. Nā, mutu pū te turi­turi, ka kōrero ia, nō ngā Hiperu te reo, ka mea:<verse eid="ACT 21:40" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 21" />
  <chapter number="22" style="c" sid="ACT 22" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 22:1" />“E ōku tuā­kana, e ōku mātua, whaka­rongo ki tēnei kōrero āku ki a koutou.” <verse eid="ACT 22:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 22:2" />Ā, ka rongo rātou ko te reo Hiperu tāna i kōrero ai ki a rātou, kātahi ka mutu rawa te kīkī. Ā, ka mea ia:<verse eid="ACT 22:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 22:3" />“He Hūrai ahau, i whānau ki Tarahu o Kiri­kia, i whaka­tupu­ria i roto i tēnei pā ki ngā wae­wae o Kamariera, i āta whaka­akona ki te tino tikanga o te ture o ngā mātua, i uaua anō ahau mō te Atua, i pēnā me koutou katoa ināia­nei. <verse eid="ACT 22:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 22:4" />Ā, whaka­toia ana e ahau ngā tāngata o tēnei Tikanga, tae ana ki te mate; herea ana e ahau ngā tāne me ngā wāhine, ā, tukua ana ki ngā whare here­here. <verse eid="ACT 22:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 22:5" />Mā te tohu­nga, nui tēnei kōrero āku e whaka­tika, mā te hui­hui hoki o ngā kaumātua katoa. I riro mai hoki i ahau ā rātou puka­puka ki ngā tēina, ā, haere ana ahau ki Ramahiku, kia herea, kia āra­hina mai hoki te hunga o reira ki Hiruhārama kia whaka­mamae­tia.”<verse eid="ACT 22:5" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Kōrero a Paora mō tōna Huringa ki te Whakapono</para>
  <para style="r">(<ref loc="ACT 9:1-19">Ngā Mahi 9.1-19</ref>; <ref loc="ACT 26:12-18">26.12-18</ref>)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 22:6" />“Nā, i ahau e haere ana, e whaka­tata ana ki Ramahiku, i te pou­tū­mārō­tanga, ka whiti whaka­rere mai ki ahau he mārama nui nō te rangi. <verse eid="ACT 22:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 22:7" />Ā, hinga ana ahau ki te whenua, ka rangona he reo e mea ana ki ahau, ‘E Haora, e Haora, he aha tāu e whaka­toi nei i ahau?’ <verse eid="ACT 22:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 22:8" />Nā, ka whaka­hokia e ahau, ‘Ko wai koe, e te Ariki?’ Ka mea ia ki ahau, ‘Ko Īhu ahau o Nahareta, e whaka­toia nei e koe.’ <verse eid="ACT 22:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 22:9" />I kite anō ōku hoa i te mārama, otirā kīhai i rongo i te reo ōna i kōrero ki ahau. <verse eid="ACT 22:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 22:10" />Ka mea ahau, ‘Me aha ahau, e te Ariki?’ Ka mea te Ariki ki ahau, ‘Whaka­tika, haere ki Ramahiku; ā, ka kōrero­tia ki a koe i reira ngā mea katoa kua whaka­ritea kia meinga e koe.’ <verse eid="ACT 22:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 22:11" />Heoi, i te mea kāhore ahau i kite, nā te korōria hoki o taua mārama, ka āra­hina-ā-ringa­tia ahau e ōku hoa haere, ka tae ki Ramahiku.<verse eid="ACT 22:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 22:12" />“Nā, ko tētahi tangata, ko Anania, he tangata kara­kia, i rite tonu nei ki tā te ture āna mahi, ā, e kōrero­tia paitia ana e ngā Hūrai katoa e noho ana i reira. <verse eid="ACT 22:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 22:13" />Haere mai ana ia ki ahau, ā, tū ana i tōku taha, ka mea mai ki ahau, ‘E tōku teina, e Haora, ti­tiro ake!’ Ā, i taua hāora anō ka ti­tiro ahau ki a ia. <verse eid="ACT 22:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 22:14" />I mea anō ia, ‘Nā te Atua o ō tātou mātua koe i whiri­whiri, kia mātau ki tāna e pai ai, kia kite i a te Tika, kia rongo hoki i te reo o tōna māngai. <verse eid="ACT 22:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 22:15" />Nō te mea ko koe hei kai­whaka­atu māna ki ngā tāngata katoa, mō ngā mea i kite ai, i rongo ai koe. <verse eid="ACT 22:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 22:16" />Nā, he aha tāu e whaka­roa nei? Whaka­tika, kia iri­iria koe, kia horoia ōu hara, me te karanga anō ki te ingoa o te Ariki.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 22:16" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Karangatanga a Paora kia Kauwhau ki ngā Tauiwi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 22:17" />“Ā, nō tōku hoki­nga mai ki Hiruhārama, i ahau e īnoi ana i roto i te teme­para, ka puta te ngākau mata­kite ki ahau, <verse eid="ACT 22:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 22:18" />ā, ka kite ahau i a ia e mea ana mai ki ahau, ‘E āhua, kia hohoro te haere atu i Hiruhārama; e kore hoki rātou e tango i tāu kōrero mōku.’ <verse eid="ACT 22:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 22:19" />Nā, ko tāku mea­tanga, ‘E te Ariki, e mātau ana rātou, he kai­here­here ahau, he kai­whiu i roto i ngā whare kara­kia, i te hunga i whaka­pono ki a koe. <verse eid="ACT 22:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 22:20" />Ā, i te whaka­heke­nga o ngā toto o tōu kai­whaka­atu, o Tepene, i reira ahau e tū ana, e whaka­ae ana, e tiaki ana hoki i ngā kākahu o ōna kai­whaka­mate.’ <verse eid="ACT 22:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 22:21" />Nā, ko tāna mea­tanga ki ahau, ‘Haere. Ka ungā hoki koe e ahau ki tawhiti ki ngā tauiwi.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 22:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 22:22" />Ā, whaka­rongo ana rātou ki a ia taea noatia tēnei kupu, nā, ka hāmama rātou, ka mea, “Whaka­matea atu te korokē nei i runga i te whenua! E kore hoki e pai kia ora ia.” <verse eid="ACT 22:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 22:23" />Heoi, i a rātou e karanga ana, e ruke­ruke ana i ō rātou kākahu, e ākiri ana i te puehu ki te rangi. <verse eid="ACT 22:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 22:24" />Ka whaka­hau te ranga­tira kia kawea ia ki te pā, ka mea kia whiua, kia uia; kia mātau ai ia ki te mea i pēnei ai rātou te karanga ki a ia. <verse eid="ACT 22:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 22:25" />Ā, ka oti ia te here e rātou ki ngā here, ka mea a Paora ki te kene­turio e tū ana i reira, “He mea tika rānei kia whiua e koutou te tangata, he tangata nō Roma, i te mea kāhore anō i mau noa tōna hē?”<verse eid="ACT 22:25" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 22:26" />Ā, nō te rongo­nga o te kene­turio, ka haere, ka kōrero ki te ranga­tira mano, ka mea, “He aha tāu e mea ai? Nō Roma hoki te tangata nei.”<verse eid="ACT 22:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 22:27" />Nā, ka haere mai te ranga­tira mano, ka mea ki a ia, “Kōrero mai ki ahau, nō Roma koe?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 22:27">Ka mea ia, “Āe.”<verse eid="ACT 22:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 22:28" />Nā, ka whaka­hoki te ranga­tira mano, “Nā te moni nui i whi­whi ai ahau ki tēnei taonga, hei tangata whenua nō Roma.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 22:28">Ka mea a Paora, “Ko ahau i whānau tonu nō Roma.”<verse eid="ACT 22:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 22:29" />Nā whaka­rērea tonu­tia iho ia e te hunga e mea ana ki te ui ki a ia; i mataku hoki te ranga­tira mano, tōna rongo­nga nō Roma ia, mōna hoki i here i a ia.<verse eid="ACT 22:29" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ko Paora kei mua o te Rūnanga</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 22:30" />Nā, i te aonga ake ka mea ia kia mātau ki te tikanga, ki te mea i whaka­wā­kia ai ia e ngā Hūrai, ka wewete i ōna here, ka whaka­hau kia haere mai ngā tohu­nga nui, me tō rātou rū­nanga katoa, ā, āra­hina iho ana a Paora, whaka­tū­ria ana ki tō rātou aro­aro.<verse eid="ACT 22:30" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 22" />
  <chapter number="23" style="c" sid="ACT 23" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 23:1" />Nā, ka ti­tiro pū a Paora ki te rū­nanga, ka mea, “E ōku tuā­kana, tika tonu ki tōku mahara tāku whaka­haere i te aro­aro o te Atua, ā taea noatia tēnei rā.” <verse eid="ACT 23:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 23:2" />Nā, ka mea a Anania tohu­nga nui ki te hunga e tū ana i tōna taha, kia pākia tōna māngai. <verse eid="ACT 23:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 23:3" />Anō rā, ko Paora ki a ia, “Tēnei ake ka papaki te Atua i a koe, e te paki­tara kua oti te pani ki te paru mā! Ā, ka noho mai koe hei whaka­wā i ahau i tā te ture i whaka­takoto ai, me te whaka­hau anō kia pākia ahau, e hē nei tēnā ki te ture?”<verse eid="ACT 23:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 23:4" />Nā, ka mea te hunga e tū tata ana, “E whaka­manu­manu ana koe ki te tohu­nga nui a te Atua?”<verse eid="ACT 23:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 23:5" />Anō rā ko Paora, “Kīhau ahau i mātau, e ōku tuā­kana, ko ia te tohu­nga nui; kua oti hoki te tuhi­tuhi, ‘Aua e kōrero­tia kino­tia te ranga­tira o tōu iwi.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 23:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 23:6" />Ā, nō ka kite a Paora nō ngā Haruki ētahi, ko ētahi nō ngā Parihi, ka karanga ia i roto i te rū­nanga, “E ōku tuā­kana, he Parihi ahau, he tama nā ngā Parihi. Ko te aranga o te hunga mate e tūmanako­hia nei te mea e whaka­wā­kia nei ahau.”<verse eid="ACT 23:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 23:7" />Ā, nō tāna kōrero­tanga i tēnei, ka tohe­tohe ngā Parihi rātou ko ngā Haruki; ka wahi­rua hoki te hui­hui. <verse eid="ACT 23:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 23:8" />E mea ana hoki ngā Haruki, kāhore he aranga, kāhore he ana­hera, he wairua rānei; ko ngā Parihi ia e whaka­ae ana ki aua mea e rua. <verse eid="ACT 23:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 23:9" />Ā, ka nui te nga­ngare; ka whaka­tika ētahi o ngā kara­ipi o tō ngā Parihi taha, ka totohe, ka mea, “Kāhore anō i mau i a mātou te hē o tēnei tangata. Tēnā, ka pēhea, me­he­mea kua kōrero tētahi wairua ki a ia, tētahi ana­hera rānei?”<verse eid="ACT 23:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 23:10" />Ā, nō ka nui te nga­ngau, ka mataku te ranga­tira mano kei motu­motu­hia a Paora e rātou, nā, ungā ana e ia ngā hōia kia heke atu, ki te tango mai i a ia i roto i a rātou, kia āra­hina hoki ki te pā.<verse eid="ACT 23:10" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 23:11" />Ā, i taua pō ka tū te Ariki ki tōna taha, ka mea, “Kia māia! Kia pēnā i a koe i whaka­atu nā mōku i Hiruhārama, tāu whaka­atu hoki ki Roma.”<verse eid="ACT 23:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Whakangārahu ki a Paora</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 23:12" />Ao ake te rā, ka hui­hui ētahi o ngā Hūrai, ka maka oati ki a rātou anō, ka mea, kia kaua rātou e kai, kia kaua e inu, kia whaka­matea rā anō e rātou a Paora. <verse eid="ACT 23:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 23:13" />Ā, e whā tekau nga­horo ngā tāngata nāna tēnei oati­tanga. <verse eid="ACT 23:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 23:14" />Nā, ka haere rātou ki ngā tohu­nga nui rātou ko ngā kaumātua, ka mea, “Kua oati mātou i tētahi oati nui, kia kaua e pā kai, kia mate rā anō a Paora i a mātou. <verse eid="ACT 23:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 23:15" />Nā, mā koutou tahi ko te rū­nanga e kī atu ki te ranga­tira mano kia āra­hina iho ia ki a koutou āpōpō, me te mea nei e mea ana koutou kia āta mōhio­tia te take ki a ia. Ko mātou ia, i te mea kīanō ia i tata noa, ka noho rite ki te whaka­mate i a ia.”<verse eid="ACT 23:15" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 23:16" />Otirā, ka rongo te tama a te tua­hine o Paora ki tō rātou whaka­aro whaka­papa, ka haere ia, ka tomo ki te pā, ka kōrero ki a Paora. <verse eid="ACT 23:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 23:17" />Kātahi, ka karanga a Paora ki tētahi kene­turio, ka mea, “Ārahina atu te tama­iti nei ki te ranga­tira mano; he kōrero hoki tāna ki a ia”. <verse eid="ACT 23:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 23:18" />Nā, ka mau ia ki a ia, ka ārahi i a ia ki te ranga­tira mano, ka mea, “I karanga te here­here, a Paora, i ahau, i mea kia āra­hina mai tēnei tama­iti ki a koe, he kōrero hoki tāna ki a koe.”<verse eid="ACT 23:18" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 23:19" />Nā, ka mau te ranga­tira mano ki tōna ringa, ka haere ki tahaki, ka ui atu, “He aha tāu mea hei kōrero ki ahau?”<verse eid="ACT 23:19" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 23:20" />Anō rā ko tērā, “Kua whaka­takoto whaka­aro ngā Hūrai kia mea ki a koe kia āra­hina iho a Paora āpōpō ki te rū­nanga, ānō e āta uia anō e koe tētahi atu mea mōna. <verse eid="ACT 23:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 23:21" />Nā, aua koe e rongo ki a rātou; e whā hoki tekau nga­horo tāngata o rātou e whanga ana ki a ia. Kua puaki tā rātou oati, kia kaua e kai, kia kaua e inu, kia mate rā anō ia i a rātou. Nā, kua rite tēnei rātou, e tatari ana ki te kupu whaka­ae i a koe.”<verse eid="ACT 23:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 23:22" />Kātahi, ka tukua atu taua tama­iti e te ranga­tira mano, ka mea ia, “Kaua e kōrero­tia ki tētahi tāu whaka­atu­ranga mai i ēnei mea ki ahau.”<verse eid="ACT 23:22" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Mauranga i a Paora ki a Pirika te Kāwana</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 23:23" />Nā, toko­rua ngā kene­turio i karanga­tia e ia; i mea ia, “Kia rite mai ētahi hōia kia rua rau hei haere ki Hiha­ria, me ētahi hōia eke hōiho kia whitu tekau, me tētahi hunga mau mātia kia rua rau, i te toru o ngā hāora o te pō. <verse eid="ACT 23:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 23:24" />Ā, ka whaka­hau ia ki a rāua, kia whaka­ritea mai he kararehe, hei whaka­noho­anga iho mō Paora ki runga, kia kawea oratia ai ia ki a Pirika, ki te kāwana.” <verse eid="ACT 23:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 23:25" />Ā, i tuhi­tuhia e ia he puka­puka, ka pēnei:<verse eid="ACT 23:25" /></para>
  <para style="pi">
    <verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 23:26" />“Nā, Karau­ria Raihia ki a Pirika, ki te kāwana pai rawa, Tēnā koe. <verse eid="ACT 23:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 23:27" />I hopu­kia tēnei tangata e ngā Hūrai, ā, i a ia ka tata te whaka­matea e rātou, ka puta atu ahau me ngā hōia, ā, tango­hia mai ana ia; i rongo hoki ahau nō Roma ia. <verse eid="ACT 23:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 23:28" />I mea anō ahau kia rongo i te take i whaka­wā­kia ai ia e rātou, ā, āra­hina ana ia e ahau ki tō rātou rū­nanga. <verse eid="ACT 23:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 23:29" />Nā ka kite ahau he kupu tau­tohe nō tō rātou ture i whaka­wā­kia ai ia, kāhore hoki ōna hē i tika ai te mate, te here rānei. <verse eid="ACT 23:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 23:30" />Ā, nō te whaka­atu­ranga mai ki ahau, kei te whaka­papa­tia he mate mō te tangata nei, tonoa tonu­tia ia e ahau ki a koe, i mea hoki ahau ki ōna kai­whaka­pae, kia kōrero­tia ki a koe ngā mea mōna.”<verse eid="ACT 23:30" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 23:31" />Nā, ka mau ngā hōia ki a Paora, ka pērā me te mea i kōrero­tia ki a rātou, ā, āra­hina ana ia i te pō ki Anatipatari. <verse eid="ACT 23:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 23:32" />Ao ake te rā ka tukua atu ngā tāngata eke hōiho hei hoa haere mōna, ā, hoki ana rātou ki te pā. <verse eid="ACT 23:32" /><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 23:33" />Ā, nō te taenga o ērā ki Hiha­ria, ka hoatu te puka­puka ki te kāwana, ā, whaka­tū­ria ana a Paora ki tōna aro­aro. <verse eid="ACT 23:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 23:34" />Ā, nō te tiro­hanga iho o te kāwana, ka ui, nō tēhea kāwana­tanga ia; ā, i tōna rongo­nga nō Kiri­kia ia, <verse eid="ACT 23:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 23:35" />ka mea ia, “Ka whaka­rongo ahau ki a koe, ina tae mai anō hoki ōu kai­whaka­pae.” Ā, i whaka­hau ia, kia tiaki­na ia i roto i te whare whaka­wā o Herora.<verse eid="ACT 23:35" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 23" />
  <chapter number="24" style="c" sid="ACT 24" />
  <para style="s1">Te Take ki a Paora</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 24:1" />Nā, ka pahure ngā rā e rima, ka haere atu a Anania, te tohu­nga nui rātou ko ētahi kaumātua, ko tētahi kai­kōrero hoki, ko Tereturu, whaka­kite ai i ngā hē o Paora ki te kāwana. <verse eid="ACT 24:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 24:2" />Ā, ka oti ia te karanga, ka tīmata a Tereturu te whaka­wā, ka mea:</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 24:2">“I te mea nāu i hua ai te rangi­mārie ki a mātou, he āta ngā­rahu hoki nāu i whaka­tika­tika­ina ai ngā kino ki tēnei iwi. <verse eid="ACT 24:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 24:3" />Nui atu tā mātou whaka­whetai mō aua mea ka riro mai nei i a mātou, i ngā wā katoa, i ngā wāhi katoa, e Pirika, e te tangata pai rawa. <verse eid="ACT 24:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 24:4" />Otiia, e kore e nui atu tāku whaka­ware i a koe, koia ka īnoi atu ki a koe kia pai koe ki te whaka­rongo mai ki ētahi kupu toru­toru a mātou. <verse eid="ACT 24:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 24:5" />I mau hoki i a mātou te korokē nei, he tangata whaka­tūtehu, e whaka­oho ana i ngā Hūrai katoa o te ao, ko ia hoki te tino take o te tītore­hanga ki tā ngā Nahareti. <verse eid="ACT 24:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 24:6" />I mea hoki ia kia whaka­noa­tia te teme­para: nā ka hopu mātou i a ia, ka mea kia whaka­wā­kia ia ki tā tō mātou ture i whaka­takoto ai. <verse eid="ACT 24:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 24:7" />Otirā, i puta mai a Raihia, te ranga­tira mano, ā, tango­hia kino­tia atu ana ia i ō mātou ringa. <verse eid="ACT 24:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 24:8" />Ā, ungā ana ōna kai­whaka­pae kia haere mai ki a koe: māu e ui ki a ia, kia rongo ai koe ki ēnei mea katoa e whaka­wā­kia nei ia e mātou.” <verse eid="ACT 24:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 24:9" />Ā, i whaka­ae hoki ngā Hūrai ki taua whaka­pae, i mea, “Koia tērā ko aua mea.”<verse eid="ACT 24:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Tā Paora Tohe i mua i a Pirika</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 24:10" />Ā, ka tohu atu te kāwana ki a ia kia kōrero, ka whaka­hokia e Paora,</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 24:10">“E mātau ana ahau, ka maha ōu tau e whaka­wā nei koe i tēnei iwi, koia i pai ai tōku ngākau ki te tohe i te tika o āku mea. <verse eid="ACT 24:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 24:11" />E takoto kau ana hoki hei mōhio­tanga mōu, kāhore i maha ake i te tekau mā rua ngā rā ōku i haere nei ki Hiruhārama, ki te kara­kia. <verse eid="ACT 24:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 24:12" />Kīhai anō ahau i mau i a rātou i roto i te teme­para e totohe ana ki tētahi, e mea ana rānei i te mano kia tutū, kāhore i ngā whare kara­kia, kāhore anō hoki i te pā. <verse eid="ACT 24:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 24:13" />E kore anō e taea e rātou te whaka­tau ki ahau i tōu aro­aro ngā mea e whaka­wā­kia nei ahau e rātou. <verse eid="ACT 24:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 24:14" />Otirā, me whāki tēnei e ahau ki a koe, ko te Ara e kīa nei e rātou he tītore­hanga, ko tāku tēnā i ahau e kara­kia nei ki te Atua o ōku mātua; e whaka­pono ana hoki ahau ki ngā mea katoa kua oti te whaka­rite i roto i te ture, kua oti hoki te tuhi­tuhi ki tā ngā poro­piti. <verse eid="ACT 24:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 24:15" />E tū­mana­ko ana ki tā te Atua, ki tā ēnei anō hoki e whaka­ae nei, arā tēnei ake ka ara te hunga mate, ngā tāngata tika, ngā tāngata hē. <verse eid="ACT 24:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 24:16" />Tēnei anō tāku e whai nei, kia hara­kore tonu tōku hine­ngaro i te aro­aro o te Atua, o ngā tāngata.<verse eid="ACT 24:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 24:17" />“Nā, muri iho i ngā tau e maha, ka tae mai ahau ki te kawe mai i ngā mea ata­whai rawa­kore ki tōku iwi, me ngā whaka­here. <verse eid="ACT 24:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 24:18" />I kitea ahau i reira e rātou, e purea ana i roto i te teme­para, kāhore he hui­hui, kāhore he nga­ngau. <verse eid="ACT 24:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 24:19" />Tērā anō rā ētahi Hūrai nō Āhia; ko te tikanga kia haere mai rātou ki a koe ki te whaka­wā, ki te mea he mea tā rātou mōku. <verse eid="ACT 24:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 24:20" />Tēnei rānei mā ēnei tāngata tonu e kōrero, me i kitea e rātou he hē tōku, i ahau e tū ana i mua i te rū­nanga, <verse eid="ACT 24:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 24:21" />ko taua kupu kotahi pea i karanga ai ahau, i ahau e tū ana i roto i a rātou, ‘Ko te aranga o te hunga mate te mea e whaka­wā­kia nei ahau e koutou ināia­nei.’ ”<verse eid="ACT 24:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 24:22" />Otirā, i te mea he nui atu tōna mōhio ki taua Ritenga, ka ungā rātou e Pirika, ka mea ia, “Kia tae mai a Raihia, te ranga­tira mano, ka tino rapu ahau ki te tikanga o ā koutou mea.” <verse eid="ACT 24:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 24:23" />Nā, ka mea ia ki te kene­turio kia tiaki­na a Paora, kia waiho noa anō ia, kia kaua e rīria ōna hoa ina mahi ki a ia.<verse eid="ACT 24:23" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ko Paora i te Aroaro o Pirikia rāua ko Ruhuhira</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 24:24" />Nā, muri iho i ētahi rā ka tae mai a Pirika rāua ko tāna wahine ko Ruruhira, he Hūrai, ka mea ia kia tīkina atu a Paora, ā, ka whaka­rongo ki a ia ki te whaka­pono ki a te Karaiti. <verse eid="ACT 24:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 24:25" />Ā, i a ia e kōrero ana ki ngā mea o te tika, ki te hia­hia kia pēhia, ki te whaka­wā­kanga kei te haere mai, ka wiri a Pirika, ka mea, “Haere āia­nei. Kia wātea ahau, ka karanga atu ai anō i a koe.” <verse eid="ACT 24:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 24:26" />Tohu noa hoki ka hoatu ki a ia he moni e Paora; koia i hono ai te tiki atu i a ia, te kōrero ki a ia.<verse eid="ACT 24:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 24:27" />Otirā, ka pahure ngā tau e rua, ka whaka­kapia a Pirika e Porohia Petuha, ā, i tōna hia­hia ki te whaka­mānawa­reka i ngā Hūrai, ka waiho e Pirika a Paora kia here ana.<verse eid="ACT 24:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 24" />
  <chapter number="25" style="c" sid="ACT 25" />
  <para style="s1">Ka Īnoi a Paora ki te Emepara</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 25:1" />Nō te taenga mai o Petuha ki te kāwana­tanga, ka toru ngā rā, ka haere atu ia i Hiha­ria ki Hiruhārama. <verse eid="ACT 25:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 25:2" />Nā, ka kōrero te tohu­nga nui me ngā ranga­tira o ngā Hūrai ki a ia mō Paora, ka tohe ki a ia, <verse eid="ACT 25:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 25:3" />kia whaka­ae­tia tā rātou mōna, kia tīkina atu ia ki Hiruhārama, he whanga hoki tō rātou mōna kia whaka­matea ki te ara. <verse eid="ACT 25:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 25:4" />Otirā, ka whaka­hokia e Petuha, kei Hiha­ria a Paora e pupuri ana, ā, tērā e hohoro tōna haere ki reira. <verse eid="ACT 25:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 25:5" />I mea anō ia, “Me haere tahi anō i ahau ki raro ngā mea ō koutou e whai mana ana, ki te whaka­wā i taua tangata, ki te mea he kino tōna.”<verse eid="ACT 25:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 25:6" />Ā, ka noho ia i a rātou mō ngā rā e waru, nga­huru rānei, nā, ka haere ki Hiha­ria; ao ake te rā ka noho ki te nohoa­nga whaka­wā, ā, ka mea kia āra­hina mai a Paora. <verse eid="ACT 25:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 25:7" />Ā, nō tōna taenga atu, e tū ana tērā ngā Hūrai i haere mai i Hiruhārama, he maha, he nui ngā hē i whaka­pā­ngia e rātou ki a Paora; heoi kīhai i ū tā rātou. <verse eid="ACT 25:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 25:8" />Ā, ka utua e Paora, “Kāhore rawa ōku hara ki te ture a ngā Hūrai, kāhore hoki ki te teme­para, kāhore anō ki a Hīhā.”<verse eid="ACT 25:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 25:9" />Heoi, ka mea a Petuha ki a Paora, i tōna hia­hia kia pai­ngia e ngā Hūrai, “E pai ana rānei koe kia haere ki Hiruhārama, ki reira whaka­wā­kia ai mō ēnei mea ki tōku aro­aro?”<verse eid="ACT 25:9" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 25:10" />Anō rā ko Paora, “E tū ana ahau ki te nohoa­nga whaka­wā o Hīhā, hei reira tonu ahau whaka­wā­kia ai; kāhore ōku hē ki ngā Hūrai, kua tino kitea nā hoki e koe. <verse eid="ACT 25:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 25:11" />Me he hē tōku, kua meinga rānei e ahau tētahi mea e tika ai te mate, e kore ahau e kino kia mate; tēnā ko tēnei he teka ngā mea e whaka­pā­ngia nei e rātou ki ahau, e kore e āhei kia tukua ahau e tētahi ki a rātou. He karanga tēnei nāku ki a Hīhā”.<verse eid="ACT 25:11" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 25:12" />Nā, ka kōrero­rero a Petuha ki te rū­nanga, ā, ka mea, “Kua karanga koe ki a Hīhā; nā me haere koe ki a Hīhā.”<verse eid="ACT 25:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ko Paora i te Aroaro o Akaripa rāua ko Pereniki</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 25:13" />Ā muri iho i ētahi rā, ka tae atu a Kīngi Akaripa, rāua ko Pereniki ki Hiha­ria, ā, ka oha ki a Petuha. <verse eid="ACT 25:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 25:14" />Ā, ka pō maha rāua e noho ana i reira, ka kōrero­tia e Petuha ki te kīngi te take mō Paora, ka mea, “Tēnei tētahi tangata i waiho iho e Pirika e here ana. <verse eid="ACT 25:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 25:15" />Ā, i ahau i Hiruhārama, ka kōrero­tia mai ia ki ahau e ngā tohu­nga nui, e ngā kaumātua o ngā Hūrai, ka tono rātou kia whaka­wā­kia ia. <verse eid="ACT 25:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 25:16" />Nā, ko tāku whaka­hoki­nga atu ki a rātou, ‘Ehara i te rite­nga nā ngā tāngata o Roma kia tukua he tangata kia mate i te mea kīanō i tū­ta­taki noa te tangata e whaka­wā­kia ana ki ngā kai­whaka­pae, i whai wāhi rānei ki te whaka­hoki kupu ki te kupu whaka­wā mōna.’ <verse eid="ACT 25:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 25:17" />Nō reira, i tō rātou mine­nga mai ki konei, kīhai ahau i whaka­roa; ao ake te rā ka noho ahau ki te nohoa­nga whaka­wā, ka mea kia āra­hina mai taua tangata. <verse eid="ACT 25:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 25:18" />Ā, i te tū­ranga o ngā kai­whaka­pae, kīhai tētahi hē o āku i whaka­aro ai i kōrero­tia e rātou mōna. <verse eid="ACT 25:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 25:19" />Heoi, he kupu tau­tohe­tohe nō tā rātou kara­kia tā rātou i mea ai ki a ia, ko tētahi Īhu anō i mate, e kīa ana hoki e Paora kei te ora. <verse eid="ACT 25:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 25:20" />Heoi, pōhewa noa iho ahau ki taua tau­tohe, ka mea hoki me kore ia e pai kia haere ki Hiruhārama, ki reira whaka­wā­kia ai mō aua mea. <verse eid="ACT 25:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 25:21" />Nō te karanga­tanga a Paora kia waiho ia kia whaka­rangona tāna e te eme­para, ka whaka­haua e ahau kia puri­tia ia, kia tukua rā anō ia e ahau ki a Hīhā.”<verse eid="ACT 25:21" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 25:22" />Ka mea a Akaripa ki a Petuha, “E hia­hia ana anō ahau kia rongo i taua tangata.”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="ACT 25:22">Ka mea ia, “Ko āpōpō koe rongo ai ki a ia.”<verse eid="ACT 25:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 25:23" />Heoi, i te aonga ake, ka tae atu a Akaripa rāua ko Pereniki, me ngā whaka­pai­pai maha, ā, tomo ana ki te whare whaka­rongo, rātou ko ngā ranga­tira mano, ko ngā tāngata nunui o te pā, ā, ka whaka­haua e Petuha, ka mauria mai a Paora. <verse eid="ACT 25:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 25:24" />Nā, ka mea a Petuha, “E Kīngi Akaripa, e ngā tāngata katoa hoki e noho nei tātou, ka kite koutou i tēnei tangata, i tohe mai ai ki ahau te hui­hui katoa o ngā Hūrai i Hiruhārama, i konei anō hoki, i karanga ai, ehara rawa i te tika kia waiho ia kia ora ana. <verse eid="ACT 25:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 25:25" />Otirā, i kite ahau, kāhore āna mahi e tika ai te mate; ā, i te mea nāna anō i karanga ki te eme­para, ka mea ahau kia ungā atu ia. <verse eid="ACT 25:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 25:26" />Kāhore ia āku tino mea e tuhi­tuhi atu ai ahau mōna ki tōku ariki. Koia ahau ka ārahi mai nei i a ia ki a koutou, ki a koe rawa anō, e Kīngi Akaripa, kia whai mea ai ahau hei tuhi­tuhi­nga atu, ua mutu te uiui. <verse eid="ACT 25:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 25:27" />Ki tāku hoki he mea hē kia ungā atu he here­here, ā, kia kaua hoki e kōrero­tia te mea i whaka­wā­kia ai ia.”<verse eid="ACT 25:27" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 25" />
  <chapter number="26" style="c" sid="ACT 26" />
  <para style="s1">Tā Paora Tohe i te Aroaro o Akaripa</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 26:1" />Nā, ko te mea­tanga a Akaripa ki a Paora, “E āhei ana koe kia kōrero i āu kōrero.” Kātahi, ka totoro te ringa o Paora, ā, ka kōrero ia:<verse eid="ACT 26:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 26:2" />“He koa ngā ngākau tēnei ki ahau, e Kīngi Akaripa, kia kōrero­tia e ahau ki a koe āia­nei ngā mea katoa e whaka­wā­kia nei ahau e ngā Hūrai; <verse eid="ACT 26:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 26:3" />he mōhio rawa hoki koe ki ngā rite­nga katoa, ki ngā tau­tohe hoki anō a ngā Hūrai; nā reira, kia pai koe ki te whaka­rongo mārie ki ahau.<verse eid="ACT 26:3" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 26:4" />“Ko tāku whaka­haere mai o tōku tama­riki­tanga, nō te tīma­tanga mai rā anō i roto i tōku iwi, i Hiruhārama hoki, e mōhio ana ngā Hūrai katoa. <verse eid="ACT 26:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 26:5" />Mōhio tonu rātou ki ahau ō mua iho, me i pai rātou ki te whaka­atu; ko tāku mahi, i whai i tā te tītore­hanga pakeke rawa o tō tātou kara­kia, i tā te Parihi. <verse eid="ACT 26:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 26:6" />Tēnei ahau te tū nei i konei, te whaka­wā­kia nei mō te tū­mana­ko ki te mea i kōrero­tia e te Atua i mua ki ō tātou mātua. <verse eid="ACT 26:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 26:7" />E tū­mana­ko nei ō tātou iwi kotahi tekau mā rua kia uru ki tēnei, i a rātou e mahi tonu nei ki te Atua i te ao, i te pō. Ko tēnei e tūmanako­hia atu nei e te kīngi, te mea e whaka­wā­kia nei ahau e ngā Hūrai. <verse eid="ACT 26:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 26:8" />He aha rawa kia kore e whaka­pono­hia e koutou, ki te mea ka whaka­ara ake te Atua i te hunga mate?<verse eid="ACT 26:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 26:9" />“Ko ahau nei, i whaka­aro ahau kia maha tonu ngā mea e mahia e ahau hei pēhi mō te ingoa o Īhu o Nahareta. <verse eid="ACT 26:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 26:10" />Āe, i meinga anō tēnei e ahau ki Hiruhārama. He toko­maha anō te hunga tapu i uakina e ahau ki ngā whare here­here, he mea tuku mai hoki ngā tikanga nā ngā tohu­nga nui ki ahau; ā, i te whaka­mate­nga i a rātou, i whaka­ae ahau kia pērā­tia rātou. <verse eid="ACT 26:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 26:11" />He maha anō āku whiu­nga i a rātou i roto i ngā whare kara­kia katoa, i meinga anō rātou e ahau kia kohu­kohu; heoi, hau­rangi noa iho ahau ki a rātou, whāia ana e ahau, ā taea noatia ngā pā o tawhiti.<verse eid="ACT 26:11" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Kōrero a Paora mō tōna Huringa ki te Whakapono</para>
  <para style="r">(<ref loc="ACT 9:1-19">Ngā Mahi 9.1-19</ref>; <ref loc="ACT 22:6-16">22.6-16</ref>)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 26:12" />“Nāwai ā, i ahau e haere ana ki Ramahiku, me ngā tikanga, me te kupu whaka­ae a ngā tohu­nga nui, <verse eid="ACT 26:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 26:13" />i te pou­tū­mārō­tanga, e te kīngi, ka kitea e ahau i te ara he mārama i te rangi e tīaho ana ki ahau, ki ōku hoa haere anō, tērā atu i te mārama o te rā. <verse eid="ACT 26:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 26:14" />Heoi, hinga ana mātou katoa ki te whenua, ka rongo ahau i te reo e kōrero ana ki ahau, nō ngā Hiperu anō hoki te reo, e mea ana, ‘E Haora, e Haora, he aha tāu e whaka­toi nei i ahau? Ehara tāu te whana ki ngā koi­koi.’ <verse eid="ACT 26:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 26:15" />Anō rā ko ahau, ‘Ko wai koe, e te Ariki?’ Ka mea ia, ‘Ko Īhu ahau e whaka­toia nei e koe. <verse eid="ACT 26:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 26:16" />Otirā whaka­tika, e tū ōu wae­wae ki runga. Ko te mea tēnei i puta ai ahau ki a koe, kia meinga koe hei kai­mahi, hei kai­whaka­atu mō ngā mea i kite nei koe, mō ngā mea anō e kitea ai ahau e koe. <verse eid="ACT 26:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 26:17" />Ka whaka­ora­ngia koe i te iwi, i ngā tauiwi, ka tonoa nei koe e ahau ki a rātou, <verse eid="ACT 26:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 26:18" />hei whaka­titiro i ō rātou kanohi, hei whaka­tahuri i a rātou i te pōuri ki te mārama, i te kaha o Hātana ki te Atua, kia whi­whi ai rātou ki te muru­nga hara, ki tētahi wāhi anō i roto i te hunga ka oti te whaka­tapu i runga i te whaka­pono ki ahau.’<verse eid="ACT 26:18" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Ka Kōrero a Paora mō āna Mahi</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 26:19" />“Nō reira, kīhai ahau i whaka­tuturi, e Kīngi Akaripa, ki tō te rangi kite­nga. <verse eid="ACT 26:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 26:20" />Heoi, i kōrero ahau ki te hunga i Ramahiku i te tua­tahi, ā, i Hiruhārama, ki te whenua katoa anō o Hūria, ki ngā tauiwi hoki, kia rīpe­netā, kia tahuri ki te Atua, me te mahi anō i ngā mahi tika o te rīpe­netā. <verse eid="ACT 26:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 26:21" />Nō reira ngā Hūrai i hopu ai i ahau i te teme­para, i whai ai ki te whaka­mate i ahau. <verse eid="ACT 26:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 26:22" />Heoi, ka āwhina­tia mai ahau e te Atua, ka tū tonu nei ahau, ā mohoa noa nei, me te kōrero ki te iti, ki te rahi, kāhore āku kupu kē ake i tā ngā poro­piti rātou ko Mohi i mea ai meāke puta: <verse eid="ACT 26:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 26:23" />arā ko te Karaiti kia mate, ko ia te mātā­mua o te aranga o te hunga mate, māna anō e whaka­puaki te mārama ki te iwi, ki ngā tauiwi.”<verse eid="ACT 26:23" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 26:24" />I a ia e kōrero ana i ēnei mea, nui atu te reo o Petuha ki te karanga, “E Paora, he hau­rangi koe; nā te nui o tāu kōrero puka­puka i hau­rangi ai koe!”<verse eid="ACT 26:24" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 26:25" />Anō rā ko ia, “Kāhore ōku hau­rangi, e Petuha, e te tangata pai rawa; engari he pono, he whai whaka­aro, āku kupu e whaka­puaki nei. <verse eid="ACT 26:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 26:26" />E mātau ana hoki te kīngi ki ēnei mea, i māia ai ahau ki te kōrero ki a ia. E mea ana hoki ahau, kāhore tētahi o ēnei mea i ngaro i a ia; kīhai hoki tēnei mea i mahia i te koko­nga. <verse eid="ACT 26:26" /><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 26:27" />E whaka­pono ana rānei koe ki ngā poro­piti, e Kīngi Akaripa? E mea ana ahau, tēnei koe te whaka­pono nei.”<verse eid="ACT 26:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 26:28" />Anō rā ko Akaripa ki a Paora, “Wāhi iti kua riro atu ahau ki tāu, ki tā te Karaiti tikanga.”<verse eid="ACT 26:28" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 26:29" />Nā, ko te mea­tanga a Paora, “Pai tonu kia īnoi ahau ki te Atua kia kaua e iti, engari kia tino nui, kia kaua anō e waiho i tōu kotahi, engari, kia tino rite ki ahau te hunga katoa e whaka­rongo nei ki ahau ināia­nei; ko ēnei meka­meka ia kia kore.”<verse eid="ACT 26:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 26:30" />Nā, ka whaka­tika te kīngi, me te kāwana, me Pereniki, me te hunga i noho tahi rātou. <verse eid="ACT 26:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 26:31" />Nā, i a rātou ka wehe kē, ka kōrero­rero ki a rātou anō, ka mea, “Kāhore he hanga a tēnei tangata e tika ai te mate, te here rānei.” <verse eid="ACT 26:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 26:32" />Kātahi, ka mea a Akaripa ki a Petuha, “Ka tukua tēnei tangata kia haere, me i kaua ia te karanga ki a Hīhā.”<verse eid="ACT 26:32" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 26" />
  <chapter number="27" style="c" sid="ACT 27" />
  <para style="s1">Ka Whakawhiti a Paora ki Roma</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 27:1" />Ā, nō ka takoto te tikanga kia rere mātou ki Itari, ka tukua a Paora me ērā atu here­here ki tētahi kene­turio ko Huriu te ingoa, nō te hapū o Ākuhata. <verse eid="ACT 27:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 27:2" />Nā, eke ana mātou ki tētahi kai­puke o Ataramitiuma, e tika ana rā ngā kāinga o Āhia, rere ana mātou; ko Aritaku o Teharonika, he tangata nō Makeronia, tō mātou hoa. <verse eid="ACT 27:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 27:3" />Pō tahi ka ū mātou ki Hairona. Nā, ka ngā­wari te mahi a Huriu ki a Paora, tukua ana ia kia haere ki ōna hoa kia ata­whai­tia. <verse eid="ACT 27:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 27:4" />Rere atu ana i reira, ka miri haere mātou i te taha o Kai­peru, nō te mea i hē te hau. <verse eid="ACT 27:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 27:5" />Whiti ana mātou i te moana o Kiri­kia, o Pamapu­ria, ka ū ki Maira, he pā nō Raikia. <verse eid="ACT 27:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 27:6" />Nā, ka mau i te kene­turio he kai­puke ki reira nō Arēhānaria, e rere ana ki Itari; ka utaina mātou e ia ki runga.<verse eid="ACT 27:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 27:7" />Ā, ka pō maha i pūhoi ai te rere, ka whiti whaka­uaua ki te rite­nga atu o Hiniru, ā, tē tukua mātou e te hau, ka miri haere mātou i te taha o Kariti i te rite­nga atu o Haramone; <verse eid="ACT 27:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 27:8" />ā, ka pahemo whaka­uaua a reira, ka ū mātou ki tētahi kāinga, ko Ngā Kokoru Āta­ahua te ingoa; e tata ana a reira ki te pā o Rāhia.<verse eid="ACT 27:8" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 27:9" />Ā, ka maha ngā rā ka pahemo, nā, kua kino te rere­nga, nō te mea kua pahemo kē te Pō Noho­puku, ā, ka whaka­tūpato a Paora, <verse eid="ACT 27:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 27:10" />ka mea ki a rātou, “E mara mā, e kite ana ahau i te kino, i te nui o te mate e pā mai i tēnei rere­nga, ehara i te mea ko te utanga anake me te kai­puke, engari, ko tātou anō.” <verse eid="ACT 27:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 27:11" />Otirā, nui kē atu te āro o te kene­turio ki te kāpene rāua ko te tangata nōna te kai­puke i tāna ki ngā mea i kōrero ai a Paora. <verse eid="ACT 27:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 27:12" />Ā, i te mea kīhai i pai taua kokoru hei tūnga i te hōtoke, ka mea te toko­maha kia rere atu anō i reira, me kore e ū ki Pinike, ki reira tū ai i te hōtoke; he kokoru ia nō Kariti, e anga ana ki te uru mā tonga, ki te uru mā raki.<verse eid="ACT 27:12" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Marangai i te Moana</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 27:13" />Ā, ka pā reka­reka te tonga, ka mea rātou kua taea tā rātou i whaka­aro ai, ka hūtia te punga; ā, miri haere ana i Kariti. <verse eid="ACT 27:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 27:14" />Nā, kīhai i roa ka puta he hau nui whaka­hara­hara, ko Urokarairona te ingoa. <verse eid="ACT 27:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 27:15" />Ā, ka kā­hakina te kai­puke, tē ngo­ngo ki te hau, nā, ka tukua e mātou ki tāna, ā, ka pāea. <verse eid="ACT 27:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 27:16" />Nā, ka miri i te taha ruru o tētahi motu, tōna ingoa ko Karaura; ka riro whaka­uaua mai te poti i a mātou. <verse eid="ACT 27:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 27:17" />Ā, ka hūtia ake, ka hanga ki te whakaū, meatia he awhi mō te tangere o te puke; ā, nō ka mataku kei eke ki te tahuna, ki Hatihi, ka tukua te rā, ā, ka pāea haere­tia. <verse eid="ACT 27:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 27:18" />Ā, nō ka tino ākina mātou e te tūpuhi, i te aonga ake ka ākiri­tia ngā utanga. <verse eid="ACT 27:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 27:19" />Ā, i te toru o ngā rā ka makā atu e rātou ki ō rātou ringa ngā mea ake o te kai­puke. <verse eid="ACT 27:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 27:20" />Ā, he maha ngā rā i kore ai e puta te rā me ngā whetū, kīhai anō i iti te tūpuhi i ākina ai mātou, nā, ka mahue katoa tō mātou whaka­aro ki te ora.<verse eid="ACT 27:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 27:21" />Heoi, ka roa te noho­puku, nā, ka tū a Paora i waenga­nui o rātou, ka mea, “E mara mā, engari rā me i rongo koutou ki ahau, kia kaua e rere mai i Kariti, kei pā mai tēnei kino, tēnei mate. <verse eid="ACT 27:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 27:22" />Nā, ko tāku kupu tēnei ki a koutou, Kia mārama te ngākau; e kore hoki e mate tētahi o koutou, ko te kai­puke anake. <verse eid="ACT 27:22" /><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 27:23" />I tū hoki ki tōku taha i tēnei pō he ana­hera nā te Atua, nāna nei ahau, ko ia tāku e kara­kia atu nei, <verse eid="ACT 27:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 27:24" />i mea mai, ‘Aua e mataku, e Paora; me tū koe ki te aro­aro o Hīhā; nāna, kua hoatu ki a koe e te Atua te hunga katoa e rere tahi nā koutou.’ <verse eid="ACT 27:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 27:25" />Nā, kia mārama te ngākau, e mara mā; e whaka­pono ana hoki ahau ki te Atua, e rite anō ki tāna i kōrero mai ai ki ahau. <verse eid="ACT 27:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 27:26" />Otirā kua takoto te tikanga kia eke tātou ki tētahi motu.”<verse eid="ACT 27:26" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 27:27" />Nā, i te tekau mā whā o ngā pō, i a mātou e kāhaki­hakina ana i te moana o Aria, i waenga­nui pō, ka mea ngā hēra­mana kei te whaka­tata rātou ki tētahi whenua. <verse eid="ACT 27:27" /><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 27:28" />Nā, ka whaka­tātūtū rātou, ka kite e rua tekau mārō, ā, ka neke tata atu, ka whaka­tātūtū anō, ka kite kotahi tekau mā rima mārō. <verse eid="ACT 27:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 27:29" />Nā, ka mataku kei pāea mātou ki ngā toka, ka tukua ngā punga e whā i te kei, ka hia­hia ki te awa­tea. <verse eid="ACT 27:29" /><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 27:30" />Ā, i ngā hēra­mana e mea ana kia oma atu i te kai­puke, e tuku ana hoki i te poti ki te moana, he whaka­ware, kia kīa ai e tukua ana ētahi punga i te ihu. <verse eid="ACT 27:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 27:31" />Ka mea a Paora ki te kene­turio rātou ko ngā hōia, “Ki te kore ēnei e noho ki te kai­puke, e kore koutou e taea te whaka­ora.” <verse eid="ACT 27:31" /><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 27:32" />Kātahi, ka tapa­hia ngā whaka­heke o te poti e ngā hōia, ā, tukua ana kia taka atu.<verse eid="ACT 27:32" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 27:33" />Ā, i te mea meāke pūao te rā, ka tohe a Paora ki a rātou katoa kia kai, ka mea, “Ko te tekau mā whā tēnei o ngā rā e tatari nei koutou, e noho­puku nei, tē ō te kai. <verse eid="ACT 27:33" /><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 27:34" />Koia ahau ka tohe nei kia kai; ko tētahi mea hoki tēnei e ora ai koutou. E kore hoki e nga­horo tētahi huru­huru o te ūpoko o tētahi o koutou.” <verse eid="ACT 27:34" /><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 27:35" />Ā, nō tāna kōrero­tanga i ēnei kupu, ka mau ki te taro, ka whaka­whetai ki te Atua i te aro­aro o te katoa; ā, ka whawhati, ka tīmata te kai. <verse eid="ACT 27:35" /><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 27:36" />Nā, ka mārama ngā ngākau o rātou katoa, ka kai anō rātou. <verse eid="ACT 27:36" /><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 27:37" />Nā, e rua rau e whitu tekau mā ono mātou katoa i te kai­puke. <verse eid="ACT 27:37" /><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 27:38" />Ā, nō ka mākona i te kai, ka whaka­māmā rātou i te kai­puke, ka ākiri­tia te wīti ki te moana.<verse eid="ACT 27:38" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Te Pākarutanga o te Kaipuke</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 27:39" />Ā, ka ao te rā kīhai rātou i mōhio ki tērā whenua; engari, i kite rātou i tētahi kokoru he one tō reira, ā, ka mea rātou me kore e āhei te āki atu i te kai­puke ki roto. <verse eid="ACT 27:39" /><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 27:40" />Nā, tapa­hia ana e rātou ngā punga, tukua ana ki te moana, i whaka­koro­koroa anō ngā here o te urungi, ka hūtia anō te rā nui ki te hau, ka tika atu ki te one. <verse eid="ACT 27:40" /><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 27:41" />Ā, ka puta atu ki tētahi wāhi, he tai papaki­rua, ka whaka­ekea te kai­puke; ā, titi tonu te ihu, mau tonu, ko te kei i pakaru i te kaha o te ngaru.<verse eid="ACT 27:41" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 27:42" />Ā, ki tā ngā hōia whaka­aro, me whaka­mate ngā here­here, kei kau tētahi ki uta, kei oma. <verse eid="ACT 27:42" /><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 27:43" />Ko te kene­turio ia i mea kia whaka­ora­ngia a Paora, kīhai hoki i tukua ki tā rātou i whaka­aro ai; nā, ka mea ia, kia mātua peke atu te hunga e mātau ana ki te kau, kia kau ki uta. <verse eid="ACT 27:43" /><verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 27:44" />Ko ērā atu, ko ētahi i runga i ngā papa, ko ētahi i runga i ētahi o ngā mea o te kai­puke. Heoi, tae ora katoa ana rātou ki uta.<verse eid="ACT 27:44" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 27" />
  <chapter number="28" style="c" sid="ACT 28" />
  <para style="s1">Kei Merita</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 28:1" />Ā, ka ora mātou, kātahi ka mōhio ko Merita te ingoa o te motu. <verse eid="ACT 28:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 28:2" />Nā, kīhai i nohi­nohi te ata­whai a ngā tāngata māori ki a mātou. Ka tahuna he kāpura, whaka­manu­hiri­tia ana mātou katoa, nō te mea e ua ana te ua, nō te mātao hoki. <verse eid="ACT 28:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 28:3" />Nā, ka kohiko­hia e Paora he pūpū wahie, ā, makā ana e ia ki te kāpura; heoi puta mai ana he neke i te wera, ka mau ki tōna ringa. <verse eid="ACT 28:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 28:4" />Ā, i te kite­nga o ngā tāngata māori i te ngā­rara e were­were ana ki tōna ringa, ka mea rātou tētahi ki tētahi, “Koia, he tangata kōhuru tēnei, ka ora nei ia i te moana, nā, kīhai i tukua e te tika kia ora.” <verse eid="ACT 28:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 28:5" />Otiia, i ruia atu e ia te ngā­rara ki te kāpura, ā, kīhai ia i mate, kīhai i aha. <verse eid="ACT 28:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 28:6" />Nā, whanga noa rātou kia tetere ia, kia hinga whaka­rere rānei, kia mate; heoi, ka roa noa tō rātou whanga­nga, ā, i te kite­nga kāhore he aha i pā ki a ia, ka puta kē ō rātou whaka­aro, ka mea, he atua ia.<verse eid="ACT 28:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 28:7" />I taua wāhi te kāinga o te tino ranga­tira o te motu, ko Pupiriu te ingoa. He manu­hiri mātou nāna; e toru ngā rā i ata­whai­tia ai mātou e ia. <verse eid="ACT 28:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 28:8" />Nā, i te takoto te papa o Pupiriu e mate ana i te kirikā, i te kōripi. Heoi, ka tomo a Paora ki a ia, ka īnoi, ka whaka­pā i ōna ringa ki a ia, ā, ora ake ia. <verse eid="ACT 28:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 28:9" />Ā, i te mea­tanga o tēnei, nā, ka haere mai anō ērā atu o te motu he mate o rātou, ā, whaka­ora­ngia ana. <verse eid="ACT 28:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 28:10" />Nui atu anō te hōnore i whaka­hōnore­tia ai mātou e rātou; ā, i tō mātou rere­nga ka utaina ngā mea e rite ana mā mātou.<verse eid="ACT 28:10" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Mai i Merita ki Roma</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 28:11" />Ā muri iho i ngā marama e toru, ka rere mātou i runga i tētahi kai­puke o Arēhānaria, i tū nei ki taua motu i te hōtoke, ko Katoro rāua ko Poruku te tohu. <verse eid="ACT 28:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 28:12" />Nā, ka ū ki Hairakuha, ā, e toru ō mātou rā i noho ai ki reira. <verse eid="ACT 28:12" /><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 28:13" />Nā, ka āwhio ake mātou i reira, ka ū ki Rekiuma. Ka pō tahi ka pā te tonga, ā, i te rua o ngā rā ka ū ki Puteori. <verse eid="ACT 28:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 28:14" />Ā, nō ka kitea ngā tuā­kana i reira, ka tohea mātou kia noho i a rātou, kia whitu ngā rā. Heoi, haere ana mātou ki Roma. <verse eid="ACT 28:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 28:15" />Ā, ka rongo ngā tuā­kana o reira ki a mātou, ka haere ake ki te whaka­tau i a mātou ki Te Mākete o Apiu, ki Whare­toru. Ā, i te kite­nga o Paora i a rātou, ka whaka­whetai ki te Atua, ka ora te ngākau.<verse eid="ACT 28:15" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Kei Roma</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 28:16" />Nā, ka tae mātou ki Roma, ka hoatu ngā here­here e te kene­turio ki te ranga­tira hōia. Ko Paora ia i tukua kia noho motu kē rāua ko tētahi hōia hei tiaki i a ia.<verse eid="ACT 28:16" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 28:17" />Ā, i muri i ngā rā e toru, ka hui­huia e Paora ngā tino tāngata o ngā Hūrai; ā, nō tō rātou mine­nga mai, ka mea ia ki a rātou, “E ōku tuā­kana, ko ahau kāhore ōku hara ki te iwi, ki ngā rite­nga rānei a ngā mātua, i tukua ai ahau i Hiruhārama hei here­here ki ngā ringa o ngā tāngata o Roma. <verse eid="ACT 28:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 28:18" />Ā, i mea rātou, i tā rātou whaka­wā­kanga i ahau kia tukua ahau, nō te mea kāhore he take e mate ai ahau. <verse eid="ACT 28:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 28:19" />Heoi, ka whaka­hē tonu ngā Hūrai; e taea hoki te aha? Karanga ana ahau ki a Hīhā; kāhore ia āku mea e whaka­wā ai ahau i tōku iwi. <verse eid="ACT 28:19" /><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 28:20" />Koia ahau i karanga ai i a koutou kia kite, kia kōrero ki ahau. Nō te mea hoki ko tā Īharaira e tū­mana­ko nei te mea i herea ai ahau ki tēnei meka­meka.”<verse eid="ACT 28:20" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 28:21" />Nā, ko tā rātou mea­tanga ki a ia, “Kāhore he puka­puka mōu i tae mai ki a mātou i Hūria, kāhore anō tētahi o ngā tuā­kana i haere mai nei i kawe kupu mai, i kōrero mai rānei i tētahi kino mōu. <verse eid="ACT 28:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 28:22" />Otirā, e mea ana mātou kia rongo ki a koe ki ōu whaka­aro. E mōhio ana hoki mātou ki tēnei wehe­nga, e kōrero­tia kino­tia ana i ngā wāhi katoa.”<verse eid="ACT 28:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 28:23" />Ā, ka oti te whaka­rite he rā ki a ia, he toko­maha i haere mai ki a ia ki tōna whare; ā, whaka­kitea ana e ia ki a rātou, whaka­atu­ria ana te ranga­tira­tanga o te Atua, ā, ka kukume i a rātou ki ngā mea o Īhu, tiki atu ai i tā te ture a Mohi, i tā ngā poro­piti, nō te ata ā ahi­ahi noa. <verse eid="ACT 28:23" /><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 28:24" />Ko ētahi i whaka­pono ki ngā mea i kōrero­tia, ko ētahi kīhai i whaka­pono. <verse eid="ACT 28:24" /><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 28:25" />Ā, te rite ā rātou kōrero, ka puta atu rātou, i muri i te kōrero­tanga a Paora i tētahi kupu, “Tika tonu te kōrero a te Wairua Tapu i a Ihāia poro­piti ki ō koutou mātua, <verse eid="ACT 28:25" /><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 28:26" />i mea nei,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 28:26">‘Haere ki tēnei iwi, mea atu,</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 28:26">Rongo noa koutou, e kore e mātau;</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:26">ti­tiro noa koutou, e kore e kite.<verse eid="ACT 28:26" /></para>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 28:27" />Kua mā­to­toru hoki te ngākau o tēnei iwi,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">he pūhoi ngā tari­nga ki te whaka­rongo,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">ō rātou kanohi kua whaka­moea e rātou;</para>
  <para style="q1" vid="ACT 28:27">kei kite ngā kanohi, kei rongo ngā tari­nga,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">kei mātau te ngākau,</para>
  <para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">ā, ka tahuri rātou, ka ora i ahau.’<verse eid="ACT 28:27" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 28:28" />“Nā, kia mōhio koutou, ka tukua tēnei whaka­ora­nga a te Atua ki ngā tauiwi, ā, ka rongo rātou.” <verse eid="ACT 28:28" /><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 28:29" />Ā, ka mutu ēnei kōrero āna, ka haere ngā Hūrai, he nui hoki tā rātou tau­tohe­tohe ki a rātou anō.<verse eid="ACT 28:29" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 28:30" />Ā, e rua tino tau i noho ai a Paora ki tōna whare i utua e ia, ā, manaaki­tia ana e ia te hunga katoa e tomo ana ki a ia; <verse eid="ACT 28:30" /><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 28:31" />ā, māia tonu ia ki te kauwhau i te ranga­tira­tanga o te Atua, ki te whaka­ako i ngā mea o te Ariki, o Īhu Karaiti, kīhai anō i rīria.<verse eid="ACT 28:31" /></para>
  <chapter eid="ACT 28" />
</usx>